window.XZ_MANUAL_SEARCH=[{"c":"getting-started","a":"","t":"Getting started","x":"XZ Mods is software for the XDJ-XZ that starts from a USB stick. It adds a MODS menu, stems you can mute live, custom beat jump, four decks over a loopback cable, DJ profiles, themes and games. It can also replace the whole play screen with its own MODERN interface.","i":""},{"c":"getting-started","a":"what-changes-and-what-stays-the-same","t":"What changes and what stays the same","x":"XZ Mods runs from the USB. Start the player without the USB and it is as it was. Hold MENU for a second Push ROTARY SELECTOR Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Press BACK The player picks up the XZ Mods loader ( autoexec.bin ) from the USB at start and runs XZ Mods from there. Your music, the library your DJ software exported and your playlists stay as they are. XZ Mods adds its own folders beside them. The player's own settings are still there. Hold MENU to open UTILITY, as without XZ Mods. Settings you change in MODS are saved on the USB, so they travel with it to another XZ running XZ Mods.","i":""},{"c":"getting-started","a":"start-without-xz-mods","t":"Start without XZ Mods","x":"Switch the player off. Start it without the XZ Mods USB, or with a USB that has no autoexec.bin on it. The player starts without XZ Mods. Plug the XZ Mods USB back in and start again to load XZ Mods. If you play from a separate music stick, that stick works without XZ Mods as before.","i":""},{"c":"getting-started","a":"what-you-need","t":"What you need","x":"Item What you need Player XDJ-XZ on firmware 1.26. No other firmware version is supported Computer 64-bit Windows with WebView2, or a Mac with macOS 14 or later, to prepare the USB Stems Made on a Windows computer or an Apple silicon Mac. An Intel Mac can import stems made elsewhere USB A USB stick for the loader. It can be your music USB, or a separate loader stick Four decks A USB-B to USB-A cable. See Four decks experimental The app gets and checks the files it needs. Nothing from the player's maker is included in the XZ Mods download. Caution XZ Mods is a preview. Test every new USB at home before you use it in a set.","i":""},{"c":"getting-started","a":"prepare-a-usb","t":"Prepare a USB","x":"You prepare the USB in the XZ Mods app on your computer. It does not format the drive or touch your music. Install the XZ Mods app and open it. Plug in your USB. The app finds it and opens it. With several USBs plugged in, choose yours from the list. Choose Install XZ Mods . Follow the short guide: your DJ profile, the screen the XZ starts with, then a checklist of what it will write. Back returns to the step before. Choose Write to USB , then Eject USB . The checklist before the write. Music, playlists and prepared stems are never touched. Loader XZ Mods itself. Games Free games the app downloads and checks. Interface The screen the XZ starts with. Write to USB Writes everything in the checklist. Every step of the app is in The XZ Mods app . To add stems to your tracks, see Stems .","i":""},{"c":"getting-started","a":"first-start","t":"First start","x":"Press BROWSE Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise Press LOAD 1 Press BACK Press MENU Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to SCREEN and push it Tap CLASSIC Tap MODERN Press MENU Plug the USB into USB 1 or USB 2 on the top of the XDJ-XZ. Switch the player on. Wait for XZ Mods to start. Load a track as usual and check it plays. Press MENU on the play screen, or touch MODS at the top right, to open the MODS menu. HOME is the first page. If you use a separate loader stick, keep it in until XZ Mods has started. Keep the USB with your music and stems in while you play.","i":""},{"c":"getting-started","a":"modern-on-first-start","t":"MODERN on first start","x":"MODERN draws the whole play screen. The player's controls work as before, and the top bar adds a few buttons. The MODERN play screen with a track on each deck. MODS Opens the MODS menu, like a short press of MENU. STEMS Shows or hides the stem rows. DECKS Chooses two or four decks. Deck lanes One waveform lane per deck, with its source and key. Deck panel The track, time, tempo and BPM of each deck. The rest of the play screen is in The play screen .","i":"modern"},{"c":"getting-started","a":"classic-on-first-start","t":"CLASSIC on first start","x":"CLASSIC keeps the player's own play screen and adds MODS to it. Touch MODS at the top right, or press MENU , to open the menu. A classic theme can restyle the screen. See Screen, interfaces and themes . Press the button above LINK Press the button above LINK","i":"classic"},{"c":"getting-started","a":"choose-modern-or-classic","t":"Choose MODERN or CLASSIC","x":"The XZ starts in the interface saved on the USB. You choose it in the app before the first start, and you can change it on the player at any time. Nothing else changes when you switch. Your settings, stems and decks stay as they are. Interface What you see MODERN XZ Mods draws the whole screen: bigger waveforms, a browse sidebar and a stems row with mute buttons. Marked Beta in the app CLASSIC The player's own play screen, with MODS added. Classic themes can restyle it A new USB starts in MODERN unless you choose the standard interface in the app. Choose the screen the XZ shows. New interface is MODERN, Standard XDJ-XZ interface is CLASSIC. New interface MODERN. Standard XDJ-XZ interface CLASSIC.","i":""},{"c":"getting-started","a":"switch-on-the-player","t":"Switch on the player","x":"There are two ways to switch. Press the button above LINK . Out of the box it switches between MODERN and CLASSIC, and the screen says which one you are in. You can give it another job in PLAY › BUTTON ABOVE LINK . Open MODS, go to SCREEN and choose CLASSIC or MODERN under INTERFACE . Press the button above LINK Press the button above LINK Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap CLASSIC Tap MODERN INTERFACE is the first choice on the SCREEN page. INTERFACE The interface the XZ shows. The change saves to the USB. CLASSIC The player's own screen with MODS. MODERN The full-screen XZ Mods layout. THEME The classic theme. See Screen, interfaces and themes. Explanation What the highlighted choice does. Save state Confirms the change is saved to the USB. Tip You can always reach MODS with the hardware alone. In CLASSIC, the button above LINK takes you to MODERN, where MENU opens MODS, and the encoder and BACK drive it.","i":""},{"c":"getting-started","a":"updating","t":"Updating","x":"There are two things to update, and they update separately. Press MENU Tap CONNECT Tap UPDATES Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise What How The app on your computer On Windows the app checks at launch and offers the update. On a Mac, download the new version from the release page. See App updates XZ Mods on your USB Open the USB in the app. When it says Update available , choose Update USB . The app backs up the old loader first XZ Mods over the network Send the update from the app and download it on the player. See Updates over the network experimental Caution Updating the app does not change the USB. After an app update, open the USB page and choose Update USB . Music, your exported library and your saved settings stay in place through an update. A USB built with Keep this version on the USB stays on its build and ignores network updates. See XZ Mods version . If something does not work after an update, see Messages and troubleshooting .","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"","t":"Controls on the player","x":"XZ Mods leaves every control on the XDJ-XZ doing its normal job unless this page says otherwise. This page covers only the controls whose behaviour XZ Mods changes or adds, and the ones you use to drive MODS. For everything else, the XDJ-XZ operating instructions still apply.","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"the-top-panel","t":"The top panel","x":"The picture is an illustration of the XDJ-XZ from straight above. The XDJ-XZ from above: the browse section with the touch screen at the top centre, a deck on each side and the four-channel mixer under the screen. Touch screen Shows the play screen in the interface you chose (MODERN or CLASSIC) and the MODS menu. Every MODS control also answers touch. MENU (UTILITY) Press: opens MODS where the screen has no MENU job of its own. Hold: opens the player's own UTILITY, as without XZ Mods. BACK Goes up one level, in MODS too. Rotary selector Turn to move the highlight in MODS, push to select. It drives every MODS page, so you never need the touch screen. SHORTCUT Opens the SHORTCUT screen, as without XZ Mods. A short MENU on that screen opens MODS. Button above LINK The media button directly above LINK. XZ Mods lets you choose what it does, alone and with SHIFT. LINK Its normal job. It can also switch the VJ.Tools view on and off. TIME MODE and DECK QUANTIZE Their normal job on decks 1 and 2. While a side drives deck 3 or 4 they also work on that deck. LOAD 1, LOAD 2 Load into the deck that side controls now: deck 1 or 3 on the left, deck 2 or 4 on the right. Left deck Controls deck 1, or deck 3 after you press SHIFT twice. Right deck Controls deck 2, or deck 4 after you press SHIFT twice. Mixer channels 3 1 2 4 Decks 3 and 4 play through CH3 and CH4 over the loopback cable.","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"browse-section-keys","t":"Browse section keys","x":"Open SOURCE ( BACK at the top of a list) Press MENU Press MENU Press INFO Press MENU Press BACK Press MENU Press SHORTCUT Press MENU Press MENU Hold MENU for a second Press BACK Key Action with XZ Mods MENU press Opens MODS on the play screen, the SOURCE screen, the INFO screen and the SHORTCUT screen experimental . Everywhere else it keeps its normal job. In MODS it closes MODS. MENU hold Opens the player's own UTILITY, in both interfaces. BACK Goes up one level. In MODS it steps from an open item to its page, then to the section rail. TURN Rotary selector, turn Moves the highlight to the next card, row or button in MODS. On a beat jump pair, after a push, it steps the jump size. PUSH Rotary selector, push Opens or changes the highlighted item in MODS. BUTTON ABOVE LINK Does what you chose in MODS > PLAY > BUTTON ABOVE LINK. The default is INTERFACE. SHIFT + BUTTON ABOVE LINK Hold SHIFT on either deck and press it. Does the second choice on the same page. The default is ITS OWN JOB. LINK Its normal job. With the screen switch key set to LINK it also switches the VJ.Tools view on and off. SHORTCUT Opens the SHORTCUT screen. In MODERN this is MODERN's own SHORTCUT screen. LOAD Loads the highlighted track into the deck that side controls: deck 1 or 3, deck 2 or 4. TIME MODE , DECK QUANTIZE Their normal job on decks 1 and 2. For decks 3 and 4, see Quantize and Four decks . A short press of MENU keeps its normal job wherever it has one. What a short press does in each place: Where you are Short press of MENU The MODS menu is open Closes MODS A game is on screen The game's own key The VJ.Tools view is on screen As before A menu, popup or dialog is open Works or closes the open menu A track list (browse, playlist, search, history) The sort menu or the track menu TAG LIST LIST MENU The play screen in GRID ADJUST The beat grid menu The play screen Opens MODS experimental The SOURCE screen Opens MODS experimental The track INFO screen Opens MODS experimental The SHORTCUT screen Opens MODS experimental The player's own UTILITY Closes UTILITY Any other screen The screen's own job","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"the-button-above-link","t":"The button above LINK","x":"The XDJ-XZ has a media button directly above LINK . Without XZ Mods it opens the library of a computer or phone connected to the player. XZ Mods gives it two slots: a plain press, and a press while SHIFT is held on either deck. Set them in MODS > PLAY > BUTTON ABOVE LINK. Press the button above LINK Press the button above LINK Both slots at their defaults. A press switches the interface, and SHIFT + press keeps the button's own job. Media buttons The four media buttons in the player's order from the top, left to right: the button above LINK, highlighted, then LINK, USB 1 and USB 2. PRESS What a plain press does. The filled choice is the current one. What it does One line explaining the current PRESS choice. SHIFT + PRESS What the button does while SHIFT is held on either deck. What it does One line explaining the current SHIFT + PRESS choice. Dock Explains the highlighted choice before you pick it. Choice What the button does MODS MENU Opens and closes MODS. MODS then works with the rotary selector and BACK . ITS OWN JOB Its normal job: the screen for playing a computer's or phone's library. In MODERN the player's own screen for it takes over until you are back on the play screen. INTERFACE Switches between MODERN and CLASSIC, with the same notice as MODS > SCREEN. VJ.TOOLS SCREEN Switches the VJ.Tools screen on and off. Without an enabled, connected VJ.Tools link it says so instead. STEMS Does what the STEMS button on the screen does: steps the stem buttons through their places in 2 DECKS, and shows or hides them in MODERN's 4 DECKS. DECK VIEW Steps DECK VIEW: 2 DECKS, 4 DECKS in number order 1 2 3 4, 4 DECKS in mixer order 3 1 2 4, then 2 DECKS again. It saves the choice and shows the new view in a short notice. NOTHING The button does nothing. Tip With the default INTERFACE on a plain press, you can always get back to MODS without touching the screen: press MENU on the play screen, or switch interface with the button above LINK and press MENU there.","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"link-and-the-vj-tools-view","t":"LINK and the VJ.Tools view","x":"When VJ.Tools on a computer is connected, the player's screen can show the VJ.Tools view instead of the play screen. MODS > CONNECT > VJ.TOOLS has a SCREEN SWITCH KEY with two choices: Press MENU Tap CONNECT Tap VJ.TOOLS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise Choice What switches the VJ.Tools view LINK (default) Pressing LINK . LINK also keeps its normal job. ONSCREEN A VJ.Tools button on the screen, in the corner opposite MODS. To switch the view with the button above LINK instead, set that button to VJ.TOOLS SCREEN. See Connect and DJ profiles for the connection itself.","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"deck-keys","t":"Deck keys","x":"The picture shows the left deck from above. The right deck has the same controls in the same places. Hold SHIFT on the left deck and press SYNC on the left deck Press MASTER TEMPO on the left deck Hold SHIFT on the left deck and press SYNC on the left deck Press SHIFT on the left deck twice quickly One deck from above. The pads are named A to D on the top row and E to H on the bottom row. SHIFT Press twice quickly to switch this side between its two decks. Held, it is the modifier for the combinations below. SYNC SHIFT + SYNC matches this deck's key to the master deck (KEY SYNC). SYNC alone does its normal job on decks 1 and 2. MASTER TEMPO While KEY SYNC holds, a press returns the deck to its own key. TEMPO slider After you switch decks, the new deck keeps its tempo until the slider reaches it. Jog wheel Its normal job on decks 1 and 2. Plays decks 3 and 4, and the games. Pad mode buttons HOT CUE, BEAT LOOP, SLIP LOOP, BEAT JUMP. One of them gives stem pads. With SHIFT, they mute stems. BEAT JUMP Press for beat jump page 1. SHIFT + BEAT JUMP gives page 2. Pads A to D Stem pads in the stem mode when the bank is A-D. Jump pairs A/B and C/D in BEAT JUMP mode. Pads E to H Stem pads when the bank is E-H. Jump pairs E/F and G/H in BEAT JUMP mode. CUE and PLAY/PAUSE Their normal job on decks 1 and 2. They play deck 3 or 4 while the side drives it. Key Action with XZ Mods SHIFT twice Switches the left side between deck 1 and deck 3, or the right side between deck 2 and deck 4. Press it twice within about half a second, without touching anything else. Decks 3 and 4 need the loopback cable; without it the screen says DECK 3 AND 4 NEED THE CH3/CH4 ROUTE. SHIFT + SYNC KEY SYNC: shifts the key of the deck this side controls to match the master deck, and turns on MASTER TEMPO. Press it again to end KEY SYNC. Works on all four decks. SYNC alone keeps its normal job on decks 1 and 2. MASTER TEMPO While KEY SYNC holds on that deck, a press ends KEY SYNC and returns the deck to its own key. Otherwise its normal job. SHIFT + MASTER TEMPO keeps its normal job. HOT CUE , BEAT LOOP , SLIP LOOP Choose the pad mode as without XZ Mods. The mode set in MODS > STEMS > STEM PADS turns four pads into stem pads. SHIFT + HOT CUE Mutes or unmutes the first stem in your STEM ORDER (vocals by default) on that deck. SHIFT + BEAT LOOP Mutes or unmutes the second stem (harmonics by default). SHIFT + SLIP LOOP Mutes or unmutes the third stem (drums by default). BEAT JUMP Beat jump mode with page 1 of your jump sizes. SHIFT + BEAT JUMP Beat jump mode with page 2 of your jump sizes. Let go of SHIFT before you press a pad. TEMPO slider After a deck switch, the deck that takes over keeps its tempo until the slider crosses its value. Then the slider moves it again. This works both ways. LOAD Loads into the deck the side controls now. Jog wheel Its normal job on decks 1 and 2. On decks 3 and 4 it bends, scratches in VINYL mode and moves loop edges. The jog games use it too. The three SHIFT + pad mode combinations work while the USB loader has the stem engine. They also turn stem audio on if it was off. With them, the player's own SHIFT + HOT CUE (CALL) is not available on decks 1 and 2. Every other deck key keeps its normal job on decks 1 and 2. While a side drives deck 3 or 4, the transport, loop, cue and tempo keys play that deck instead. Four decks lists what each one does there.","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"performance-pads","t":"Performance pads","x":"The eight pads keep their normal job in every pad mode, with two exceptions: the stem pads, and the BEAT JUMP pads. Press HOT CUE on the left deck Press BEAT LOOP on the left deck Press SLIP LOOP on the left deck Press BEAT JUMP on the left deck Hold SHIFT on the left deck and press HOT CUE on the left deck, then BEAT LOOP on the left deck, then SLIP LOOP on the left deck Pad mode Pads with XZ Mods HOT CUE The player's own hot cues. Gate cue and smart cue change what a hot cue does when you turn them on; see Gate cue and smart cue . BEAT LOOP The player's own beat loops. SLIP LOOP The player's own slip loops. BEAT JUMP Your jump sizes. A/B, C/D, E/F and G/H are pairs: the first pad jumps back, the second forward. With a loop on, the loop moves instead. SHIFT + pad keeps its normal job on decks 1 and 2. See Beat jump . The stem mode Four pads (A to D, or E to H) mute stems instead. The other four keep their job in that mode.","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"stem-pads","t":"Stem pads","x":"In the pad mode you choose for stems, four pads switch stems on that deck. A, B and C mute the three stems in your STEM ORDER. D is BYPASS: it plays the original track instead of the stems. On a 4-stem track, D mutes bass instead. With the E-H bank, E to H do the same. Press MENU Tap STEMS Tap STEM PADS Tap HOT CUE Tap BEAT LOOP Tap SLIP LOOP Tap BEAT JUMP Tap PADS A-D Tap PADS E-H Tap ORDER Tap STEM COLOURS Tap OFF Press HOT CUE on the left deck Press pad A on the left deck Press pad B on the left deck Press pad C on the left deck Press pad D on the left deck Press pad A on the left deck HOT CUE gives stem pads on A to D, in the default order, with stem colours on the pad lights. Pad mode The pad mode button that gives stem pads. The others keep their pads. Pad diagram What each pad does in that mode, laid out like the pads on the deck. STEMS ON Which four pads carry the stems: PADS A-D or PADS E-H. Order The order of the stems on pads A, B and C and on the play screen. Push, then turn to change it. Stem pad lights STEM COLOURS lights stem pads in their stem colours and dims muted stems. OFF leaves the pad lights to the player. Works on Stem pads work on decks 1 and 2. Decks 3 and 4 have no stems. Setting on this page Choices Default Pad mode HOT CUE, BEAT LOOP, SLIP LOOP, BEAT JUMP HOT CUE STEMS ON PADS A-D, PADS E-H PADS A-D STEM PAD LIGHTS STEM COLOURS, OFF STEM COLOURS If you choose BEAT JUMP for stems, beat jumps win its pads. Page 2 always jumps. Page 1 jumps while it uses MY SIZES, and gives stem pads only while it is set to PAGE 1: STOCK. Stems explains the stem audio itself, the order and the stem buttons on the screen.","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"pad-lights","t":"Pad lights","x":"What you see Meaning Stem pads in stem colours, muted stems dim STEM PAD LIGHTS is STEM COLOURS, on decks 1 and 2. Warm red and amber pads in BEAT JUMP mode Beat jump page 2 is selected on that deck. The player's own pad colours Every other mode, and page 1 of BEAT JUMP.","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"decks-3-and-4-from-the-deck-controls","t":"Decks 3 and 4 from the deck controls","x":"Each side of the XZ drives one of two decks: the left side deck 1 or deck 3, the right side deck 2 or deck 4. Press SHIFT twice to switch. LOAD on that side then loads into the deck it controls. Press SHIFT on the right deck twice quickly Connect the loopback cable and wait until MODS > 4 DECKS says the route is ready. Press SHIFT twice quickly on the left side. The left side now drives deck 3. Move the TEMPO slider until it reaches deck 3's tempo. Until then the slider does not change deck 3. Press SHIFT twice again to go back to deck 1. If the loopback route goes down, both sides go back to decks 1 and 2. Four decks covers setup, the deck view and every status.","i":""},{"c":"hardware","a":"when-a-control-does-not-respond","t":"When a control does not respond","x":"What happens Why, and what to do MENU opens one of the player's own menus instead of MODS That screen has its own MENU job. Press BACK to the play screen, then press MENU . MENU opens UTILITY You held it. A short press opens MODS. The button above LINK does nothing It is set to NOTHING. Change it in MODS > PLAY > BUTTON ABOVE LINK. SHIFT twice shows DECK 3 AND 4 NEED THE CH3/CH4 ROUTE Decks 3 and 4 are not connected. Open MODS > 4 DECKS. The TEMPO slider does not change the deck Pickup after a deck switch. Move the slider through the deck's tempo. A key sync press shows a message on the deck's key See Keys and KEY SYNC . A BEAT JUMP pad shows JUMP UNAVAILABLE See When a jump is refused .","i":""},{"c":"play-screen","a":"","t":"The play screen","x":"The play screen is where you spend the set. XZ Mods gives you two ways to draw it. MODERN replaces the whole screen with its own layout. CLASSIC keeps the player's own screen and adds a row of buttons, the playing key and the stem rows to it. You choose between them in MODS under SCREEN (see Screen, interfaces and themes ).","i":""},{"c":"play-screen","a":"the-modern-play-screen","t":"The MODERN play screen","x":"MODERN draws every deck the same way: a top bar across the screen, one waveform lane per deck with a narrow info column on its left, a row of hot-cue lamps, and a deck strip at the bottom. Two decks share the screen in halves. For four decks, see Four decks . Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 6 clicks clockwise Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 6 clicks anticlockwise Tap TIME 1 Tap TIME 1 Tap INFO HEADER Press BACK","i":"modern"},{"c":"play-screen","a":"top-bar","t":"Top bar","x":"Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Tap STEMS HEADER Tap STEMS HEADER Deck 1 is the master, deck 2 plays in a 4-beat loop with KEY SYNC holding its key. SINGLE CONTINUE | PLAY MODE. The lit word is what a deck does at the end of a track: SINGLE stops, CONTINUE loads the next track in the list and plays it. Tap to switch. A. HOT CUE Lit while HOT CUE AUTO LOAD is on. Red means every track brings its hot cues, white means only the tracks marked for it in the library. Tap to step through ON, the library setting and OFF. A. CUE Lit while AUTO CUE is on, so the cue point lands where the music starts. Tap to switch it. BEAT FX The effect, its beat and time, the FX BPM and the channel it is on. It fills red while the effect is on. DECKS Shows which decks the sides drive and opens DECK VIEW. See Four decks . INFO Opens INFO for the active deck's track. STEMS Steps the stem buttons through their layouts. Lit blue while stems are on. In 4 DECKS it shows or hides them. See Stems . MODS Opens MODS. A lamp label in grey shows a mode the player does not let XZ Mods change from the screen. Change it in the player's own UTILITY instead (hold MENU ). You can hide the three lamps in MODS under SCREEN , LAMPS AND TITLES . The BEAT FX readout then takes their room. ECHO on: the readout fills red, with the beat, the time in milliseconds and the FX BPM PING PONG chosen but off: a quiet outline An effect without beats shows its name alone VINYL BRAKE with a long time and the FX BPM set by TAP The first moments after start, before the effect has been read MODE LAMPS and QUANTIZE LAMP hidden: the readout starts at the left edge The same with ECHO on","i":"modern"},{"c":"play-screen","a":"deck-column-and-waveform-lanes","t":"Deck column and waveform lanes","x":"Each deck gets an info column and a scrolling waveform. The playhead is the red line in the middle. DECK tag Tap to make this the active deck. The blue tile marks the active deck. The dashes beside the name count the beats of the bar. Source Where the track came from: USB1 or USB2. Key The key the deck plays now. Green or amber means it mixes with the master deck's key. See Key . KEY SYNC Replaces the KEY caption while KEY SYNC holds this deck's key. Tuning How many cents the playing key sits off the nearest semitone. ORIGINAL The track's analysed key, shown once the playing key has moved away from it. Beat countdown Bars and beats to the next cue ahead of the playhead, as bars.beats. Bar number Counts bars every four bars, so you can count phrases. Loop A running loop shades the waveform and names its length. Playhead The current position. The waveform scrolls past it. ZOOM How far the waveforms are zoomed. Turn the rotary encoder to zoom in or out. Hot-cue lamps Pads A to H in their cue colours. A dark lamp is an empty pad. Turn the rotary encoder on the play screen to zoom both lanes together. There are seven zoom steps. The zoom is kept when you leave the screen, and saved to the USB with your other settings. Zoomed fully in on deck 2 Zoomed fully out WAVEFORM CURRENT POSITION set to LEFT: more of what is coming up. This choice is saved to the USB too","i":"modern"},{"c":"play-screen","a":"deck-strip","t":"Deck strip","x":"The two deck strips. Deck 1 is the tempo master, deck 2 is synced to it. DECK badge The deck this strip belongs to, lit when it is the active deck. Title and artist The loaded track. Play state A triangle while the deck plays, two bars while it is paused. TRACK The track's number in the list it was loaded from. REMAIN / TIME The lit word says how the time counts: REMAIN counts down to the end, TIME counts up from the start. Tap the time to switch. QUANTIZE Red while QUANTIZE is on, with the beat value loops and cues snap to. Tempo range The tempo slider's range, for example ±10. MT MASTER TEMPO. It blinks while KEY SYNC holds the key. SYNC Lit while the deck is synced. BPM The deck's playing BPM. MASTER marks the tempo master. Cue marks Hot cues as lettered chips and memory cues as red marks above the overview. Overview The whole track. The lighter part is what has played. Minute scale Minutes to the end in REMAIN, from the start in TIME. In the last 30 seconds of a track the overview's playing address flashes slowly, and in the last 15 seconds it flashes fast, in either time mode. Deck 1 in its last 12 seconds, the end warning flashing Deck 2 with no track: Not Loaded. in its lane and strip A three-digit track number TIME MODE that you can switch by touch: the lit word is white The first frame after start, before anything has been read: dashes everywhere","i":"modern"},{"c":"play-screen","a":"key-and-key-sync","t":"Key and KEY SYNC","x":"The large key in each deck's column is the key the deck plays right now. Tempo with MASTER TEMPO off, a key shift and KEY SYNC all move it. Its colour compares it with the master deck's key. Green means it mixes with the master's key: the same key, its relative major or minor, or one step away on the key wheel, tuned within 25 cents of the master. Amber means it would mix, but it is detuned by more than 25 cents. White means neither, and the master deck itself is always white. Turn KEY MATCH COLOURS off in SCREEN and every key is white. The cents beside it show how far it sits off the semitone, so you can match by ear. Once the playing key leaves the track's analysed key, ORIGINAL shows the analysed key below it. Press MENU Tap PLAY Tap KEYS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to KEY UP and push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to KEY DOWN and push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to RESET and push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to KEY SYNC and push it While KEY SYNC holds a deck's key, the KEY caption becomes a blue KEY SYNC chip and the deck's MT lamp blinks, half a second lit and half a second dark. KEY SYNC holds Bbm, MT lit Half a second later, MT dark MASTER TEMPO off: +2.20 % lifts A minor by 38 cents, still Am At +6.10 % the playing key reaches Bbm Keys written as wheel numbers, with a key shift on deck 1 The whole play screen with wheel-number keys An older loader without the analysed key: the key and its key-shift step No key read on deck 1, and a key name too long for the large face on deck 2 You choose how keys are written (as on the USB, musical or wheel numbers) and whether the playing key shows at all in MODS under SCREEN . See Screen, interfaces and themes .","i":"modern"},{"c":"play-screen","a":"waveform-colours","t":"Waveform colours","x":"MODS under SCREEN offers four waveform colours for MODERN. They change the lanes and the overviews together. Your choice is saved to the USB. 3-BAND COLOURS , beside LAMPS AND TITLES, changes the colour of each band; see 3-band colours . Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap STOCK Tap RGB Tap 3-BAND Tap STEMS Tap LAMPS AND TITLES Tap MODE LAMPS Tap QUANTIZE LAMP Tap TITLES IN WAVEFORMS Tap DECK + WAVE Tap DECK ONLY Tap OFF Tap CLOSE Choice What you see STOCK One blue waveform with white peaks RGB Lows red, mids green, highs blue 3-BAND Lows blue, mids amber, highs white, or the colours you chose in 3-BAND COLOURS STEMS Drums, harmonics and vocals in their stem colours. A track without stems shows 3-BAND STOCK RGB 3-BAND STEMS USB COLORS (MODS, SCREEN , LAMPS AND TITLES ) lets each deck take the colours saved on the USB stick its track came from. DECK + WAVE: the deck tile takes the stick's colour and the waveform the stick's waveform colour DECK ONLY: only the deck tile takes the stick's colour OFF: every deck uses the player's own colours","i":"modern"},{"c":"play-screen","a":"notices","t":"Notices","x":"When something you asked for does not happen, a notice appears in the middle of the screen for two and a half seconds. It says what went wrong in one line, for example DECK 1 DID NOT LOAD THE TRACK . A long notice wraps. Messages and troubleshooting explains each one. Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Tap CHOOSE TRACK Push ROTARY SELECTOR Tap TRACK ROW Tap LOAD DECK 3 A notice over the lanes A long notice The same screen once the notice has gone If a deck cannot go on, its lane turns red and names the problem, for example EMERGENCY LOOP (the deck loops until you load a track) or CANNOT READ THE TRACK with the player's error code. Tap CHOOSE TRACK on the red band to make that deck active and open BROWSE. EMERGENCY LOOP on deck 2 CANNOT READ THE TRACK with error E-8302 A deck that plays its whole track from RAM after the music USB went out is not in trouble, so its lane says so in teal instead: WHOLE TRACK IN RAM · PLAYABLE , in the waveform's place. See RAM tracks .","i":"modern"},{"c":"play-screen","a":"shortcut","t":"SHORTCUT","x":"Press SHORTCUT on the play screen to see the settings you change most during a set on one page. It has the same four groups as the player's own SHORTCUT screen: PLAYER SETTINGS, DECK STATUS, DEVICE SETTINGS and MY SETTINGS. Press BACK or tap the arrow in the top left corner to return to the play screen. Press SHORTCUT Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Press BACK The SHORTCUT screen with quantize, waveform and time settings for both decks. Highlighted row Turn the encoder to move between rows. The line under the title explains the highlighted row. Locked value A lock and READ ONLY HERE mean XZ Mods shows this value but cannot change it here. Pushing or tapping it does nothing. Choice buttons Tap a value to change it. The lit button is the current value. DECK 1 lamps QUANTIZE (or Q1), SYNC, SLIP, MASTER and the time mode for deck 1. Tap QUANTIZE to switch it, tap REMAIN or TIME to change the time mode. LINK lamp Shows whether the player is linked to other players. Jumps TRACK, PLAYLIST and SEARCH open those lists. MATCHING opens matching tracks, or hands over to the player's own browser when XZ Mods cannot list them. DEVICE SETTINGS Waveform colour, playhead position, key display format and waveform zoom. These change the MODERN screen at once. MY SETTINGS Time mode, play mode and auto cue for the decks. Which rows you can change depends on what the player lets XZ Mods write. A locked row shows its value and the reason it is read-only. A short MENU on SHORTCUT opens MODS. NEEDLE LOCK appears in PLAYER SETTINGS when the player reports it. LOCK prevents a waveform touch from searching a playing deck. Pause the deck to search, or choose UNLOCK when that setting is writable. HOT CUE AUTO LOAD has choices; QUANTIZE BEAT VALUE and AUTO CUE LEVEL are read-only in this fixture QUANTIZE BEAT VALUE as four choices, play mode and auto cue locked The waveform colour row with STEMS chosen The player's own settings shown as values while it is not accepting changes. DEVICE SETTINGS still change the MODERN screen With four decks, SHORTCUT also shows DECK SELECT. See Four decks .","i":"modern"},{"c":"play-screen","a":"the-classic-play-screen","t":"The CLASSIC play screen","x":"CLASSIC keeps the familiar play screen, in the classic theme you chose, with a row of XZ Mods buttons across the top, the playing key under each deck's key, and stem rows under the waveforms. Everything else stays where the XDJ-XZ operating instructions put it. Tap the screen Tap the screen Tap the screen The ORIGINAL theme with stems on in the BELOW / HALF layout. Deck 1's playing key has moved from 2A to 11A. VJ.TOOLS Switches to the VJ.Tools screen when a VJ.Tools computer is connected. See Connect and DJ profiles . DECKS Shows which decks the sides drive and opens DECK VIEW. See Four decks . Metrics The player's CPU load, free memory and temperature. Tap METRICS to set it up. See Extras . STEMS Steps the stem rows through their layouts. The marks under the label show the current one. Dark in 4 DECKS, which has no stem rows. See Stems . MODS Opens MODS. Playing key Shown under the player's own key. The analysed key, an arrow, then the key the deck plays now, with its tuning in cents. Same key When the playing key has not moved, KEY and the key, with the cents. Stem rows VOCALS, DRUMS, HARMONICS and BYPASS for each deck. See Stems . This picture shows CLASSIC with the XZ Mods buttons and stem rows. Everything else on it is the player's own: the deck tabs, source, key, BEAT FX, ZOOM, the deck strips with A.HOTCUE, A.CUE, QUANTIZE, TEMPO and the BPM box. The XDJ-XZ operating instructions explain those. The key line replaces the player's beat countdown under the key. You choose the key notation and whether the playing key shows in MODS under SCREEN . An earlier capture with stems in the BELOW / FULL layout, the rows taller with room for the stem level bars. Stem colours here follow an older default. Today drums are blue and harmonics red; see Stem colours .","i":"classic"},{"c":"play-screen","a":"scrolling-waveform","t":"Scrolling waveform","x":"In CLASSIC, SCREEN offers three scrolling waveforms. The setting is wave_mode on the USB. Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap CLASSIC Tap 2 DECKS Tap 4 DECKS Tap 4 DECKS Tap STOCK Tap 3-BAND Tap STEMS Tap AS ON THE USB Tap MUSICAL Tap WHEEL Tap PLAYING KEY Tap KEY MATCH COLOURS Tap KEY BEFORE TITLE Tap CLOSE Choice What you see STOCK The player's own scrolling waveform 3-BAND Layered lows, mids and highs (the default). 3-BAND COLOURS chooses their colours; see 3-band colours STEMS Drums, harmonics and vocals layered in their stem colours. A track without prepared stems shows 3-BAND The overview in each deck strip stays the player's own in every choice. When a deck plays its whole track from RAM after the music USB went out, a teal card in its lane says WHOLE TRACK IN RAM · PLAYABLE where the waveform was. See RAM tracks .","i":"classic"},{"c":"play-screen","a":"if-something-looks-wrong","t":"If something looks wrong","x":"Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap PLAYING KEY Tap PLAYING KEY Tap KEY MATCH COLOURS Tap KEY BEFORE TITLE Tap CLOSE You see Why What to do Dashes instead of numbers The value has not been read yet, or the deck has no track Wait a moment, or load a track A grey mode lamp that does not react The player does not let XZ Mods change that mode Change it in UTILITY (hold MENU ) NO STEM WAVE YET · 3BAND in a lane STEMS waveform chosen, but this track's stems are not loaded yet Wait, or prepare the track's stems. See Stems The key stays white on every deck No master deck, or KEY MATCH COLOURS is off Set a tempo master, or turn KEY MATCH COLOURS on in SCREEN","i":""},{"c":"browse","a":"","t":"Browsing and loading","x":"This chapter covers finding a track and putting it on a deck. MODERN has its own browse screens, built for touch and the rotary encoder. CLASSIC uses the player's own browse screens and adds the key, colours for compatible keys and a few labels to them.","i":""},{"c":"browse","a":"browsing-in-modern","t":"Browsing in MODERN","x":"Press BROWSE or TAG LIST to open that list, or hold BROWSE for SEARCH. PLAYLIST is in the BROWSE category rail and on the SHORTCUT screen. Press BACK to go up one level. At the top of a list BACK opens SOURCE, where you pick the USB to browse. Press BROWSE Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 7 clicks clockwise, then push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Press BACK Press BACK The TRACK category of USB1, sorted by title, with PREVIEW on and a row touched. Source The USB you are browsing, in its own colour. Tap to open SOURCE. Category rail ARTIST, ALBUM, TRACK, KEY, BPM, GENRE, RATING, COLOR, PLAYLIST, FOLDER, HISTORY and MATCHING. Tap one, or drag the rail to see the rest. BACK Goes up one level. PREVIEW Shows or hides the preview waveform column. INFO Opens the INFO panel for the highlighted track. Column title The arrow marks the column the list is sorted by. The number in brackets is how many items the list holds. Preview A small waveform of each track, so you can see breaks and builds before you load. Played A green note marks a track you have played. On a deck A blue number says the track is loaded on that deck. LOAD Appears on the row you touched. Tap 1 or 2 to load the track on that deck. Key colour Green or amber means the key mixes with the master deck's key. Deck strip Both decks' time, overview, tempo, key and BPM stay in view while you browse.","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"moving-through-a-list","t":"Moving through a list","x":"Press BROWSE Push ROTARY SELECTOR Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 5 clicks clockwise Press BACK Control What it does Turn the encoder Moves the highlight one row Push the encoder Opens a folder. On a track, opens the track menu: LOAD TO DECK for each deck, CUE / LOOP LIST when the track has memory points and the deck can load at one, and CANCEL. The active deck is highlighted, so a second push loads it there Hold the encoder Turns letter jump on. Turning then jumps by first letter, or by page where the list has no index. Push or hold again to stop Drag or flick the list Scrolls Tap a row Highlights it and shows LOAD BACK Up one level. At the top, opens SOURCE MENU Opens the list's MENU panel: sort, columns and the track menu INFO Opens or closes the INFO panel PREVIEW off: the PREVIEW OFF tile and the full width for the columns PREVIEW on Letter jump: the letter shows large while you turn Page jump in a list with no letter index The highlight near the end of a long list Rows still on their way from the USB stay blank for a moment The PLAYLIST category: folders and playlists The category rail dragged down to HISTORY and MATCHING Long names are cut to fit their column The first moment after opening, before the list has been read BROWSE before the USB's library has been read: LIST NOT READ YET PLAYLIST before it has been read TAG LIST before it has been read SEARCH before the library has been read Deck 2 empty in the deck strip The preview column starts hidden. One tap on PREVIEW shows it, and XZ Mods remembers your choice on the USB ( browse_preview ). PREVIEW is touch only.","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"loading-a-track","t":"Loading a track","x":"There are three ways to load the highlighted track: Press BROWSE Push ROTARY SELECTOR Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press LOAD 1 Press BACK Tap the row, then tap 1 or 2 on its LOAD chip. Push the encoder twice to load on the active deck, or push, turn to another deck and push. Press the LOAD button of the deck you want. If no track is highlighted, LOAD says SELECT A TRACK, THEN PRESS LOAD . On a screen that is not a track list it says OPEN A TRACK LIST TO LOAD . To load onto decks 3 and 4, see Four decks . The same row with deck 2 active: its 2 is highlighted Loading not available on this list: the row highlights without LOAD SELECT A TRACK, THEN PRESS LOAD","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"info-panel","t":"INFO panel","x":"Press INFO or tap INFO to open a panel with the highlighted track's details beside the list. The list narrows to make room. Press INFO Tap the screen Tap the screen Tap the screen Tap the screen Tap the screen The INFO panel: BPM, KEY, TIME, RATING, COLOR, PLAYED and ON DECK The INFO panel opened with INFO while keys are colour coded Keys coloured against deck 1's Fm","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"sort-columns-and-the-track-menu","t":"Sort, columns and the track menu","x":"Press MENU or tap a column title. The MENU panel opens on the right with the sort order, the columns to show, and the actions for the highlighted track. Press BROWSE Push ROTARY SELECTOR Press MENU Tap CUE/LOOP LIST Tap INTRO CUE The MENU panel on a track list, with three tracks already in the tag list. TRACK Actions for the highlighted track. ADD TO TAG LIST Adds the track to the tag list. On a track already in it this reads REMOVE FROM TAG LIST. CUE/LOOP LIST Not on the player in this version. MARK PLAYED Marks the track played. A played track offers MARK UNPLAYED. SEARCH Opens SEARCH. Tag marks Tracks in the tag list carry a check mark. Close Closes the panel. MENU and BACK close it too. Sort by: one choice at a time COLUMNS: tick the columns the list shows Six columns with PREVIEW off, sorted by BPM, highest first COLOR and TIME columns Check marks on tracks in the tag list HISTORY: ADD ALL TO TAG LIST, DELETE HISTORY and DELETE ALL HISTORIES","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"filter","t":"Filter","x":"Tap FILTER to narrow the list without leaving it. The filters stay on while you move between categories, and a chip in the header says which are on. Press BROWSE Press TRACK FILTER Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise, then push it Press BACK Filter What it keeps BPM Tracks within a range of the master deck's BPM, for example MASTER ±6 MATCH MASTER KEY Tracks whose key mixes with the master deck's key AT LEAST Tracks rated at least that many stars COLOR Tracks with any of the colours you tick MY TAG Not available yet CLEAR ALL FILTERS in the panel, or a tap on the chip, turns every filter off. Filters that compare with the master deck need one. Without it you see NO MASTER DECK: BPM FILTER OFF or NO MASTER KEY: KEY FILTER OFF . TRACK FILTER with BPM, key, rating and colour filters on The filter chip in the header. Tap it to clear every filter","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"search","t":"Search","x":"Hold BROWSE (SEARCH is printed above it), or tap SEARCH on the SHORTCUT screen. Type on the keyboard and the list updates as you type. SEARCH puts the keyboard away so you can scroll the results. DELETE removes a letter and CLEAR empties the field. Hold BROWSE for a second Tap A Tap B Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise Typing NEON. Eleven tracks match so far. Search field What you have typed. Count How many tracks match. SEARCH Puts the keyboard away and moves to the results. DELETE Removes the last letter. Key The key you touched is outlined. SEARCH before you type The results with the keyboard put away","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"tag-list","t":"Tag list","x":"The tag list is a quick list of tracks you want to play next. It holds up to 100 tracks and shows how many it has in the header. XZ Mods keeps it on the USB in XZMODS/playlists.txt , with your playlist changes. To add a track, use ADD TO TAG LIST in the MENU panel. To add a whole folder, highlight it and use ADD ALL TO TAG LIST. Press TAG LIST Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise Press MENU Press BACK The tag list with 12 of 100 tracks, one row touched The tag list full at 100 tracks MENU in the tag list: REMOVE FROM TAG LIST, CREATE PLAYLIST and REMOVE ALL TRACKS CREATE PLAYLIST: the tag list saved as a new playlist REMOVE ALL TRACKS armed: push again to clear the tag list","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"playlists","t":"Playlists","x":"Tap PLAYLIST in the BROWSE category rail, or on the SHORTCUT screen, to open the USB's playlists. You can also make your own and change them on the player. Press MENU in the playlist list or inside a playlist. Press BROWSE Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 6 clicks clockwise, then push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise, then push it Press BACK In the MENU panel What it does NEW PLAYLIST Makes a playlist in the folder that is open. Type its name on the keyboard RENAME Renames the highlighted playlist DELETE Deletes the highlighted playlist. Push again to confirm ADD TO PLAYLIST Adds the highlighted track to a playlist you pick REMOVE FROM PLAYLIST Takes the highlighted track out of the playlist MOVE TRACK Picks up a track. Turn the encoder to move it, push to drop it Playlists, the tag list, played marks and histories can change only on a USB that is not read-only. Changes made on the player are saved on the same USB in XZMODS/playlists.txt . They never change the library your DJ software exported, so your DJ software and the CLASSIC browse screens do not show them. A playlist you changed on the player is marked in the list. In HISTORY the MENU panel offers DELETE HISTORY and DELETE ALL HISTORIES, each after a second push. If the USB is read-only you see THIS STICK IS READ-ONLY: PLAYLISTS CANNOT CHANGE . If it is full you see THE STICK IS FULL: PLAYLIST NOT SAVED . The playlist list with its MENU panel open and DELETE highlighted. PLAYLIST Actions for the playlist list. NEW PLAYLIST Makes a playlist here. RENAME Renames the highlighted playlist. DELETE Deletes it after a second push. Sort and columns The same sort and column choices as in BROWSE. A playlist's tracks Playlist folders DELETE armed: push again to delete Naming a new playlist on the keyboard ADD TO PLAYLIST: pick the playlist A track picked up to move A playlist changed on the player, marked in the list","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"source","t":"SOURCE","x":"SOURCE shows every place music can come from, one tile each. Press BACK at the top of a list, or tap the source tile at the top left of BROWSE. Open SOURCE ( BACK at the top of a list) Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise Press BACK USB1 is being browsed and plays on both decks. USB2 is still loading. BROWSING The source BROWSE shows now. Name and colour The USB's name and the colour saved on it. Status READY, LOADING, NOT CONNECTED, or DECK'S OWN SCREEN where the player's own screen handles that source. FREE Free space on the USB. Decks The decks playing a track from this source. LINK Players on LINK. Browsing LINK from MODERN is not available yet. COMPUTER DJ software on a computer linked to the player. Browsing it from MODERN is not available yet. Hint Opening a source opens its library in BROWSE. Turn the encoder to pick a tile and push to open it, or tap it. A source the player's own screen handles opens that screen. Touch cannot open it yet; push the encoder instead. The highlight on COMPUTER USB2 being browsed while it loads Nothing connected LINK handled by the player's own screen COMPUTER handled by the player's own screen Long device names cut to fit Before the sources have been read SOURCE opened before anything has been read SOURCE reached with BACK from the top of BROWSE USB2 asked for with nothing in it BROWSE on a USB that has been removed: no old rows remain","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"info","t":"INFO","x":"Press INFO on the play screen, or tap the INFO icon in the top bar, to see everything about a loaded track. INFO for deck 1's track. Deck tabs Switch between the decks' tracks. Close Back to where you were. INFO and BACK close it too. Artwork The track's artwork, when the USB has it. RATING The track's stars. Linked field A field with an arrow opens BROWSE with every track that shares it. ARTIST, ALBUM, KEY, BPM and GENRE are linked. KEY and BPM Tap to open the KEY or BPM category at this value. COMMENT The comment saved with the track in your DJ software. SOURCE Where the track came from. Deck strip Both decks stay in view. Deck 2's track with a long title The highlight on KEY, ready to push The highlight on GENRE INFO for the track highlighted in a list, in its own tab A deck with no track INFO when browsing is not available: fields are not linked Long names cut to fit Before the track has been read INFO opened before anything has been read","i":"modern"},{"c":"browse","a":"browsing-in-classic","t":"Browsing in CLASSIC","x":"CLASSIC keeps the player's own browse screens: the same lists, keys and menus the XDJ-XZ operating instructions describe. XZ Mods adds three things to them. The key in every row. Each track row shows up to three fields from the library exported to your USB inside the title cell. The default is the title, then the key, then the BPM. Key before title. With KEY BEFORE TITLE on, the key leads the row, so you can read keys down the list. Key match colours. With KEY MATCH COLOURS on, a leading key is green when it mixes with the master deck's key, amber when it is detuned against it, and grey otherwise. The table header names what the player's own MENU click changes: SORT over the title column and COLUMN over the right-hand column. The STEMS and MODS buttons stay at the top right. These additions only use tracks on a USB with an exported library. A track XZ Mods cannot match in the export keeps the player's own row, and a field the export does not have is left out.","i":"classic"},{"c":"browse","a":"browse-settings","t":"Browse settings","x":"Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap KEY MATCH COLOURS Tap KEY BEFORE TITLE Tap CLOSE Press BROWSE Push ROTARY SELECTOR Press MENU Tap ARTIST Setting MODS What it does Default browse_preview PREVIEW tile in MODERN browse Shows the preview waveform column in MODERN browse Hidden browse_traffic SCREEN , KEY MATCH COLOURS Colours keys that mix with the master deck's key, in both interfaces On browse_key_prefix SCREEN , KEY BEFORE TITLE Puts the key first in each CLASSIC browse row On browse_1 , browse_2 , browse_3 none The three fields in each CLASSIC browse row, in order. Each is TITLE, ARTIST, KEY or BPM TITLE, KEY, BPM modern_browse_columns COLUMNS in the MODERN MENU panel The columns of the MODERN track list. TITLE always shows Automatic MODS has no control for the three CLASSIC row fields in this version. They keep the values stored on the USB. In MODERN, choose columns from the MENU panel instead.","i":""},{"c":"browse","a":"if-browsing-goes-wrong","t":"If browsing goes wrong","x":"Open SOURCE ( BACK at the top of a list) Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Press BROWSE Push ROTARY SELECTOR Press LOAD 1 You see What to do USB1 IS NOT CONNECTED or USB2 IS NOT CONNECTED Insert the USB, or pick another source USB SOURCE CHANGED: SELECT TRACK AGAIN The USB changed while you chose. Highlight the track again LOAD FROM THIS LIST IS OFF Load from a track list instead LINK BROWSING IS NOT AVAILABLE YET or COMPUTER BROWSING IS NOT AVAILABLE YET Switch to CLASSIC to browse that source TOUCH CANNOT OPEN THIS YET: PUSH THE ENCODER Highlight the tile and push the encoder PLAYLIST CHANGE NOT APPLIED Try again. If the USB is read-only or full, the notice says so","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"","t":"Stems","x":"Stems split a track into its parts so you can mute them live. XZ Mods plays three stems per track: VOCALS , HARMONICS (everything melodic that is not a voice) and DRUMS . You mute them from the pads or from buttons on the screen, change their levels by sliding, and switch back to the whole track with BYPASS . Stems work on decks 1 and 2. Decks 3 and 4 have no stems. Note MODERN labels the harmonics stem INST and the vocals stem VOCAL on its stem buttons. They are the same stems.","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"prepare-stems","t":"Prepare stems","x":"The player cannot split a track itself. You prepare stems on your computer, once per track, and they travel on the USB beside your music. Prepare the stems in the XZ Mods app on your computer, or in OverCue Desktop. See The XZ Mods app . Keep the stems on the same USB as the music. Your original files and the library your DJ software exported stay unchanged. On the player, load the original track through the normal browser and wait a moment for its stems to load. A track without prepared stems plays as normal. Its stem buttons say why, and the button at their end tells you what to do (see Stem readiness ).","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"turn-stems-on","t":"Turn stems on","x":"Open MODS, choose STEMS on the section rail, and turn USB STEMS on. It is on by default. With it off, every pad keeps its normal job and the stem buttons say STEMS ARE OFF or STEMS OFF . Press MENU Tap STEMS Tap USB STEMS Tap USB STEMS Tap CLOSE The STEMS page with USB stems on. USB STEMS Plays prepared stems from the USB. Off gives every pad its normal job back. Without the stem engine on the USB it reads SET UP USB STEMS and starts the setup. STEMS IN DJ SOFTWARE Sets up stem control for DJ software on a computer. See Stems in DJ software . STEM PADS Which pad mode gives stem pads, the stem order and the pad lights. See Stem pads . Stem buttons on screen Where the stem buttons sit on the play screen. The outlined tile is the current layout. STEM COLOURS The colour of each stem. See Stem colours . WORKS ON The decks this page applies to. Decks 3 and 4 have no stems.","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"stem-buttons-on-the-play-screen","t":"Stem buttons on the play screen","x":"Each deck gets three stem buttons and BYPASS . Tap a stem button to mute that stem, and tap it again to bring it back. A muted stem goes dark and keeps its level in its label. Tap STEMS HEADER Tap STEMS HEADER Tap STEMS HEADER Tap STEMS HEADER Tap STEMS HEADER Tap STEMS HEADER","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"modern-stem-buttons","t":"MODERN stem buttons","x":"Tap DRUMS Tap BYPASS Tap BYPASS BELOW / FULL rows. Deck 1 plays its stems with INST muted. Deck 2 is bypassed and plays the whole track. STEMS Lit blue while stems are on. Tap to step to the next layout. The marks under the label show which one is current. In 4 DECKS it shows or hides the stem buttons. DRUMS Tap to mute. Slide sideways to set the level. The fill and the percentage show it. VOCAL The vocals stem. INST Muted. It goes dark and keeps its level in the label. BYPASS Grey while the stems play. BYPASS lit Lit white, the deck plays the original track and every stem button goes dark. Tap again to hear the stems as you left them. On full-height rows each stem button is also a fader. Put a finger on it and slide right to raise the level or left to lower it. One button's width covers the whole range. A tap without a slide toggles the mute. Half-height rows and the small buttons beside the hot cues mute only. In 2 DECKS, STEMS in the top bar steps through six layouts in this order: beside the hot cues, below each deck at full height, below at half height, at the outer edges at full height, at the outer edges at half height, and hidden. You can also pick one in MODS under STEMS . MODERN keeps its own layout ( modern_stems ), so switching to CLASSIC and back does not change it. The default is the small buttons beside the hot cues. BY THE CUES: small buttons beside the hot-cue lamps (the default) BELOW / FULL: a full row under each deck's waveform BELOW / HALF: half-height rows, more room for the waveforms OUTER / FULL: above deck 1 and below deck 2 OUTER / HALF HIDDEN: full-height waveforms, stems still play The marks under STEMS follow the same order, so the lit mark tells you the layout without looking at the decks. First mark: BY THE CUES Second mark: BELOW / FULL Third mark: BELOW / HALF Fourth mark: OUTER / FULL Fifth mark: OUTER / HALF Sixth mark: HIDDEN BYPASS BUTTON in MODS under STEMS shows or hides the BYPASS button. Hidden, the stem buttons take its room and the pads still bypass. BYPASS beside the hot cues, deck 2 bypassed An older loader that does not report the layout: small buttons with BYPASS BYPASS on half rows BYPASS at the outer edges BYPASS at the outer edges, half height BYPASS BUTTON hidden: three wider stem buttons Sliding deck 1's DRUMS down to 35 % Deck 2 with DRUMS and VOCAL muted beside deck 1 playing all three Stems on with the stem buttons beside the hot cues STEMS waveform with stems muted on both decks VOCAL muted on deck 2 Two stems muted on deck 2, with stem colours of the DJ's own choice A track without stems: only the hot-cue lamps If stems are off when you tap STEMS , the layout still changes, and a notice says STEM ROWS SHOW ONCE STEMS ARE ON IN MODS .","i":"modern"},{"c":"stems","a":"stem-buttons-in-4-decks","t":"Stem buttons in 4 DECKS","x":"In a 4 DECKS view the lanes are too short for the layouts, so STEMS is a switch there. One tap hides the stem buttons on every deck, and the screen says STEM BUTTONS HIDDEN . The next tap brings them back and says STEM BUTTONS SHOWN . STEMS is lit while they show and has no layout marks. Your 2 DECKS layout does not change, and XZ Mods saves the 4 DECKS choice on the USB separately. Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Tap STEMS HEADER Tap STEMS HEADER A deck whose track has no prepared stems shows no stem buttons in 4 DECKS, and its waveform keeps the whole lane. The buttons appear when you load a track with stems. Decks 3 and 4 have no stems, so they never show stem buttons. Four decks has pictures.","i":"modern"},{"c":"stems","a":"classic-stem-rows","t":"CLASSIC stem rows","x":"In CLASSIC the stem rows sit inside the player's own waveform area, one row per deck. Tap the screen Tap the screen Tap the screen Two full rows. Deck 1 plays HARMONICS at 70 % with DRUMS muted. VOCALS Tap to mute. Slide sideways to set the level. Level The fill and the percentage show the stem's level. Muted A muted stem goes dark and reads MUTE with the level it returns to. BYPASS D1 OFF means deck 1 plays its stems. Tap to play the original track. In 2 DECKS, the STEMS button in the top right corner of the play screen steps the rows through five layouts: BELOW / FULL, BELOW / HALF, OUTER / FULL, OUTER / HALF and HIDDEN, then back to BELOW / FULL. Its five marks show the current one. Half rows give each waveform more height. HIDDEN gives the player's waveforms their full size back while the stems keep playing. CLASSIC keeps its own layout ( stems_overlay ). While four decks show in CLASSIC, no stem rows are drawn, and STEMS stays dark. A tap changes nothing and says STEM BUTTONS SHOW IN 2 DECKS VIEW . The layout comes back when you return to two decks.","i":"classic"},{"c":"stems","a":"stem-pads","t":"Stem pads","x":"The pads mute stems too, without looking at the screen. Open STEM PADS on the STEMS page. Press HOT CUE on the left deck Press pad A on the left deck Press pad B on the left deck Press pad C on the left deck Press pad D on the left deck Press pad A on the left deck HOT CUE gives stem pads on A to D, in the order VOCALS, HARMONICS, DRUMS. Pad mode button Pick the pad mode that gives stem pads: HOT CUE, BEAT LOOP, SLIP LOOP or BEAT JUMP. The other modes keep their normal pads. Stem pads Pads A, B and C mute the three stems in the order below. BYPASS pad Pad D plays the original track while lit. Other pads Pads E to H keep their normal job. STEMS ON Put the stems on pads A to D or on pads E to H. Order The stem order on the pads and on the screen. Push, then turn to change it. Pad lights STEM COLOURS lights the stem pads in their stem colours and dims a muted one. OFF leaves the lights to the player. SHIFT shortcut SHIFT + HOT CUE, BEAT LOOP or SLIP LOOP always gives stem pads, whatever mode you picked. Mute and bypass are performance state. They are not saved, and every track starts with all stems playing.","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"stem-order","t":"Stem order","x":"The order puts the stems where your fingers expect them. It changes the pads and the stem buttons on the screen together. There are six orders. Press MENU Tap STEMS Tap USB STEMS Tap BY THE CUES Tap BELOW / FULL Tap BELOW / HALF Tap OUTER / FULL Tap OUTER / HALF Tap HIDDEN Tap BYPASS BUTTON Order Pads A, B, C VOCALS / HARMONICS / DRUMS The default VOCALS / DRUMS / HARMONICS HARMONICS / VOCALS / DRUMS HARMONICS / DRUMS / VOCALS DRUMS / VOCALS / HARMONICS DRUMS / HARMONICS / VOCALS The layered STEMS waveform and the stem row for DJ software keep their own order.","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"stem-colours","t":"Stem colours","x":"Each stem has a colour on the pads, the stem buttons and the STEMS waveform. In the ORIGINAL theme drums are blue, harmonics red and vocals green. Every theme has its own shades. Press MENU Tap STEMS Tap STEM COLOURS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise All three stems follow the theme. Stem DRUMS, HARMONICS and VOCALS each have their own column. THEME Follows the theme you chose. The outlined tile is the current choice. Bass A four-stem track's bass always follows the theme. Preview The three colours as the STEMS waveform draws them. RESET STEM COLORS Puts all three back to THEME. The choices are THEME, BLUE, RED, GREEN, AMBER, PURPLE, CYAN, PINK and WHITE. A fixed colour stays when you change theme. Amber drums, cyan harmonics and pink vocals on half rows The STEMS waveform zoomed out The STEMS waveform zoomed in The STEMS waveform at full zoom on the play screen Deck 2's stems not loaded yet: it draws 3-BAND and says NO STEM WAVE YET","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"stem-readiness","t":"Stem readiness","x":"Each deck's stem buttons tell you whether its stems can play. When they cannot, the stem buttons go dark and the last button names the reason. Where you can fix it from the player, that button does it. Press MENU Tap STEMS Tap SET UP USB STEMS Tap CHECK STEM ENGINE Tap TURN ON USB STEMS / DECKS 1 + 2 Tap CHECK THIS DECK AGAIN Tap CHECK THIS DECK AGAIN Tap STEMS READY / BACK TO PLAY On the stem row What it means What to do STEMS READY The stems play Nothing NO STEM ENGINE, with SET UP The USB loader has no stem engine Update the USB loader with XZ Mods on your computer, then restart the player STEMS OFF, with TURN ON USB STEMS is off Tap TURN ON, or turn USB STEMS on in MODS NO TRACK LOADED The deck is empty Load a track from USB on this deck NOT PREPARED, with HOW TO FIX This track has no prepared stems Prepare it in XZ Mods on your computer, then load it again LOADING STEMS The stems are loading from USB Wait a moment PLAY TO ALIGN The stems are loaded and wait for the track Press PLAY. The stems lock to the track a few seconds in STEM SET ERROR, with HOW TO FIX A stem file is missing or damaged Verify the track in XZ Mods on your computer STEMS READY on deck 1 NO STEM ENGINE on both decks STEMS OFF on both decks NO TRACK LOADED on deck 1 NOT PREPARED on deck 1, with HOW TO FIX LOADING STEMS on deck 1 PLAY TO ALIGN on deck 1 STEM SET ERROR on deck 1 USB STEMS off and no deck ready: TURN ON for all decks In MODERN the stem buttons on a deck that cannot play stems read STEMS ARE OFF or NO STEMS ON THIS TRACK , and only the hot-cue lamps stay in the pad row. In 4 DECKS such a deck shows no stem buttons, and its waveform keeps the whole lane.","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"usb-stems-setup","t":"USB STEMS setup","x":"Tap SET UP or HOW TO FIX on a stem row, or SET UP USB STEMS in MODS, to open USB STEMS setup. It checks one deck at a time and walks you through the three steps: check the engine, turn stems on, load a prepared track. Deck 1 has found its OverCue stems and waits for PLAY. DECK 1 / DECK 2 The deck this setup checks. Steps Check the engine, turn stems on, load a prepared track. Deck status Where this deck stands now. FOUND The stem format found for this track. Next step What to do next, in one line. Action Does the next step, or checks the deck again. STEMS READY: STEMS READY / BACK TO PLAY NO STEM ENGINE STEMS OFF NO TRACK LOADED NOT PREPARED LOADING STEMS STEM SET ERROR, with the missing file named The setup page reached from MODS","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"stems-in-dj-software","t":"Stems in DJ software","x":"When the XZ plays from DJ software on a computer over USB, the stem buttons can switch the software's stems instead. Open STEMS IN DJ SOFTWARE on the STEMS page and follow its four steps for each deck: DETECT , MAP STEMS , LIVE TEST and CONFIRM . Press MENU Tap STEMS Tap STEMS IN DJ SOFTWARE Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise Experimental Stem switching works after the live test. Levels and BYPASS for DJ software need more checking, and the software has no stem bypass over USB. Deck 1 before setup, with no computer deck found yet. Deck The deck this setup checks. Status The deck's source, the link to the computer and whether stem switching has been tested. Steps DETECT, MAP STEMS, LIVE TEST and CONFIRM. DETECT PC Checks that this deck plays from the computer. Connect the XZ to the computer by USB and open your DJ software in Performance mode before you start. A deck playing from the computer then shows a stem row for the software, with three or four stems. Four software stems ready on deck 1, the XZ's own stems on deck 2 Four stems with the software's on and off state shown A switch sent, waiting for the software to confirm A stem button held down Not tested yet: SET UP PC LINK LOST: nothing is sent Source not confirmed yet Three software stems ready Three stems with feedback Three stems, a switch pending Three stems, a button held Three stems, not tested yet Three stems, PC link lost Three stems, source not confirmed Setup, four stems, before the live test Setup done, four stems Four stems with feedback Four stems, a switch pending Four stems, link lost Four stems, source not confirmed Setup, three stems, before the live test Setup done, three stems Three stems with feedback Three stems, a switch pending Three stems, link lost Three stems, source not confirmed","i":""},{"c":"stems","a":"if-stems-do-not-play","t":"If stems do not play","x":"You see What to do No stem buttons at all in MODERN Tap STEMS in the top bar until the layout you want shows. HIDDEN shows none. In 4 DECKS, tap STEMS once. A deck whose track has no stems shows none STEMS ARE OFF Turn USB STEMS on in MODS under STEMS NO STEMS ON THIS TRACK or NOT PREPARED Prepare the track in the XZ Mods app, copy it to the USB, then load it again PLAY TO ALIGN does not go away Let the track play for a few seconds. If it stays, check the track in the XZ Mods app Stems on decks 3 and 4 Not available. Stems work on decks 1 and 2 only","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"","t":"Beat jump and performance features","x":"XZ Mods adds performance features to the pads and deck keys: two pages of beat jump sizes you choose, gate cue, smart cue, key shift and KEY SYNC, and RAM tracks. Their settings live on one MODS page, PLAY. Every change saves to your USB as you make it.","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"the-play-page","t":"The PLAY page","x":"Open MODS and choose PLAY in the section rail. Press MENU Tap PLAY Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press BACK The PLAY page with the default settings: gate cue and smart cue off, the default jump sizes, and the button above LINK on INTERFACE. BEAT JUMP PADS Opens the beat jump editor. The numbers are your page 1 and page 2 sizes in beats. GATE CUE Hot cues play only while you hold the pad. Off by default. SMART CUE A hot cue press also moves the CUE point there. Off by default. KEYS Opens the key page: key shift and KEY SYNC for all four decks. RAM TRACKS Opens RAM TRACKS: copy a deck's track into memory. BUTTON ABOVE LINK What the button above LINK does, alone and with SHIFT. See Controls on the player. Dock Explains the highlighted row in plain words. Works on The decks the highlighted feature works on, in mixer order 3 1 2 4. A dim number is a deck it does not work on, with the reason below. If the cue engine has not reported on this USB loader, GATE CUE and SMART CUE show as SET UP GATE CUE and SET UP SMART CUE instead of switches. See Feature setup .","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"beat-jump","t":"Beat jump","x":"In BEAT JUMP mode the eight pads form four pairs: A/B, C/D, E/F and G/H. The first pad of a pair jumps back, the second jumps forward, by the same number of beats. With a loop on, the loop moves by that amount instead. Press MENU Tap PLAY Tap BEAT JUMP PADS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise Press BEAT JUMP on the left deck Press pad A on the left deck Press pad B on the left deck Press pad C on the left deck Press pad D on the left deck Press pad E on the left deck Press pad F on the left deck Press pad G on the left deck Press pad H on the left deck Hold SHIFT on the left deck and press BEAT JUMP on the left deck Press pad A on the left deck Press pad B on the left deck Press pad C on the left deck Press pad D on the left deck Press pad E on the left deck Press pad F on the left deck Press pad G on the left deck Press pad H on the left deck You get two pages of sizes: Page How you select it Default sizes A/B, C/D, E/F, G/H Page 1 Press BEAT JUMP 1, 2, 4, 8 beats Page 2 Hold SHIFT , press BEAT JUMP , let go of SHIFT 16, 32, 64, 128 beats (4, 8, 16, 32 bars) Page 1 Press BEAT JUMP . With the default sizes the pairs A/B, C/D, E/F and G/H jump 1, 2, 4 and 8 beats. The first pad of a pair jumps back, the second forward. Page 2 Hold SHIFT , press BEAT JUMP , let go of SHIFT . The pairs jump 16, 32, 64 and 128 beats, and the pads light warm red and amber. With a loop on With a loop on, the loop moves by the jump instead. Press BEAT JUMP for page 1, or SHIFT + BEAT JUMP for page 2. Let go of SHIFT . Press a pad. The first pad of a pair jumps back, the second forward. Each deck remembers its own page. Choosing another pad mode and coming back with BEAT JUMP gives page 1 again. On page 2 the pads light warm red and amber, so you can see which page you are on. SHIFT + pad keeps its normal job on decks 1 and 2.","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"change-the-jump-sizes","t":"Change the jump sizes","x":"Open MODS > PLAY > BEAT JUMP PADS. The editor shows the pads as they sit on the deck: A to D on top, E to H below. Press MENU Tap PLAY Tap BEAT JUMP PADS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to PAGE 2 and push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to PAGE 1 and push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to PAGE 1: MY SIZES and push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to PAGE 2 and push it Editing page 2. Pads A and B are selected and jump 16 beats. PAGE 1 Edit the sizes BEAT JUMP gives. PAGE 2 Edit the sizes SHIFT + BEAT JUMP gives. The filled tab is the page you are editing. PAGE 1: STOCK or MY SIZES STOCK keeps the player's own 1, 2, 4 and 8 beats on page 1. MY SIZES uses yours. Page 2 always uses yours. Pad pair Two pads with one size. The left pad jumps back, the right pad forward. The selected pair has a light outline. Beats The size in beats. Bars The same size in bars. 4 beats make 1 bar. Readout The selected pair and its size. Sizes Tap a size to give it to the selected pair. The filled size is the current one. Dock What the highlighted control does. Works on Beat jump works on all four decks. Choose PAGE 1 or PAGE 2. For page 1, choose PAGE 1: MY SIZES. With STOCK, page 1 keeps the player's own sizes. Tap a pad in the pair you want to change. Tap a size in the row along the bottom. Without the touch screen, turn the rotary selector to a pair, push it, then turn to step the size. It stops at the smallest and largest size. Push or press BACK when you are done. Sizes you can choose Beats 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256 Bars 1/4, 1/2, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64 The sizes apply to every deck. UTILITY's own beat jump setting is separate and does not change them. Setting Choices Default PAGE 1 STOCK, MY SIZES MY SIZES Page 1 A/B, C/D, E/F, G/H 1 to 256 beats 1, 2, 4, 8 beats Page 2 A/B, C/D, E/F, G/H 1 to 256 beats 16, 32, 64, 128 beats","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"decks-3-and-4","t":"Decks 3 and 4","x":"Decks 3 and 4 use the same sizes and both pages. They jump along the track's beat grid, or by its BPM when there is no grid. A track with neither jumps at 120 BPM, as on decks 1 and 2. With a loop on, the loop moves.","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"when-a-jump-is-refused","t":"When a jump is refused","x":"A jump the deck cannot make does nothing else. XZ Mods never silently shortens the selected distance. The screen shows why: Press BEAT JUMP on the left deck Press pad A on the left deck Notice Deck What it means JUMP UNAVAILABLE: TRACK EDGE, BUFFER OR DECK STATE 1 or 2 The player refused the jump. It would pass the start or end of the track, or the deck cannot jump right now. JUMP UNAVAILABLE: BEFORE TRACK START 3 or 4 The jump would land before the start of the track. JUMP UNAVAILABLE: AFTER TRACK END 3 or 4 The jump would land after the end of the track. JUMP UNAVAILABLE: LOOP MOVE OUT OF TRACK 3 or 4 Moving the loop would push it past the start or end. JUMP UNAVAILABLE: NO BEAT GRID OR BPM 3 or 4 The track's beat grid is damaged, so beats can't be counted. Analyse it again in your DJ software.","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"gate-cue-and-smart-cue","t":"Gate cue and smart cue","x":"Both change what a hot cue pad does in HOT CUE mode. Turn them on in MODS > PLAY. Both are off by default, and each works on its own. Press MENU Tap PLAY Tap GATE CUE Tap SMART CUE Tap CLOSE Press HOT CUE on the left deck Press pad A on the left deck Feature What a hot cue pad does GATE CUE The track plays from the hot cue only while you hold the pad. Let go and it jumps back to the hot cue and pauses. Use it to stab hot cues like samples. Press PLAY/PAUSE while you hold the pad to keep playing after you let go. SMART CUE Calling a hot cue also moves the CUE point there, so CUE takes you back to the last hot cue you used. Recording a new hot cue does not move it. Gate cue and smart cue work on all four decks. On decks 1 and 2 they need the cue engine; see below.","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"feature-setup","t":"Feature setup","x":"When the cue engine has not reported on a deck, MODS shows a short setup instead of the switch. It checks the feature on a loaded USB track in four steps: detect, choose deck, enable and test. Press MENU Tap PLAY Tap SET UP GATE CUE Tap DETECT FEATURE Tap DETECT FEATURE Tap USE SELECTED DECK Tap ENABLE FEATURE Tap I TESTED IT / DONE The setup page at its first step, checking gate cue. For smart cue it reads SMART CUE. Feature The feature this setup checks. Steps The four steps. The button at the bottom always runs the next one. Deck Choose deck 1 or deck 2. What to do The instruction for the current step. Track The track loaded on the chosen deck. Status FEATURE DETECTED, or what to do when it is missing. Next step Runs the step. Missing support keeps its reason on the screen. Load a track from USB on deck 1 or deck 2. Press DETECT FEATURE. Choose the deck, then enable the feature. Close MODS and test it: hold and release a hot cue for gate cue, or call a hot cue and check that the cue point follows for smart cue. Reopen the setup and confirm. If the status still asks you to load a USB track while one is loaded, prepare the USB again with the current XZ Mods app .","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"keys-and-key-sync","t":"Keys and KEY SYNC","x":"XZ Mods can move the key of any deck a semitone at a time, and match a deck's key to the master deck with KEY SYNC. The master can be any deck, 1 to 4. The key display then shows the key the track plays in now. Press MENU Tap PLAY Tap KEYS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise Hold SHIFT on the left deck and press SYNC on the left deck","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"from-the-deck","t":"From the deck","x":"Load tracks with analysed keys, and make the deck you want to match to the tempo master. Hold SHIFT and press SYNC on the deck you want to move. On a side that drives deck 3 or 4, this moves that deck. The deck shifts to a key that fits the master deck and MASTER TEMPO turns on. A notice shows the new key and the master deck, with RELATIVE KEY when it matches the relative major or minor. To end KEY SYNC, press SHIFT + SYNC again, or press MASTER TEMPO . Both return the deck to its own key and put MASTER TEMPO back the way it was. After that, MASTER TEMPO does its normal job. KEY SYNC changes the key only. The tempo, SYNC and the master deck stay as they were. All four decks can hold key shifts and KEY SYNC together. Before starting a new shift on deck 3 or 4, the player checks its measured audio workload. If there is too little headroom, it shows KEY SHIFT REFUSED: AUDIO LOAD TOO HIGH and leaves the current keys unchanged. Shifts already in use keep running. SYSTEM READOUT shows render times and the number of active key shifters. If KEY SYNC cannot work, a notice or the deck's key display shows why for a few seconds: Message What to do KEY ENGINE OFF: SET UP KEYS This USB loader has no key engine. Open MODS > PLAY > KEYS and press SET UP KEYS, or prepare the USB again with the current XZ Mods app. DECK 1 TRACK HAS NO KEY (or another deck) The track on this deck has no analysed key. Analyse it in your DJ software. LOAD AN ANALYZED TRACK / SET UP KEYS The deck has no track with an analysed key. Load one. LOAD A KEYED TRACK ON DECK 2 (or another deck) The master deck has no track with an analysed key. THIS DECK IS MASTER, MAKE DECK 2 MASTER FIRST The deck you pressed is the master, so there is nothing to match. Make another deck the master. On the KEYS page the master deck has no KEY SYNC button and says it is the master. SELECT ONE LOCAL MASTER / SET UP KEYS No deck on this player is the tempo master. Press MASTER on the deck to match to. VERIFY MASTER PLAYING KEY / SET UP KEYS The master deck's playing key is not known yet. Let it play a moment, then try again. MASTER CHANGED / RETRY KEY SYNC, TRACK CHANGED / RETRY KEY CONTROL The master or the track changed before the key moved. Press again. KEY SHIFT REFUSED: AUDIO LOAD TOO HIGH Measured audio work leaves too little headroom for a new shift. Existing shifts keep running. Check SYSTEM READOUT and retry when the load falls. SHIFT OUT OF RANGE, KEY RANGE IS -12 TO +12 SEMITONES The key that fits is further away than the deck can shift. EMERGENCY LOOP / LOAD NEXT TRACK The deck lost its track and loops. Load another track first.","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"the-keys-page","t":"The KEYS page","x":"MODS > PLAY > KEYS does the same from the screen, and adds key shift by semitones. On the play screen, tapping a deck's key opens the same controls for that deck. Press MENU Tap PLAY Tap KEYS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to KEY UP and push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to KEY DOWN and push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to RESET and push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to KEY SYNC and push it The KEYS page for deck 1 with the key engine ready. The deck is in its own key. Deck Choose deck 1, 2, 3 or 4. Where there is room, a tab adds USB DECK for decks 1 and 2 and SOFTWARE for decks 3 and 4. KEY DOWN Lowers the deck's key one semitone. RESET Shows the current shift. Press it to return the deck to its own key. KEY UP Raises the deck's key one semitone. KEY SYNC Shifts the deck to a key that fits the master deck, as SHIFT + SYNC does. Deck keys Each deck's own key, the key it plays in now, the cents and SYNC or MASTER. The rows are empty in this picture. Works on Key shift and KEY SYNC work on all four decks. With MASTER TEMPO on, the key holds while the tempo moves. Without it, the tempo changes the key too, and the key display shows that. When the key engine has not reported, the buttons show an amber dot, the dock says NOT READY and SET UP KEYS appears. It opens a short setup that checks the key engine and the chosen deck's track, and ends with a live test: The KEYS page before the key engine reports, with SET UP KEYS The KEYS page before the key engine reports, with SET UP KEYS","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"the-key-on-the-modern-play-screen","t":"The key on the MODERN play screen","x":"In MODERN each deck's panel beside its waveform shows its key. With PLAYING KEY on, the big key is the key the track plays in now, after tempo and key shift. Deck 2 holds KEY SYNC: it plays Bb minor, moved up from its own A minor, 12 cents sharp. Key panel KEY SYNC, the key the deck plays in now, the cents left over and the track's own key. Deck in its own key Deck 1 plays in its own key, so the panel shows only KEY and the key. MT MASTER TEMPO. It blinks while KEY SYNC holds on that deck. Part of the key panel Meaning KEY SYNC KEY SYNC holds on this deck. The big key The key the deck plays in now. Green or amber compares it with the master deck's key; see Key and KEY SYNC . +12¢ Cents between the playing key and the nearest semitone. ORIGINAL The track's own key, shown when the playing key differs. ▲1 The key shift in semitones, on older USB loaders that do not report the analysed key. KEY SYNC with the MT lamp in the dark half of its blink With MASTER TEMPO off, +2.20 % tempo lifts A minor by 38 cents With MASTER TEMPO off and +6.10 % tempo, the track plays in Bb minor Keys in WHEEL notation, deck 1 shifted down two semitones An older USB loader shows the key and its shift step only No key on deck 1, and a key name too long for the panel The top bar lamps and QUANTIZE lamps hidden The same, with BEAT FX on","i":"modern"},{"c":"performance","a":"the-key-on-the-classic-play-screen","t":"The key on the CLASSIC play screen","x":"In CLASSIC, XZ Mods draws the playing key where the player shows its beat countdown, under the key: What you see Meaning KEY and a key The track plays in its own key. TRACK KEY Deck 3 or 4 shows the track's own key until it reports the key it plays in. Own key ▸ playing key The tempo or a key shift moved the key. SYNC KEY SYNC holds on this deck. The tile turns green while the key matches the master. MASTER This deck is the master that KEY SYNC matches to. +12c in amber Cents between the playing key and the nearest semitone. Green or amber key The playing key compared with the master deck's key, as KEY MATCH COLOURS sets it. A message in red KEY SYNC could not work; see the table above.","i":"classic"},{"c":"performance","a":"playing-key","t":"PLAYING KEY","x":"PLAYING KEY is on by default. Turn it off in MODS > SCREEN to show the track's own key instead. In CLASSIC, off brings the beat countdown back. Key notation (AS ON THE USB, MUSICAL or WHEEL) is set on the same page; see Screen, interfaces and themes . Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap PLAYING KEY Tap PLAYING KEY Tap KEY MATCH COLOURS Tap KEY BEFORE TITLE Tap CLOSE Decks 3 and 4 show their playing key too, after tempo and key shift. Until a software deck reports it, the deck shows the track's own key.","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"ram-tracks","t":"RAM tracks","x":"RAM TRACKS copies the track on a deck into the player's memory. The deck then plays from memory, so it keeps playing if the music USB goes out. It works on all four decks. Decks 3 and 4 need the loopback cable connected to start a copy. Press MENU Tap PLAY Tap RAM TRACKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to LOAD TRACK INTO RAM and push it Deck 1 on a USB loader without the RAM engine. Deck Choose deck 1, 2, 3 or 4. State The deck and the state of its RAM copy. Source The track loaded on that deck, or what to do next. Progress How much of the track is copied, in MiB. Memory How much of the 128 MiB the copies use, prepared stems apart, then each deck's copy and state. Action The one next step for this state: set up, choose a track, load, cancel, retry or release. Scope What RAM holds for this deck. COPIES AUDIO / STEMS STAY ON USB means only the original audio goes into RAM. Reason Why the feature is not available. Here the RAM engine is missing. Load a track from USB on the deck. Open MODS > PLAY > RAM TRACKS and choose that deck. Press LOAD TRACK INTO RAM. Keep the USB connected while it copies. Wait for ORIGINAL AUDIO IN RAM. A track that plays is also copied on its own when there is room. CANCEL COPY or RELEASE RAM COPY stops that for the loaded track. State Button What it means RAM ENGINE NOT DETECTED SET UP RAM TRACKS This USB loader has no RAM engine, or it has not reported yet. The setup checks the engine. If it stays, prepare the USB again with the current XZ Mods app. LOOPBACK CABLE NOT CONNECTED SET UP FOUR DECKS Deck 3 or 4 is chosen and decks 3 and 4 are not running. The button opens 4 DECKS. NOT IN RAM LOAD TRACK INTO RAM The deck plays from USB. COPYING TO RAM CANCEL COPY The copy is running. Cancel leaves the track playing from USB. ORIGINAL AUDIO IN RAM RELEASE RAM COPY The deck plays from memory. Release frees the memory and needs the USB still connected. COPY FAILED RETRY LOAD INTO RAM The track keeps playing from USB. Retry; if it fails again, load the track again from USB. USB OUT / RAM COPY ONLY BACK TO PLAY The USB is out and the deck plays from memory. The play screen says so in the deck's lane; see below . Load another track to release the copy. When a copy does not fit, the page says why and offers the next step: Message What to do This file exceeds the 64 MiB RAM limit. Press CHOOSE ANOTHER TRACK. Other RAM tracks leave too little space for this file. Press MANAGE RAM TRACKS, choose a deck with a copy and release it. Free RAM cannot keep the 64 MiB safety reserve. Release another copy the same way. One track per deck. Each file can be up to 64 MiB, and all four decks together up to 128 MiB. The player always keeps 64 MiB of its memory free. RAM TRACKS copies the original audio. On decks 1 and 2, the line under the action button says what else is held; see the table below. On decks 3 and 4 the waveform, beat grid and cues already loaded stay with the copy when the USB goes out. Cues you change then are kept for the session and not written to a USB. If the loopback cable goes out, decks 3 and 4 keep their copies and pause, as they do without RAM. They do not start again on their own when the cable returns. Loading another track on the deck drops its RAM copy.","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"when-the-music-usb-goes-out","t":"When the music USB goes out","x":"Press BROWSE Push ROTARY SELECTOR Press LOAD 1 NOT IN RAM The deck plays from USB. COPYING TO RAM Press LOAD TRACK INTO RAM. Keep the USB connected while it copies. ORIGINAL AUDIO IN RAM The deck plays from memory. USB OUT / RAM COPY ONLY The music USB goes out and the deck plays on from memory. A teal card, WHOLE TRACK IN RAM · PLAYABLE, takes the waveform's place and says how to get it back. A deck with its whole track in RAM keeps playing when the music USB goes out. The waveform was read from the USB, so the deck's lane cannot draw it any more. A teal card takes its place: WHOLE TRACK IN RAM · PLAYABLE , and under it how to get the waveform back. Everything else about the deck stays on screen: title and artist, time and remain, BPM, tempo, key, the lamps, the hot cues and the playhead. 2 DECKS: deck 1 plays from RAM. Deck 2 is unchanged Both decks play from RAM 4 DECKS: decks 2 and 4 play from RAM MIXER order: the card stays with its deck Deck 1 plays from RAM after the USB went out. The stem rows, the deck column and the deck strip stay as the player shows them. RAM card The deck plays its whole track from RAM. The second line says how to get the waveform back. To get the waveform back, reinsert the same USB or insert another, then load a track from it. The card goes as soon as the deck has a waveform to draw again. Loading a track also ends the deck's RAM copy, as it always does. On decks 3 and 4 the waveform loaded before the USB went out stays, so the card shows there only if the waveform had not loaded yet. Line under the button, decks 1 and 2 What it means COPIES AUDIO / STEMS STAY ON USB No copy yet. RAM TRACKS copies the audio, not the stems. AUDIO IN RAM / STEMS NEED USB The audio is in RAM. The stems still read the USB. AUDIO + STEMS IN RAM / WAVES KEPT The deck's prepared stems are held in RAM as well, and the loaded waveforms stay. Experimental Playing on from RAM after the USB goes out has not been confirmed on a player yet. Keep the USB in during a set.","i":""},{"c":"performance","a":"quantize","t":"Quantize","x":"On decks 1 and 2, quantize is the player's own: DECK QUANTIZE and UTILITY work as without XZ Mods. In MODERN each deck shows its QUANTIZE lamp and beat value above its time. You can hide them in MODS > SCREEN > LAMPS AND TITLES. Press DECK QUANTIZE Press DECK QUANTIZE While a side drives deck 3 or 4: Key Action DECK QUANTIZE Switches quantize for every deck. Decks 1 and 2 switch through the player as before. SHIFT + DECK QUANTIZE Switches quantize only for the deck of that side. With quantize on, decks 3 and 4 put cue points, loop in and out, hot cues and beat and slip loops on the beat grid, at a one-beat value. SYNC then also locks the deck to the master's beat. Four decks has the rest of what decks 3 and 4 do.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"","t":"Four decks","x":"Four decks adds two software players, DECK 3 and DECK 4, to the XDJ-XZ's own DECK 1 and DECK 2. You hear them on mixer channels CH3 and CH4. A short USB cable from the back of the player to a top USB port carries their sound into the mixer: it leaves through a top USB port and comes back in at the rear USB socket, where a computer with DJ software would connect. The physical controls switch between decks with the same presses DJ software uses on the XDJ-XZ. Decks 3 and 4 Decks 3 and 4 are software players. They run inside the player, beside decks 1 and 2. Top USB Their sound leaves the player through the top USB port the cable is in, USB 1 or USB 2. Loopback cable The loopback cable carries it over the back edge of the player. Rear USB It comes back in at the rear USB socket, where a computer with DJ software would connect. CH3 and CH4 With their input switches on USB, mixer channels CH3 and CH4 play decks 3 and 4. Experimental Four decks is experimental in this version. Test it with your own tracks before a set, keep the music stick connected, and keep a two-deck plan ready.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"what-you-need","t":"What you need","x":"The loopback cable : a USB cable with a USB-B plug on one end and a USB-A plug on the other, the kind a printer uses. For tracks, a music stick in the other top USB port, or music sticks on one USB 2.0 hub in that port. Decks 3 and 4 can start before you insert any music. Decks 1 and 2 stopped or paused while decks 3 and 4 start. Once they run, you can play all four decks. CH3 and CH4 on the mixer set to USB so you hear decks 3 and 4. The cable goes directly from the rear USB socket to either USB 1 or USB 2 on top. Put music in the other top port. The picture uses USB 1 as an example; both arrangements work. One USB-B to USB-A cable runs from the rear USB socket over the back edge into a top USB port; the picture shows USB 1. No computer is involved.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"set-up-four-decks","t":"Set up four decks","x":"Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Tap RESCAN Stop or pause decks 1 and 2. Choose either top USB port for the loopback cable. Leave the other port for music. Plug the USB-B end of the loopback cable into the rear USB socket . Plug the USB-A end directly into your chosen top port, USB 1 or USB 2 . Set the CH3 and CH4 input switches to USB . Tap DECKS at the top of the play screen and choose one of the 4 DECKS pictures, or open MODS and choose 4 DECKS . Wait for DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY . The card in the lanes of decks 3 and 4 tells you each step it is waiting for. Press SHIFT twice on the left side to play deck 3, or on the right side to play deck 4. Decks 3 and 4 start as soon as the cable is in, even when decks 1 and 2 have no tracks loaded. You can leave the cable connected before starting the USB loader. No RESCAN is needed. Decks 1 and 2 must be stopped or paused while the route starts. RESCAN checks at once if you want to check again. After a disconnection, reconnect the cable to the same top port. To move it to the other port, stop playback and restart the USB loader first. Note The XZ Mods app shows steps 2 to 5 with an animation of the cable while it writes your USB and when it is done. You set four decks up at the player, not in the app. Tip You can choose a four-deck view before you plug in the cable. Decks 3 and 4 then show a card with the cable steps and their current state, and decks 1 and 2 keep playing as usual.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"add-music-and-a-usb-hub","t":"Add music and a USB hub","x":"Once the USB loader is running, you can bring up decks 3 and 4 with only the loopback cable connected. Insert music later in the other top port. Starting the audio route does not load a track. To connect several music sticks, put one high-speed USB 2.0 hub in the top port opposite the loopback cable. Stop or pause decks 1 and 2 while a newly connected hub starts. Connect the sticks to that hub and choose the sources the player makes available. The hub does not add more decks or source buttons. Connect the loopback cable directly to the player, never through the music hub. Do not connect a second hub behind the first. Check that your hub and drives have enough power; use the hub's own power supply if it has one. Keep any drive that holds a playing track connected.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"the-4-decks-page-in-mods","t":"The 4 DECKS page in MODS","x":"MODS > 4 DECKS shows the cable's state, lets you choose the deck view, and lists what works on each deck. Press MENU Tap 4 DECKS Tap 4 DECKS Tap 4 DECKS Tap 2 DECKS The 4 DECKS page before the cable is plugged in. In this picture the key and RAM engines have not reported yet, so KEY SYNC has no tick on decks 1 and 2 and RAM TRACKS none on any deck. Cable picture Shows USB 1 as an example; USB 2 works too. The picture explains the connections, not which port is currently occupied. State Where four decks stand now, with one sentence on what happens next. The states are listed under The card in every state . RESCAN Checks the cable and the audio route now. Reads TRY AGAIN after a failed start and SCANNING while a check runs. DECK VIEW 2 DECKS, 4 DECKS in number order (1 2 3 4) or 4 DECKS in mixer order (3 1 2 4). The highlighted box is the saved view. Deck columns One column per deck, in mixer order 3 1 2 4, the same on both halves of the grid. Feature row A tick means the feature works on that deck. A dash means it does not. Turn the encoder onto a row and the dock says why. Dock Explains the highlighted control or row. Save state Confirms that your deck view is saved to the USB. The HOME page shows the same state on the 4 DECKS card. When four decks need you (no cable found, a failed start, a lost connection, or no four-deck engine on the USB loader) HOME also shows SET UP FOUR DECKS , which opens this page. If the USB loader has no four-deck engine, the page says so and offers CHECK INSTALLED ENGINE . Rebuild the USB loader in the XZ Mods app , restart the player with it, then press CHECK INSTALLED ENGINE . HOME status line What it means Not connected No loopback cable found yet. Looking for the cable A check is running now. Starting decks 3 and 4 The cable is found and the software players are starting, or they wait for decks 1 and 2 to stop. Ready, 2 decks shown Decks 3 and 4 run. The play screen shows two decks. Ready, 4 decks shown Decks 3 and 4 run. The play screen shows four decks. Could not start The start failed. The 4 DECKS page says why. Disconnected The cable was unplugged or lost power. Not available on this player The software players are not running in this build.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"the-card-in-every-state","t":"The card in every state","x":"While decks 3 and 4 are not running, a four-deck view puts a card in their lanes. The card shows the cable steps, the state, and the buttons you need. Decks 1 and 2 stay live above it. In number order the card fills the lanes of decks 3 and 4 under decks 1 and 2. In mixer order it splits into a strip above deck 1 and a strip below deck 2. Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Four decks in number order before the cable is plugged in. CLASSIC draws the same card in its own colours, with shorter sentences. Cable picture USB 1 is the illustrated example; USB 2 works too. The picture moves for a minute after the card appears or your last input, then rests. Steps The two things to do: connect the cable, and set the CH3 and CH4 input switches to USB. State The state's title and what happens next. RESCAN Checks for the cable now. TWO DECKS Goes back to the two-deck view. Decks 3 and 4 keep trying in the background. Deck 3 tag NOT CONNECTED while deck 3 is not running. Deck 3 channel The bottom channel of deck 3 waits for the loopback cable. DECKS button Shows the current view. The small amber dot means decks 3 and 4 are not connected. You can drive the card with the encoder. While the card shows, push the encoder to highlight RESCAN , turn it to move between the card's buttons and the DECKS button, and push again to press. BACK , or six seconds without input, gives the encoder back to the player. Card title What it means What to do NO CABLE FOUND The XZ does not see the loopback cable. Connect the cable directly to either top port. Music goes in the other port and is optional for startup. Press RESCAN to check at once. LOOKING FOR THE CABLE... A check runs now. The button reads SCANNING . Wait a moment. STARTING DECKS 3 AND 4 The cable is found and the audio input is starting. Wait a few seconds. The card's sentence says which step is running. STOP DECKS 1 AND 2 Decks 3 and 4 or a newly connected music hub wait for decks 1 and 2 to stop. Stop or pause decks 1 and 2. The card changes by itself. COULD NOT START DECKS 3 AND 4 The start failed. The picture marks the type of connection that needs attention: top USB, cable, rear socket or CH3/CH4 switches. The drawn port is an example. Read the sentence, fix that part, then press TRY AGAIN . DECKS 3 AND 4 DISCONNECTED The cable was unplugged or lost power while decks 3 and 4 ran. Plug the cable back into the same top port and press RESCAN . FOUR DECKS ARE NOT AVAILABLE The software players are not running in this build. Decks 1 and 2 play as usual. Press TWO DECKS . DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY The route came up. The card turns green, then wipes away. Press SHIFT twice on a side to play deck 3 or 4. LOOKING FOR THE CABLE. A check is running, so the button reads SCANNING STARTING DECKS 3 AND 4. The cable is found and the audio input is starting STOP DECKS 1 AND 2, in mixer order. The card splits into two strips COULD NOT START. The failed part is marked in red and the button reads TRY AGAIN DECKS 3 AND 4 DISCONNECTED. The cable went away while decks 3 and 4 ran FOUR DECKS ARE NOT AVAILABLE. Only TWO DECKS is offered NO CABLE FOUND in mixer order The encoder on the card. RESCAN is highlighted DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY. The card turns green The card wipes away and decks 3 and 4 appear When the route comes up, a banner says DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY for a few seconds. If the play screen shows two decks at that moment, the banner says DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY. TAP DECKS AT THE TOP FOR FOUR DECKS. The view does not change by itself.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"the-loopback-cable-connected-card","t":"The LOOPBACK CABLE CONNECTED card","x":"With the loopback cable in, CLASSIC shows a LOOPBACK CABLE CONNECTED card, and decks 3 and 4 work as described here. MODERN and MODS keep working as usual. The LOOPBACK CABLE CONNECTED card in CLASSIC The same card in a larger window When you connect a music hub with the loopback cable in, stop or pause decks 1 and 2 and let the hub finish connecting. A hub in the loopback port, a second hub behind the first, or a hub that does not support high-speed USB 2.0 does not work. Remove that hub or connect the music stick directly.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"deck-view","t":"DECK VIEW","x":"DECK VIEW chooses what the play screen shows. It changes neither the sound, the mixer channels, nor which deck a side controls. Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Tap DECKS Press BACK DECK VIEW Waveform lanes, top to bottom Bottom channels 2 DECKS (the default) The two decks the sides control The same two decks 4 DECKS, number order 1 2 3 4 1, 2, 3, 4 3, 1, 2, 4 4 DECKS, mixer order 3 1 2 4 3, 1, 2, 4 3, 1, 2, 4 The bottom channels always follow the mixer, left to right: CH3, CH1, CH2, CH4. Mixer order puts the lanes in the same order, top to bottom. Each lane and each channel carries its deck's number in a badge, so you can always tell which deck is which. Decks 1 and 2 have a white number on grey. Decks 3 and 4 have a black number on white, as on the jog displays. DECK VIEW is saved to the USB with your other settings. You can change it in five places, and they all change the same setting: the DECKS button at the top of the play screen; TWO DECKS on the card; MODS > SCREEN > DECK VIEW ; MODS > 4 DECKS > DECK VIEW ; the button above LINK , when you set it to DECK VIEW in MODS > PLAY > BUTTON ABOVE LINK . Each press then steps 2 DECKS, 4 DECKS in number order, 4 DECKS in mixer order.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"the-decks-button-and-its-picker","t":"The DECKS button and its picker","x":"The DECKS button is always at the top of the play screen in both interfaces. It names the decks on screen: DECKS 1 2 , DECKS 1234 , DECKS 3124 , or the pair the sides control in 2 DECKS, such as DECKS 3 2 . In MODERN it sits left of the INFO button. In CLASSIC it sits in the black space between VJ.TOOLS and the METRICS readout. Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Tap DECKS to open the picker. Tap a picture to choose it. DECKS button Opens and closes the picker. It shows the view now on screen. 2 DECKS The two decks the sides control, like the player itself. 4 DECKS, number order All four decks, lanes 1 2 3 4. 4 DECKS, mixer order All four decks, lanes 3 1 2 4, matching the mixer channels. Status LIKE THE PLAYER ITSELF for two decks. DECKS 3 AND 4 READY in green, or 3 AND 4 NOT CONNECTED in amber. A tap outside the picker, BACK , or six seconds without input closes it. The encoder also turns and pushes inside the open picker. 2 DECKS. The player's own two-deck screen with the DECKS button at the top 4 DECKS in number order with decks 3 and 4 ready 4 DECKS in mixer order. Lanes 3 1 2 4 over channels 3 1 2 4 2 DECKS with the left side on deck 3. The screen shows decks 3 and 2 2 DECKS when decks 3 and 4 come up. The banner says how to show four","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"switch-a-side-between-decks","t":"Switch a side between decks","x":"The left controls play DECK 1 or DECK 3. The right controls play DECK 2 or DECK 4. Decks 3 and 4 must be ready. Press SHIFT on the left deck twice quickly Press SHIFT on the right deck twice quickly Press SHIFT twice quickly on a side to switch it. The left SHIFT switches between decks 1 and 3, the right SHIFT between decks 2 and 4. These are the presses the XDJ-XZ uses for DJ software. Or press SHORTCUT and tap the deck under DECK SELECT modern . After a switch the tempo fader does not jump. The deck you switched to keeps its tempo until you move the fader across that deck's value. The same holds when you switch back. In 2 DECKS the screen follows the sides. A side on deck 3 or 4 shows that deck's waveform, tag and channel, and the screen says where the side went for two seconds, for example LEFT: DECK 3 . In a four-deck view the lanes stay where they are, and a pale blue tag marks the decks the sides control. If decks 3 and 4 are not running, SHIFT pressed twice does not switch. The screen says DECK 3 AND 4 NEED THE CH3/CH4 ROUTE . If the route is lost while a side plays deck 3 or 4, both sides go back to decks 1 and 2 and the screen says DECK 3/4 ROUTE LOST . SHORTCUT with the left side on deck 3. DECK SELECT Each deck row has its switch. Tap 1 or 3 for the left side, 2 or 4 for the right side. CONTROL In the bottom strip, the decks the sides control carry CONTROL with an arrow. SHORTCUT with four decks before the software players report. No DECK SELECT yet DECK SELECT with both sides on decks 1 and 2 DECK SELECT with both sides on decks 3 and 4 The play screen with the left side on deck 3. Its tag and channel read CONTROL","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"the-modern-four-deck-screen","t":"The MODERN four-deck screen","x":"Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Tap LANE 3 Tap the screen Tap LANE 3 Tap STEMS HEADER Tap STEMS HEADER All four decks loaded and playing. DECKS button Shows DECKS 1234 or DECKS 3124. Tap it to change the view. Lane tag The deck's badge, source stick and the key it plays in now, in the key match colours. VINYL Whether VINYL is on for deck 3 or 4. Bottom channels The four decks in mixer order 3 1 2 4: time, tempo, range, BPM, hot cues and the whole-track overview. MASTER The tempo master. A software master reads 3/4 MASTER. SYNC What SYNC is doing. SYNC 3 means synced to deck 3, BPM 3 deck 3's tempo only, LIMIT a tempo out of reach. See SYNC on decks 3 and 4 . Tap a lane of deck 3 or 4 to open its detail panel. It shows the full pad bank, the deck's modes, what SYNC is doing and a whole-track overview you can touch to search. Tap the lane again, or CLOSE , to close it. Deck 3 is the deck the encoder and screen act on Decks 3 and 4 with no track loaded Deck 4 is the tempo master and plays a loop A software deck as master. Deck 3 reads 3/4 MASTER and deck 4 reads SYNC 3 SYNC states. Deck 3 reads BPM 1 and follows deck 1's tempo only. Deck 4 reads SYNC 3 and follows deck 3 Mixer order 3 1 2 4 ON AIR marks and NEEDLE LOCK, with the playhead on the left Long titles are cut short to fit A read error on deck 3. CANNOT READ THE TRACK, with CHOOSE TRACK GRID ADJUST on deck 4 GRID ADJUST on deck 4 with stem rows on decks 1 and 2 Stem buttons show in a half row under a deck's waveform, only for decks 1 and 2 and only while the deck's track has prepared stems. Decks 3 and 4 have no stems. A deck without stems shows no stem buttons and its waveform keeps the whole lane. STEMS in the top bar shows or hides the stem buttons on all four lanes: one tap hides them, the next shows them. The screen says STEM BUTTONS HIDDEN or STEM BUTTONS SHOWN , and STEMS is lit while they show. Your 2 DECKS stem layout does not apply here and does not change. See Stems . Stem buttons on decks 1 and 2. STEMS is lit One tap of STEMS: the stem buttons are hidden and every waveform has its whole lane Deck 2's track has no prepared stems: no stem buttons, the whole lane BYPASS on deck 2","i":"modern"},{"c":"four-decks","a":"the-classic-four-deck-screen","t":"The CLASSIC four-deck screen","x":"CLASSIC keeps the player's own look and adds what four decks need. Tap the screen Tap the screen Tap the screen Tap the screen Tap the screen Waveforms. The waveform area holds four narrower lanes, one per deck, in the order DECK VIEW chooses. Decks 3 and 4 draw the same 3-band waveform with beat ticks, hot cue flags A to H, the cue point, loops and the playhead. Side column. The left column has one tag per lane. The tag of a deck a side controls is pale blue with LEFT or RIGHT. Decks 1 and 2 show the analysed key, the playing key and its cents. Decks 3 and 4 show their playing key and its cents the same way, TRACK KEY until they report it, or NOT CONNECTED and SEE THE CARD while they are not running. Bottom panel. Four channels in mixer order 3 1 2 4. Each shows the deck's title, time, QUANTIZE, tempo and range, AUTO CUE and MT, what SYNC follows, what the pads do, the BPM (orange with MASTER for the master deck) and the whole-track overview. A deck that is not connected shows a dim band with NOT CONNECTED and DECK n WAITS FOR THE LOOPBACK CABLE. Stem rows are not drawn while four decks show, because there is no room, and STEMS stays dark. Your stem layout comes back when you return to two decks. Pressing STEMS meanwhile changes nothing and says STEM BUTTONS SHOW IN 2 DECKS VIEW . 2 DECKS shows the decks the sides control. A side on deck 3 or 4 gets a whole half: its waveform, its side tag and its bottom panel. Tap a lane, side tag or channel title of deck 3 or 4 to open its detail panel. Touch the overview in the bottom channel to search the track. NEEDLE LOCK refuses a search while the deck plays.","i":"classic"},{"c":"four-decks","a":"load-tracks-onto-decks-3-and-4","t":"Load tracks onto decks 3 and 4","x":"LOAD on a side loads the highlighted track into the deck that side controls, deck 3 or deck 4 included. In CLASSIC this goes through the player's own browser. In MODERN, tap a track to see a LOAD chip with one cell per deck, then tap the deck number. See Browsing and loading for the rest. Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Press BROWSE Push ROTARY SELECTOR Tap TRACK ROW Tap LOAD DECK 3 A tapped track with its LOAD cells. LOAD Tap a deck number to load the track there. LOAD returns to the play screen. Target deck The blue cell is the deck the screen acts on now. Bottom strip The four decks in mixer order while you browse. Browsing with four decks. The bottom strip shows all four decks Browsing while the sides control decks 3 and 2 Deck 4 with no track. Not Loaded in the strip The play screen after a load After LOAD on the left side. The track went to the left side's deck After LOAD on the right side. The track went to the right side's deck Decks 3 and 4 cannot load a track at a memory point from the CUE/LOOP LIST. The screen says DECK 3 AND 4 CANNOT LOAD AT A MEMORY POINT .","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"info-source-and-utility-with-four-decks","t":"INFO, SOURCE and UTILITY with four decks","x":"INFO has a tab for each deck. SOURCE shows which decks use each stick. UTILITY and the other full screens keep a compact strip of all four decks at the bottom. Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Press INFO Tap the screen Tap the screen Press BACK Open SOURCE ( BACK at the top of a list) Press BACK Hold MENU for a second Press BACK INFO with tabs DECK 1 to DECK 4 SOURCE. Decks 1 and 2 on USB 1, decks 3 and 4 on USB 2 UTILITY with the four-deck strip at the bottom INFO tabs named PLAYER 3 and PLAYER 4 are other players on the LINK network, not decks 3 and 4 A LINK player with no track loaded","i":"modern"},{"c":"four-decks","a":"what-decks-3-and-4-can-do","t":"What decks 3 and 4 can do","x":"Decks 3 and 4 are software players. They follow the player's own controls on the side that controls them. MODS > 4 DECKS shows the current answer for each feature. Tap DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Press PLAY/PAUSE on the left deck Press CUE on the left deck Press PLAY/PAUSE on the left deck Press SYNC on the left deck Press DECK QUANTIZE on the left deck Press SYNC on the left deck Press MASTER on the left deck Press SYNC on the left deck Press PLAY/PAUSE on the left deck Press IN/CUE on the left deck Press OUT on the left deck Press RELOOP/EXIT on the left deck Feature Decks 1 and 2 Decks 3 and 4 Beat jump pads with your own sizes Yes Yes, the same sizes and both pages Gate cue and smart cue Yes Yes Waveform colours, key notation, titles Yes Yes Playing key Yes Yes Key sync and key shift Yes Yes. Both can shift together; new shifts check measured audio headroom. Stems Yes, with USB stems set up No. Decks 3 and 4 have no stems. RAM tracks Yes Yes, while the loopback cable is connected. See RAM tracks . On a side that controls deck 3 or 4, these controls work on that deck experimental : Control What it does on deck 3 or 4 PLAY/PAUSE , CUE Play and pause, back cue and cue audition. With VINYL on, pause brakes to a stop at the VINYL SPEED ADJUST rate. HOT CUE , BEAT LOOP , SLIP LOOP , BEAT JUMP Set the pad mode of deck 3 or 4. Deck 1 or 2 on that side keeps its own mode. Pads Hot cues, beat loops, slip loops and beat jumps, as on decks 1 and 2. IN/CUE , OUT , RELOOP/EXIT Manual loops, loop adjustment with the jog, reloop and exit. SLIP , DIRECTION REV , VINYL Slip, reverse and vinyl mode. TEMPO RANGE , TEMPO RESET , MASTER TEMPO Tempo range up to WIDE, original speed, and key lock while the tempo moves. SYNC , MASTER Follow the master deck's tempo, and with QUANTIZE its beat. Make this deck the master. See SYNC on decks 3 and 4 . SHIFT + SYNC , MASTER TEMPO KEY SYNC to the master deck, and back to the deck's own key. See Keys and KEY SYNC . DECK QUANTIZE Cue, loop and hot cue points land on the beat. DECK QUANTIZE switches every deck. SHIFT + DECK QUANTIZE switches only this side's deck. MEMORY , DELETE , CUE/LOOP CALL Store, delete and call memory points. TRACK SEARCH , SEARCH Previous and next track, and fine search. With AUTO CUE on, the new track waits at its cue. Previous and next follow the list the track was loaded from in MODERN. After a CLASSIC load the deck shows NO SAVED TRACK ORDER, and TRACK SEARCH back returns to the cue. On decks 3 and 4, TRACK SEARCH respects AUTO CUE. With AUTO CUE on, a newly loaded track waits at its cue point. With AUTO CUE off, a deck that was playing continues with the new track; a paused deck stays paused. Hot cues and memory points you set on decks 3 and 4 are saved on the music stick for those decks only. Decks 1 and 2 and your DJ software do not see them, and the exported library stays unchanged.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"sync-on-decks-3-and-4","t":"SYNC on decks 3 and 4","x":"Press SYNC and the deck takes the master deck's BPM at once. The SYNC button stays lit for as long as SYNC is on. With QUANTIZE on and a beat grid on both tracks, the deck also locks to the master's beat. Press SYNC again to turn it off. Master Deck 1 is the tempo master. Deck 3 plays at its own tempo, with SYNC off. SYNC Press SYNC on deck 3. It takes the master's BPM at once and reads SYNC 1. With QUANTIZE on and a beat grid on both tracks, it also locks to the master's beat. Tempo only With QUANTIZE off, only the tempo follows, and deck 3 reads BPM 1. If the beats drift apart, press SYNC off and on again. With QUANTIZE on, every engage snaps to the nearest position at the selected beat value, even for a small drift. The beat value can be 1, 1/2, 1/4 or 1/8 beat. With QUANTIZE off, only the tempo follows. The tempo follows even when the master or the synced deck is paused. If the beat position is available, the paused deck aligns once. If it is unavailable, alignment happens as soon as it can be read. Continuous beat lock resumes when both decks play. A pause, a jump, a loop or a new master never turns SYNC off. The deck follows again on its own, with no second press. Nudge the jog from the side to move the deck a little off the master's beat. SYNC stays on and the tempo stays matched. The deck keeps the new alignment, also when the master's tempo changes, and the SYNC button flashes. Nudge the master's jog from the side to move only the master. It stays master, and the synced decks keep their tempo and the new alignment. To line the beats up again, press SYNC off and on. The deck snaps to the nearest beat and the button lights steadily. Scratching on the platter top takes control of the deck. When you let go, QUANTIZE snaps it back to the beat. Press SYNC off and the deck keeps its position and the synced tempo. The tempo fader takes over once you move it to that tempo. The tempo fader does not move the deck while SYNC is on. The bottom channel, the lane and the detail panel say what SYNC is doing: Shown What it means SYNC 1 to SYNC 4 SYNC is on and follows that deck. BPM 1 to BPM 4 Only the tempo can follow that deck: QUANTIZE is off, a track has no beat grid, a loop is running, or the master's beat position is not available. MASTER This deck is the tempo master. 3/4 MASTER This deck is the master for decks 3 and 4 only. LIMIT The master's tempo is out of this deck's reach. The deck keeps its last tempo. EXT MASTER The master is another player on the LINK network, which decks 3 and 4 cannot follow. NO BPM The track has no BPM to sync with. Analyse it in your DJ software. The detail panel adds a line about the reason, for example: Detail panel What it means SYNC ON / FOLLOWING DECK 1 The deck follows deck 1. SYNC ON / TEMPO MATCHED, PAUSED / TEMPO MATCHED The tempo matches. The beat locks once both decks play. BPM SYNC / MASTER PAUSED, BPM SYNC / DECK PAUSED One of the two decks is paused. The tempo follows, and the beat locks once both play. BPM SYNC / NO BEAT GRID A track has no beat grid, so only the tempo follows. BPM SYNC / LOOP ACTIVE A loop is running, so only the tempo follows until it ends. BPM SYNC / BEAT POSITION UNAVAILABLE The master's beat position cannot be read, so only the tempo follows. BPM SYNC / QUANTIZE OFF QUANTIZE is off, so only the tempo follows. SYNC ON / JOG CONTROL You are nudging or scratching. SYNC picks up again when you let go. After a side nudge it keeps the new alignment. NO MASTER / TEMPO UNCHANGED No deck is master. The deck keeps its tempo and follows as soon as there is one. MASTER CLOCK UNAVAILABLE / LAST TEMPO RETAINED The master's tempo cannot be read right now. The deck keeps the last tempo. SYNC TEMPO LIMIT / LAST TEMPO RETAINED The master's tempo is out of reach. EXTERNAL MASTER / SYNC SOURCE UNAVAILABLE A LINK player is master. TRACK BPM UNAVAILABLE / SYNC ON The track has no BPM.","i":""},{"c":"four-decks","a":"limits","t":"Limits","x":"Decks 1 and 2 must be stopped or paused while decks 3 and 4 start. Keep the music stick connected while you play. Decks 3 and 4 read from it all the time. Decks 3 and 4 play WAV, AIFF, FLAC, MP3 and Ogg Vorbis files. AAC and M4A files do not play on decks 3 and 4. A deck 3 or 4 master reads MASTER when decks 1 and 2 can follow it too, and 3/4 MASTER when it drives decks 3 and 4 only. Press MASTER on a playing deck 3 or 4 and it is master at once. The MASTER buttons show the change. When you pause the master, MASTER passes at once to the next playing deck. A deck with SYNC on comes first. Otherwise after deck 3 comes deck 4, then decks 1 and 2. After deck 4 come decks 1 and 2, then deck 3. In VINYL mode MASTER passes when you press pause, while the deck slows down. When you pause a deck 1 or 2 master, a playing deck 3 or 4 takes MASTER at once. If the other of decks 1 and 2 is playing, MASTER goes to that deck instead, as with two decks. In VINYL mode, hold the master's platter top and MASTER passes to the other synced, playing deck after a moment. Load a new track on the master and MASTER passes to the other playing deck. The loading deck keeps SYNC on and plays its new track at the tempo the decks shared. A handover never changes the tempo. A master set by another player over LINK is never taken. Some lamps on the player do not yet light as they do for decks 1 and 2. The beat loop and slip loop pad colours are provisional. Four decks, the handover of MASTER between decks 1 and 2 and decks 3 and 4, and scratching on decks 3 and 4 are experimental in this version. If something goes wrong, the card or the 4 DECKS page names the state. Messages and troubleshooting lists every notice.","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"","t":"The MODS menu","x":"MODS is the menu XZ Mods adds to the player. Everything the mod can change lives here, sorted by what you want to do. Both interfaces open the same menu, so what you learn here works in MODERN and CLASSIC. In MODERN, MODS uses the MODERN look. In CLASSIC, it uses the theme you chose.","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"open-and-close-mods","t":"Open and close MODS","x":"Press MENU on the play screen. A short press opens MODS wherever MENU has no other job, and leaves its normal job alone everywhere else. Hold MENU to open the player's own UTILITY, as without XZ Mods. Press MENU Press MENU Press MENU Tap CLOSE Where you are Short press of MENU The MODS menu is open Closes MODS A game is on screen The game's own key The VJ.Tools view is on screen As before A menu, popup or dialog is open Works or closes the open menu A track list (browse, playlist, search, history) The sort menu or the track menu TAG LIST LIST MENU The play screen in GRID ADJUST The beat grid menu The play screen Opens MODS experimental The SOURCE screen Opens MODS experimental The track INFO screen Opens MODS experimental The SHORTCUT screen Opens MODS experimental The player's own UTILITY Closes UTILITY Any other screen The screen's own job Note Rows marked experimental follow the XDJ-XZ operating instructions but have not been checked on every firmware version yet. If a press does something different on your player, report it github.com/OpticMystic/XZ-Mods/issues . To leave MODS, press MENU again, tap CLOSE in the top right corner, or press BACK until you are back on the play screen. You can also open MODS from the MODS button at the top of the MODERN play screen, or from the button above LINK when you set it to MODS MENU in PLAY .","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"move-around","t":"Move around","x":"You can drive the whole menu with the rotary encoder, with touch, or with both. Press MENU Push ROTARY SELECTOR to choose PLAY Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to GATE CUE and push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to SMART CUE and push it Press BACK Control What it does in MODS Turn the encoder Moves the highlight to the next card, row or button Push the encoder Opens or changes the highlighted item BACK Goes up one level: from an open item to its page, then from a page to the section rail Tap Opens or changes whatever you tap The hints in the bottom right corner ( TURN MOVE · PUSH SELECT · BACK UP ) always show what the encoder and BACK will do next. Every page has the same frame. The section rail on the left lists HOME, PLAY, STEMS, SCREEN, 4 DECKS, CONNECT and EXTRAS. The dock along the bottom explains whatever is highlighted. On the right of the dock, WORKS ON shows which decks the highlighted feature works on, in mixer order 3 1 2 4. A dimmed number means the feature does not work on that deck, and a short amber line says why.","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"home","t":"HOME","x":"HOME is the first page. It shows one card for each section, with a one-line summary of what the section does and the current state of its most important setting, so you can see at a glance whether stems are ready or four decks are connected. Press MENU Tap HOME Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press BACK The HOME page with stems ready and four decks not connected yet. BACK Goes up one level. On HOME it closes MODS. Section rail Every section of MODS, top to bottom. Tap one, or turn the encoder while the rail is highlighted. Section card Opens that section. The highlighted card has a light outline. Status line The state of the section's main setting. Green means ready, amber means it needs you. Setup button Appears when a feature needs setting up, and starts a short guide for it. Dock Explains the highlighted item in plain words before you open it. Save state Confirms your changes are saved to the USB, or says why they cannot be. Encoder hints What turning, pushing and BACK will do right now. CLOSE Closes MODS and returns to where you were. Card Its status line shows PLAY Your beat jump sizes, page 1 then page 2 STEMS Not set up, Off, or On with the state of deck 1 and deck 2 SCREEN The interface, the waveform colours and the key notation 4 DECKS Not connected, Looking for the cable, Starting decks 3 and 4, Ready with the deck view, Could not start, Disconnected, or Not available on this player CONNECT Your DJ profile and its USB, and whether VJ.Tools is connected EXTRAS The games and how many USB apps are on the stick Two setup buttons can appear on HOME. SET UP USB STEMS opens the USB stems guide when the stem engine is not ready. SET UP FOUR DECKS opens 4 DECKS when no cable is found, a start failed, the cable was lost, or the USB loader has no four-deck engine.","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"play","t":"PLAY","x":"PLAY changes what the pads and buttons do while you perform. Press MENU Tap PLAY Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press BACK BEAT JUMP PADS Your own beat jump distances for both pad pages. The row shows the sizes now in use. GATE CUE and SMART CUE Switch each cue trick on or off. A feature the player has not reported yet shows a SET UP button instead. KEYS and RAM TRACKS Open their own pages. BUTTON ABOVE LINK What the button above LINK does on a press, and with SHIFT. WORKS ON The decks the highlighted feature works on. Beat jump and performance features explains every item on this page.","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"stems","t":"STEMS","x":"STEMS mutes vocals, harmonics and drums from the pads or the screen. Press MENU Tap STEMS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press BACK USB STEMS Switches stems from the USB on or off. Reads SET UP USB STEMS until the stem engine is ready. STEM PADS Which pad mode and pad bank the stems use. Stem buttons on screen Where the stem buttons sit on the play screen. Each picture is one layout. STEM COLOURS The colours of drums, harmonics and vocals. WORKS ON Only decks 1 and 2 are lit. The amber line under it says decks 3 and 4 have no stems. STEMS IN DJ SOFTWARE sets up stems for a computer playing through the player. MODERN adds a BYPASS BUTTON switch beside STEM COLOURS. Stems explains every item on this page.","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"screen","t":"SCREEN","x":"SCREEN sets how the play screen looks. Press MENU Tap SCREEN Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press BACK INTERFACE CLASSIC or MODERN. The picture shows each one. DECK VIEW 2 DECKS, 4 DECKS in number order, or 4 DECKS in mixer order. THEME The CLASSIC theme. In MODERN this place holds LAMPS AND TITLES instead. 3-BAND COLOURS A colour for the lows, mids and highs of the 3-BAND waveform. The squares show the colours in use. WAVEFORM COLOURS STOCK, 3-BAND or STEMS. MODERN adds RGB. KEY NOTATION AS ON THE USB, MUSICAL or WHEEL, each with an example key. Keys and the track list PLAYING KEY, KEY MATCH COLOURS, KEY BEFORE TITLE and TRACK LIST COLUMNS. SYSTEM READOUT CPU, memory and temperature on the top bar, on its own row at the bottom of the page. Screen, interfaces and themes explains every item on this page. DECK VIEW is explained in Four decks .","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"4-decks","t":"4 DECKS","x":"4 DECKS plays decks 3 and 4 over the loopback cable experimental . Press MENU Tap 4 DECKS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press BACK Cable state Where four decks stand, and what happens next. RESCAN Checks the cable now. Reads TRY AGAIN after a failed start. DECK VIEW How many decks the play screen shows, and in what order. What works on each deck A tick for every deck a feature works on. Four decks explains the cable, every state and what decks 3 and 4 can do.","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"connect","t":"CONNECT","x":"CONNECT links the player to you and to computers. Press MENU Tap CONNECT Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press BACK DJ PROFILE Your DJ name and logo from the USB, for VJ screens. VJ.TOOLS Lets VJ.Tools on a computer connect, and shows its picture instead of the play screen. NETWORK The network adapter and address, applied for this start of the player. UPDATES Signed updates over the network. An update becomes active at the next start. Connect and DJ profiles explains every page here.","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"extras","t":"EXTRAS","x":"Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press BACK GAMES Doom, Chex Quest, Beat Arcade, Wave Rider, Rhythm Lab and Static Surfer. The music keeps playing. USB APPS Apps for the XZ from the USB. REPORT AN ISSUE Sends a problem, a question or an idea, in three presses. ABOUT XZ MODS Credits, links and support. Extras explains every page here.","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"utility-the-player-s-own-settings","t":"UTILITY, the player's own settings","x":"MENU held opens the player's own UTILITY: quantize, auto cue, play mode, the display and the player's other settings. Hold MENU for a second Push ROTARY SELECTOR Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Press BACK In CLASSIC you see the player's own UTILITY screen, unchanged. In MODERN, UTILITY shows the player's settings in the MODERN colours. In MODERN, MODS also has a UTILITY cell at the bottom of the section rail. It closes MODS and opens UTILITY. Until MODERN has read the player's settings, it reads NOT READY.","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"modern-utility","t":"MODERN UTILITY","x":"Press SHORTCUT Tap the screen Tap the screen UTILITY in MODERN, open on its first setting. UTILITY STOCK The player's own settings. On the player, the rail lists the MODS sections below it, and each one opens MODS on that section. Group DJ SETTING, DISPLAY (LCD), MIXER, SYSTEM and INFO, as on the player. Lock XZ Mods shows this setting but cannot change it here. The help says why. Current value A locked setting shows its value without choice buttons. Writable settings open a list of choices. Help What the setting does and why it is read-only here, or what a writable choice means. Version The player's firmware version. Deck strip Decks 1 and 2 stay in view while you change settings. Turn the encoder to move through the settings. On a writable row, push to open its choices, turn to pick one and push to set it. A locked row stays in the list and shows a read-only value and explanation. BACK goes back to the list. MENU or X closes UTILITY. A lock next to a setting comes with one of these notes: Note What it means PLAYER CONTROLLED The player sets this itself. XZ Mods only shows it. FIRMWARE LIMIT XZ Mods cannot read or set it on this firmware version. READ-ONLY BUILD This start of XZ Mods shows settings but changes none. Start from the USB loader to change them. READ ONLY HERE XZ Mods shows this setting but cannot change it here. Pushing a locked setting does nothing. A setting highlighted in the list The choices open. Turn and push to set one A setting XZ Mods can change, its choices open A locked setting further down. Its help says it is read only here The end of the list. MIXER, SYSTEM and VERSION No. Before the version is read. TIME MODE first, then the display settings UTILITY on its DJ SETTING and DISPLAY (LCD) groups Before the decks report. The deck strip shows dashes SETTINGS NOT AVAILABLE HERE when the settings cannot be read UTILITY with four decks. A compact strip of all four decks","i":"modern"},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"my-settings","t":"MY SETTINGS","x":"MY SETTINGS shows the player settings saved on a USB stick, and the DJ profiles on it. In MODERN, open the stick in browse, highlight the category rail on the left, and press MENU . Press BROWSE Press MENU Tap the screen Tap the screen Tap the screen Tap the screen MY SETTINGS for USB 1 while deck 1 plays. MY SETTINGS The panel for the stick you browse. X closes it. Stick The stick whose settings these are: USB 1, USB 2, or a LINK player's USB. LOAD TO DECK Applies the settings saved on the stick to the active deck. Reads PAUSE DECK 1 TO LOAD while that deck plays. SAVE TO USB 1 Saves the player's current settings to the stick, replacing the ones there. Push once to arm it, then again to save. DJ PROFILE The DJ profiles on the stick. Push one to make it active and apply its settings and look. ACTIVE marks the one in use. DAMAGED A profile whose files cannot be read. SAVE SETTINGS TO Saves the current settings into the active DJ's profile. Push twice. Help What the highlighted row does. Further down, WAVEFORM sets COLOR, POSITION, ZOOM, USB COLORS and the stem row layout. SAVED ON USB 1 lists the settings stored on the stick, which you can change there. PUSH AGAIN TO SAVE. The save is armed The DJ PROFILE rows The WAVEFORM rows SAVED ON USB 1. The settings on the stick, with help for the highlighted one A locked stick with nothing saved. Only the WAVEFORM rows remain A LINK player's USB while deck 1 plays After a load. How many settings applied and how many do not exist on this deck","i":"modern"},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"saving-to-the-usb","t":"Saving to the USB","x":"There is no save button in MODS. Every change saves on its own to the settings USB, the stick you browse. The settings live in the VJ.Tools folder on that stick, so they travel with you to another XZ running XZ Mods. When you browse a stick, the player takes that stick's settings. A stick with no settings, or with damaged ones, leaves the current settings as they are. Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap CLASSIC Tap MODERN Press MENU The XZ also remembers the last settings it applied. If you start it with no stick, it uses them. The save state at the right of the dock says what happened to your last change: Save state What it means SAVING... The change is being written. SAVED TO USB 1 (or USB 2) The change is on the stick. SAVED ON THIS XZ / NO USB No stick is in. The change is kept on this XZ. SAVED ON THIS XZ / USB CHANGED The settings stick changed. The change is kept on this XZ. SAVED ON THIS XZ / USB PROFILE KEPT The stick is locked. The change is kept on this XZ and the stick is left as it was. USB REMOVED: SETTINGS KEPT You pulled the settings stick. Nothing resets. NOT SAVED TO USB 1: CHECK USB Writing failed. Check that the stick is in and not locked. NOT SAVED: USB PROFILE KEPT The stick is locked and the XZ could not keep the change either. NO SETTINGS USB: CHANGES LAST UNTIL POWER OFF. Nothing can be saved. Your change works until you switch the player off. NOT SAVED: CHANGES LAST UNTIL POWER OFF. This build does not save settings. Changes work until you switch the player off. Lines that say NOT SAVED or NO SETTINGS USB show in amber. DJ profiles are not settings. They stay on the DJ's stick and never on the XZ. See Connect and DJ profiles .","i":""},{"c":"mods-menu","a":"older-pages","t":"Older pages","x":"Earlier versions had GENERAL, CONTROLS, THEMES and SETTINGS pages in MODS. They are gone. Anything that pointed at them now opens the page that replaced them: Old page Opens GENERAL HOME CONTROLS STEM PADS, in STEMS THEMES SCREEN SETTINGS PLAY","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"","t":"Screen, interfaces and themes","x":"SCREEN is the MODS section for how the player looks. Here you choose between the MODERN and CLASSIC interfaces, pick a theme, set the waveform colours and the 3-band colours, and decide how keys are written. Nothing on this page changes how a track sounds. Open MODS with MENU , then choose SCREEN in the section rail.","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"the-screen-page","t":"The SCREEN page","x":"Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap 2 DECKS Tap 4 DECKS Tap 4 DECKS Tap STOCK Tap RGB Tap 3-BAND Tap STEMS Tap AS ON THE USB Tap MUSICAL Tap WHEEL Tap PLAYING KEY Tap KEY MATCH COLOURS Tap KEY BEFORE TITLE The SCREEN page with CLASSIC chosen. Under MODERN, the THEME row reads LAMPS AND TITLES, 3-BAND COLOURS sits beside it, and WAVEFORM COLOURS offers four choices. INTERFACE MODERN or CLASSIC. The framed picture is the one in use. DECK VIEW How many decks the play screen shows and in what order. See Four decks . THEME Opens CLASSIC THEMES. The value is the theme in use. Under MODERN this row is LAMPS AND TITLES. 3-BAND COLOURS Opens the 3-BAND COLOURS page. The three squares are the colours of the lows, mids and highs now. WAVEFORM COLOURS How the scrolling waveforms are coloured. KEY NOTATION How keys are written everywhere MODS draws them. PLAYING KEY Shows the key a track plays in after tempo and key shift. KEY MATCH COLOURS Colours keys by how well they mix with the master deck. KEY BEFORE TITLE Shows the key in front of each title in the track list. TRACK LIST COLUMNS Tells you where to change the columns of the track list. SYSTEM READOUT CPU, memory and temperature on the top bar. Reads SET UP until you have run its setup. WORKS ON The decks the highlighted control applies to, in mixer order 3 1 2 4. Control Choices What it changes INTERFACE CLASSIC, MODERN Who draws the play screen. See MODERN and CLASSIC DECK VIEW 2 DECKS, 4 DECKS in number order, 4 DECKS in mixer order Which decks the play screen shows. Sound and controls do not change. Hidden on a player that cannot run decks 3 and 4 THEME (CLASSIC) 24 classic themes The look of the player's own screen and of MODS LAMPS AND TITLES (MODERN) A page of switches Which parts of the MODERN play screen you see 3-BAND COLOURS A page of colours The colours of the lows, mids and highs in every 3-BAND waveform. See 3-band colours WAVEFORM COLOURS STOCK, 3-BAND, STEMS (MODERN adds RGB) The colours of the scrolling waveforms KEY NOTATION AS ON THE USB, MUSICAL, WHEEL How keys are written PLAYING KEY ON, OFF The key a track plays in now, or its original key KEY MATCH COLOURS ON, OFF Green or amber keys on the play screen and in the track list KEY BEFORE TITLE ON, OFF The key in front of each title in the track list TRACK LIST COLUMNS Information only Tap a column title in the track list, or press MENU there, to choose its columns and sort SYSTEM READOUT Opens its setup CPU, RAM and temperature on the top bar. It has the last row of the page to itself The HOME card for SCREEN sums the page up in one line, for example Classic | 3-band | Am keys .","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"modern-and-classic","t":"MODERN and CLASSIC","x":"XZ Mods gives the player two interfaces. You choose one with INTERFACE on the SCREEN page, or when you prepare the USB in the XZ Mods app. MODERN is the default. Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap CLASSIC Tap MODERN Press the button above LINK Press the button above LINK MODERN is a full-screen layout drawn by XZ Mods, with bigger waveforms and a browse sidebar. CLASSIC keeps the familiar play screen and adds MODS to it, in the classic theme you choose. MODERN CLASSIC Play screen Drawn by XZ Mods, full screen The familiar layout, in your theme Themes One look, STANDARD. MODS uses the MODERN look 24 themes. MODS uses the theme you pick Waveform colours STOCK, RGB, 3-BAND, STEMS STOCK, 3-BAND, STEMS Lamps and titles Each part can be shown or hidden Not available Playing key Shown as the big key in each deck's column Shown where the beat countdown sits Stem buttons Six places, including small buttons beside the hot cues Five places Browse The XZ Mods browser with a sidebar. See Browsing and loading The player's own browser Each interface keeps its own theme. If you switch from CLASSIC to MODERN and back, your classic theme comes back with you. To switch without opening MODS, press the button above LINK . Out of the box it switches between MODERN and CLASSIC. You can give it another job in PLAY › BUTTON ABOVE LINK . See Controls on the player . The MODERN play screen with two decks, 3-BAND waveforms and the playing key shown. Mode lamps SINGLE or CONTINUE, A. HOT CUE and A. CUE. Hide them in LAMPS AND TITLES. QUANTIZE lamp Red while QUANTIZE is on, with its beat value. Hide it in LAMPS AND TITLES. Playing key The key the track plays in now. ORIGINAL below it is the key it was analysed in. Scrolling waveform Coloured by WAVEFORM COLOURS. STEMS and MODS STEMS steps the stem buttons through their places, or shows and hides them in 4 DECKS. MODS opens the MODS menu.","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"classic-themes","t":"Classic themes","x":"A classic theme restyles the player's own play screen and the MODS menu: artwork, text, waveforms, cue marks and dialogs. Track positions, numbers and touch areas stay where the player puts them, so a theme never moves a control under your finger. Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap CLASSIC Tap THEME Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise, then push it Choose THEME on the SCREEN page to open CLASSIC THEMES . Tap a theme, or turn the encoder to it and push. Close MODS to see the play screen in the new theme. Every classic theme on one page. ORIGINAL is in use. Theme in use Framed, with SELECTED under its name. Colour dots The theme's main colours, so you can compare themes before you pick one. Dock Says what a theme restyles before you choose it. WORKS ON Themes apply to decks 1 to 4. The gallery shows the HOME page of MODS in every theme. Original White Cyberpunk Neon Mocha Aurora Sandstone Game Boy Super Nintendo Windows 95 Game Boy Color Aqua / Itunes Game Boy Dark Super Nintendo Dark Windows 95 Dark Game Boy Color Dark Aqua / Itunes Dark Game Boy Dmg Game Boy Dmg Dark Liquid Glass Liquid Glass Dark Lcars Matrix Analog Modern","i":"classic"},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"theme-families","t":"Theme families","x":"Tap the screen Tap the screen Family Themes What to expect Modern palettes ORIGINAL, WHITE, CYBERPUNK, NEON, MOCHA, AURORA, SANDSTONE Colour schemes on the player's own artwork. ORIGINAL is the player as it ships Game Boy GAME BOY, GAME BOY DARK, GAME BOY COLOR, GAME BOY COLOR DARK, GAME BOY DMG, GAME BOY DMG DARK Handheld palettes, with their own player artwork and title treatment Super Nintendo SUPER NINTENDO, SUPER NINTENDO DARK Console colours with their own player artwork Windows 95 WINDOWS 95, WINDOWS 95 DARK Grey bevelled windows and title bars Aqua AQUA / ITUNES, AQUA / ITUNES DARK Glossy rounded panels Liquid Glass LIQUID GLASS, LIQUID GLASS DARK Translucent rounded panels LCARS LCARS Amber and violet swept panels and capsules. Its own MODS layout with a sidebar Matrix MATRIX A green terminal with inverse selections and pixel lettering Analog ANALOG A brushed metal faceplate with lamp keys and switches. Its needle shows the VJ.Tools frame rate, not audio level Most families come in a light and a DARK version. Pick the dark one for dim booths. Note Themes change the screen only. The pad and button lights on the player keep their own colours.","i":"classic"},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"modern-look","t":"MODERN look","x":"MODERN has one look, STANDARD , so it has no theme list. MODS uses the MODERN look: black pages, a grey section rail and blue selections. More MODERN looks are planned. Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap LAMPS AND TITLES Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise Instead of THEME, the SCREEN page offers LAMPS AND TITLES . Its row shows ALL SHOWN , or how many parts you have hidden. Group Switch or choice Shown Hidden TOP BAR MODE LAMPS The SINGLE / CONTINUE, A. HOT CUE and A. CUE lamps light while their mode is on The lamps leave the screen. The modes keep working TOP BAR QUANTIZE LAMP Each deck's QUANTIZE lamp and beat value above its time The QUANTIZE button's own light still shows it WAVEFORMS TITLES IN WAVEFORMS Track titles inside the waveform lanes The waveforms use that space. Titles at the bottom stay TRACK COLOURS DECK + WAVE The colours set for the USB in your DJ software show on the deck tag and its waveform TRACK COLOURS DECK ONLY Those colours show on the deck tag only TRACK COLOURS OFF USB colours are not shown A hidden lamp also stops answering touch. Your LAMPS AND TITLES choices, TRACK COLOURS and the BYPASS BUTTON switch are saved to the USB with your other settings, so they come back after the player restarts. So are MODERN's waveform colour, its waveform position and zoom, and how it writes keys. Every lamp shown MODE LAMPS and QUANTIZE LAMP hidden TRACK COLOURS DECK + WAVE. Deck 1 comes from a yellow USB set to RGB waveforms, deck 2 from a pink USB TRACK COLOURS DECK ONLY TRACK COLOURS OFF The BYPASS BUTTON switch for MODERN sits with the stem buttons in STEMS . See Stems .","i":"modern"},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"waveform-colours","t":"Waveform colours","x":"WAVEFORM COLOURS sets how the scrolling waveforms are coloured. The setting itself is explained with the rest of the play screen in The play screen . Choice What you see STOCK The player's own waveform colours RGB The full-colour waveform. MODERN only 3-BAND Lows, mids and highs as layers: lows outside, mids around them, highs at the core. Blue, amber and white unless you choose your own 3-band colours STEMS Drums outside, harmonics around them, vocals at the core, in your stem colours The preview strip on the 3-BAND COLOURS page draws the three layers in the colours in use: lows outside, mids around them, highs at the core. 3-BAND and STEMS read the track analysis your DJ software and the XZ Mods stem builder already put on the USB. You do not prepare anything extra. A track without stems shows 3-BAND under STEMS. A track with four stems also shows 3-BAND, because its stems carry no waveform data yet. Stem colours are set in STEMS › STEM COLOURS . See Stems . In MODERN, UTILITY's WAVEFORM COLOR is the same setting. Your choice is saved to the USB and comes back after a restart.","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"3-band-colours","t":"3-band colours","x":"3-BAND COLOURS chooses the colour of each band in the 3-BAND waveform: the lows, the mids and the highs. On the SCREEN page it sits beside THEME in CLASSIC and beside LAMPS AND TITLES in MODERN. Its row shows the three colours in use. Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap 3-BAND COLOURS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise Every band on STANDARD, the interface's own colours. LOWS The colour of the lows, the outer layer of the waveform. MIDS The colour of the mids, the middle layer. HIGHS The colour of the highs, at the core. STANDARD Keeps the interface's own colour for that band. The highlighted choice in each band is the colour in use. Colour choices BLUE, RED, GREEN, AMBER, PURPLE, CYAN, PINK and WHITE. Tap one to give it to that band. Preview A strip drawn the way the 3-BAND waveform stacks the bands, in the colours you chose. RESET 3-BAND COLOURS Puts all three bands back to STANDARD. WORKS ON 3-band colours apply on all four decks. Open MODS > SCREEN > 3-BAND COLOURS . Tap a colour under LOWS , MIDS or HIGHS . Without the touch screen, turn the encoder to a colour and push. Close MODS to see the play screen in the new colours. Band Choices Default LOWS STANDARD, BLUE, RED, GREEN, AMBER, PURPLE, CYAN, PINK, WHITE STANDARD MIDS The same nine STANDARD HIGHS The same nine STANDARD The colours apply to every 3-BAND waveform: the MODERN lanes and overviews, the CLASSIC scrolling waveform, decks 3 and 4, and the browse preview. STANDARD is not one fixed colour. It is the colour the interface itself uses for that band, so MODERN and CLASSIC can differ a little. The 3-BAND pictures under WAVEFORM COLOURS on the SCREEN page are drawn in your colours too. Stem colours are separate. Set them in STEMS › STEM COLOURS . The colours are saved to the USB with your other settings.","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"keys","t":"Keys","x":"","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"key-notation","t":"Key notation","x":"KEY NOTATION sets how keys are written everywhere MODS draws them: on the play screen, in the track list and in MODS. Choice Example When to use it AS ON THE USB as set in your library Keys look the way your DJ software writes them MUSICAL Am You think in note names WHEEL 8A You mix by key wheel numbers MUSICAL. Deck 2 plays Bbm, analysed in Am WHEEL. Deck 2 plays 3A, analysed in 8A","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"playing-key","t":"Playing key","x":"With PLAYING KEY on, each deck shows the key the track plays in now, after tempo changes and key shifts. The original key and the offset in cents sit beside it. In MODERN the playing key is the big key in each deck's column. Off shows the track's original key there. In CLASSIC the playing key sits where the beat countdown is. Off brings the countdown back. Decks 3 and 4 show their playing key too. Until a software deck reports it, the deck shows the track's own key, marked TRACK KEY in CLASSIC. Deck 2 sped up with MT off. It still plays in Am, 38 cents sharp Faster still. Deck 2 now plays in Bbm, and ORIGINAL shows Am The key readout and Key Sync are explained in The play screen and Beat jump and performance features .","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"key-match-colours-and-key-before-title","t":"Key match colours and key before title","x":"KEY MATCH COLOURS colours keys green or amber by how well they mix with the master deck, in the track list and on the play screen. Green means the key mixes with the master's key and sits within 25 cents of it. Amber means it would mix, but it is detuned by more than 25 cents. KEY BEFORE TITLE puts the key in front of each title in the track list. See Browsing and loading .","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"deck-colours","t":"Deck colours","x":"When a screen names a deck, it draws the deck number in a small badge. The badge tells you the deck by its digit and the pair by its colours. Decks Badge 1 and 2 White digit on grey 3 and 4 Black digit on white A deck that is not live The same badge, dimmed No deck owns a colour. Blue and pale blue mark the deck a side of the player controls. Amber, red, green, the waveform bands and USB colours keep their own meanings. The WORKS ON row in the MODS dock uses the same badges, in mixer order 3 1 2 4 . See Four decks for the deck view.","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"system-readout","t":"System readout","x":"SYSTEM READOUT puts CPU load, memory and temperature beside STEMS and MODS on the top bar. Open it to see deck 3 and 4 audio render times and active key shifters across all four decks. P99 is the time at or below which 99% of the last 256 rendered blocks finished; MAX is the longest. Short blocks are scaled to a full block. D3+D4 MAX adds both maxima and compares them with the 5,805 microseconds available per block. New shifts use a stricter 3,483 microsecond budget, leaving time for other work. These render numbers include decoding, time stretch and key shift; they do not measure the complete output path. Use them when you suspect the player is working hard, for example with stems on both decks and four decks running. Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap SYSTEM READOUT Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise The first setup step with live readings and four key shifters engaged. STEP Where you are in the setup. What the numbers mean CPU 100% means all four cores are busy. RAM leaves out cache. 80 C turns yellow, 90 C flashes red with HOT. Audio render time Each software deck shows its p99 and maximum render time in microseconds. LAST RUN means the reading is no longer live. Key shifters Counts shifted decks, including decks 1 and 2. The combined software maximum is shown against one audio block. DETECT METRICS Runs the current step. Push to move through the setup. Choose SYSTEM READOUT on the SCREEN page. Push DETECT METRICS . The setup looks for CPU, memory and the temperature sensor. Follow the remaining steps until the live readings show. After setup the row on the SCREEN page reads ON . On the top bar, METRICS STARTING - TAP TO SET UP means the readings have not arrived yet. METRICS STALE - TAP TO VERIFY means they stopped updating. Tap either one to open the setup again. Note Only the temperature of the main chip is available on the XDJ-XZ.","i":""},{"c":"screen-and-themes","a":"when-something-looks-wrong","t":"When something looks wrong","x":"Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap CLASSIC Tap MODERN Tap 3-BAND COLOURS Tap STANDARD Tap BLUE Tap RED Tap GREEN Tap AMBER Tap PURPLE Tap CYAN Tap PINK Tap WHITE Tap STANDARD Tap BLUE Tap RED Tap GREEN Tap AMBER Tap PURPLE Tap CYAN Tap PINK Tap WHITE Tap STANDARD Tap BLUE Tap RED Tap GREEN Tap AMBER Tap PURPLE Tap CYAN Tap PINK Tap WHITE Tap RESET 3-BAND COLOURS Tap RESET 3-BAND COLOURS Press BACK Press MENU What you see What to do The theme did not change Close MODS. The play screen takes the new theme once MODS is closed DECK VIEW is missing from SCREEN This player's USB loader cannot run decks 3 and 4. See Four decks STEMS waveforms look like 3-BAND The track has no prepared stems, or it has four stems. See Stems Keys show in the wrong notation Set KEY NOTATION. AS ON THE USB follows your library's own setting The waveform colours are not the ones you expect Check 3-BAND COLOURS. RESET 3-BAND COLOURS puts every band back to STANDARD","i":""},{"c":"connect","a":"","t":"Connect and DJ profiles","x":"CONNECT is the MODS section for people and computers: your DJ profile, the VJ.Tools link, the player's network and updates over the network. Everything here is optional. The player plays the same with all of it switched off. Open MODS with MENU , then choose CONNECT in the section rail.","i":""},{"c":"connect","a":"the-connect-page","t":"The CONNECT page","x":"Press MENU Tap CONNECT Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press BACK The four parts of CONNECT. The highlighted card is explained in the dock. DJ PROFILE Your DJ name and logo from the USB, for VJ screens. VJ.TOOLS The optional link to VJ.Tools on a computer, and the VJ.Tools screen view. NETWORK The player's network adapters and addresses. UPDATES Signed XZ Mods updates over the network. An update starts at the next power cycle. Dock Explains the highlighted card before you open it. The HOME card for CONNECT shows your active DJ profile and its USB, then the state of the VJ.Tools link, for example DJ Kai (USB 1) | VJ.Tools waiting . With no profile it reads No DJ profile .","i":""},{"c":"connect","a":"dj-profile","t":"DJ profile","x":"A DJ profile is your DJ name and logo, with an optional tagline. It lives on your USB, next to your music. VJ software such as VJ.Tools shows the profile of the USB that is playing on the master deck, so the screens behind you show who is playing. Nothing is stored on the XZ and nothing is uploaded. Press MENU Tap CONNECT Tap DJ PROFILE Tap SET UP DJ PROFILE Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise DJ Profile is an open standard. Any player, mixer or VJ program can read the same folder.","i":""},{"c":"connect","a":"make-a-profile-on-a-computer","t":"Make a profile on a computer","x":"Press MENU Tap CONNECT Tap DJ PROFILE Tap SET UP DJ PROFILE Tap CHECK USB FOR PROFILES Press BACK On the USB, make a folder named DJPROFILE at the top level. Inside it, make a folder with your DJ name, for example DJPROFILE/DJ Kai . Put your logo in that folder as logo.png or logo.jpg . Put the USB in the XZ, open CONNECT › DJ PROFILE and push CHECK USB FOR PROFILES . A folder with a usable logo is a profile. A folder without one is skipped. A USB shows at most 16 profiles. The XZ Mods app can also make and edit profiles. See The XZ Mods app .","i":""},{"c":"connect","a":"make-a-profile-on-the-xz","t":"Make a profile on the XZ","x":"You can type a profile on the player with the encoder or by touch. Press MENU Tap CONNECT Tap DJ PROFILE Tap SET UP DJ PROFILE Tap CREATE ON THIS XZ Type dj test on the screen keyboard Tap NEXT: LOGO Tap NO LOGO Tap NEXT: TAGLINE Type fixture set on the screen keyboard Tap NEXT: REVIEW Tap SAVE TO USB 1 Tap NEW PROFILE Type dj two on the screen keyboard Tap NEXT: LOGO Tap NO LOGO Tap NEXT: TAGLINE Tap SKIP TAGLINE Tap SAVE TO USB 1 Tap < PREV Tap MAKE ACTIVE Open CONNECT › DJ PROFILE . Push CREATE ON THIS XZ , or NEW PROFILE if the USB already has one. Type your DJ name on the on-screen keyboard, then push NEXT: LOGO . Pick a PNG or JPEG image from the USB, or NO LOGO . Images in your own DJPROFILE folder are listed first. Then push NEXT: TAGLINE . Type a few words, such as your genre, city or crew, and push NEXT: REVIEW . To leave the tagline out, push SKIP TAGLINE . Check the review, then push SAVE TO USB 1 or SAVE TO USB 2 . A new profile becomes the active profile on the USB you save it to. Only the DJPROFILE folder on that USB is written. Your music, playlists and stems are not touched. Step Controls Name and tagline The keyboard, SHIFT for capitals, #+= for symbols ( ABC goes back), SPACE , DELETE , BACK to the step before Logo One row per image on the USB, PREV and NEXT for more, RESCAN (or CHECK USB AGAIN ), NO LOGO , KEEP CURRENT when you edit Review CHANGE NAME , CHANGE LOGO , CHANGE TAGLINE , then SAVE TO USB 1 or SAVE TO USB 2 A name holds up to 64 characters and a tagline up to 80. With NO LOGO , your initial is shown on the accent colour. Logos are shown square over black. Nothing is saved until you push SAVE. The bottom line says NOTHING IS SAVED UNTIL YOU PRESS SAVE on the review step.","i":""},{"c":"connect","a":"choose-and-switch-profiles","t":"Choose and switch profiles","x":"With profiles on the USB, the DJ PROFILE page shows one profile at a time: its logo, name and tagline, which USB it is on, and whether it is active there. Control or line What it means < PREV , NEXT > Step through the profiles on both USBs. 2 OF 3 shows where you are EDIT Change this profile's name, logo or tagline MAKE ACTIVE Makes this the active profile on its USB. Only the USB is written NEW PROFILE Makes another profile on the USB, for an alias or a back to back set CHECK USB Reads both USB ports again ACTIVE ON THIS USB This profile is the one its USB says is playing SHOWN TO THE VJ NOW This is the profile VJ software sees right now FROM ITS FOLDER IN DJPROFILE A profile made from a folder and a logo OLDER CARD: EDIT IT IN VJ.TOOLS An older profile card. Edit it in VJ.Tools, or make a new profile Your active profile also sits in the MODS header, with its logo and name. Tap it, or highlight it and push, to switch between the profiles on both USBs. Note The player's own saved settings are MY SETTINGS in UTILITY. They are separate from your DJ profile.","i":""},{"c":"connect","a":"when-a-profile-will-not-save-or-show","t":"When a profile will not save or show","x":"Press MENU Tap CONNECT Tap DJ PROFILE Tap SET UP DJ PROFILE Tap CREATE ON THIS XZ Type dj test on the screen keyboard Tap NEXT: LOGO Tap pictures/alternate.jpg Tap NEXT: TAGLINE Tap SKIP TAGLINE Tap SAVE TO USB 1 Tap CHANGE LOGO Tap NO LOGO Tap NEXT: TAGLINE Tap SKIP TAGLINE Tap SAVE TO USB 1 Message What to do INSERT THE USB WITH YOUR MUSIC Put your USB in. Profiles live on the USB only NO DJ PROFILE ON THIS USB YET Make one on a computer or on the XZ, as above INSERT A USB FIRST Insert a USB before you push CREATE ON THIS XZ TYPE YOUR DJ NAME FIRST The name cannot be empty THE NAME IS FULL, THE TAGLINE IS FULL You reached 64 or 80 characters THAT USB IS NOT IN / PUT IT BACK Put the USB back in the port you are saving to THIS LOGO CANNOT BE USED / CHANGE LOGO Pick another image, or NO LOGO THIS PROFILE FILE IS DAMAGED / SAVE IT AGAIN FROM VJ.TOOLS Save the profile again from VJ.Tools or the XZ Mods app SAVING YOUR PROFILE TO THE USB / KEEP THE USB IN Wait. Do not pull the USB","i":""},{"c":"connect","a":"vj-tools","t":"VJ.Tools","x":"VJ.Tools is a desktop app for VJs. The VJ.TOOLS page lets VJ.Tools on a computer connect to the player, announces the player on the network, and can show the computer's picture instead of the play screen. Press MENU Tap CONNECT Tap VJ.TOOLS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise VJ.Tools connected and sending frames. The player still shows its own play screen. STATUS CONNECTED, WAITING FOR VJ.TOOLS, DISABLED or NOT AVAILABLE. DEVICE IP The player's address for VJ.Tools. PORT The port VJ.Tools connects to. PROTOCOL What the link carries. You only need it when you report a problem. RECEIVED FPS Frames per second arriving from VJ.Tools. NOT REPORTED until frames arrive. Screen in use NATIVE PLAY SCREEN ACTIVE, or COMPUTER SCREEN ACTIVE while the VJ.Tools view is on. VJ.TOOLS VIEW Shows the computer's VJ.Tools screen instead of the player screen. SCREEN SWITCH KEY What switches the VJ.Tools view while you play: LINK or an ONSCREEN button. VJ.TOOLS CONNECTION Lets VJ.Tools on a computer connect to this player. DISCOVERABLE Announces this player so VJ.Tools finds it on the network. vj.tools Where to get VJ.Tools. Control Choices What it does Waiting for VJ.Tools. The link controls are read only on this player Waiting for VJ.Tools. The link controls are read only on this player VJ.TOOLS VIEW ON, OFF ON shows the computer's VJ.Tools screen on the player. OFF shows the play screen SCREEN SWITCH KEY LINK, ONSCREEN LINK makes the LINK key switch the view. ONSCREEN puts a button for it on the screen. See Controls on the player VJ.TOOLS CONNECTION ON, OFF Lets VJ.Tools connect DISCOVERABLE ON, OFF Lets VJ.Tools find the player without typing its address When a link control shows READ ONLY , MODS cannot change it on this player. Pushing it shows CONTROL IS NOT AVAILABLE . To switch the view without opening MODS, use the key you chose under SCREEN SWITCH KEY. You can also give the button above LINK the job VJ.TOOLS SCREEN in PLAY › BUTTON ABOVE LINK . It needs an enabled, connected VJ.Tools link, and says so when there is none. In CLASSIC, a VJ.TOOLS button can appear on the top bar. It reads EXIT VJ while the view is on. Experimental The VJ.Tools view has shown video on the player during development. Long playback and touch while the view is on have not been accepted yet. Keep it off during a set unless you have tested it.","i":""},{"c":"connect","a":"network","t":"Network","x":"NETWORK sets up the player's network adapters for VJ.Tools and network updates. You do not need it to play. Press MENU Tap CONNECT Tap NETWORK Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise The NETWORK page before the adapters have been read. Status line What the page knows now. CHANGES LAST UNTIL REBOOT reminds you that nothing here is permanent. What is known Which parts the player reports, and that nothing changes until you apply. SET UP NETWORK Starts the setup: read the adapters, choose, review, apply. DETECT ADAPTERS AGAIN Reads the adapters again, for example after you plug in a cable. NETWORK UPDATES Opens UPDATES. NETWORK SETUP before the adapters have been read NETWORK SETUP before the adapters have been read Setup runs in four steps. Every change lasts until the player is switched off. Detect. The page lists each adapter with its link state and current address. Choose. Pick an adapter and how it gets an address: KEEP CURRENT , DHCP ON or STATIC IP . With STATIC IP, use EDIT IP , EDIT MASK / PREFIX and EDIT GATEWAY . PRIORITY UP and PRIORITY DOWN set which adapter XZ Mods prefers. Review. Push REVIEW CHANGES and read the summary. Apply. Push APPLY FOR THIS BOOT . The page then checks the result. REVERT TRIAL / MODS DHCP OFF undoes what this setup added. The keypad for an address, mask or gateway. Field Which value you are typing and what you have typed. Digits and point Type the address one character at a time. BACKSPACE Deletes the last character. CLEAR Empties the field. DONE Keeps the value and goes back to the setup. CANCEL Leaves the value as it was. Message What to do DETECT ACTUAL ADAPTERS FIRST Push DETECT ADAPTERS AGAIN, then choose ENTER A VALID IP AND CONTIGUOUS MASK / PREFIX Check the address and mask you typed ENTER A VALID GATEWAY OR KEEP ROUTE OFF Type a valid gateway, or set MODS ROUTE: OFF NETWORK CHANGED / DETECT AND CHOOSE AGAIN A cable or adapter changed. Start the setup again RELOAD A PRIVATE USB IMAGE WITH NETWORK SUPPORT This USB loader has no network support. Update the loader with the XZ Mods app, then push VERIFY RELOADED LOADER Experimental The NETWORK pages still use technical wording and may change. Your changes never outlive a power cycle, so switching the player off and on always brings back its own network setup.","i":""},{"c":"connect","a":"updates-over-the-network","t":"Updates over the network","x":"UPDATES fetches a newer signed XZ Mods version from the XZ Mods app on your computer and saves it to the USB. The update starts at the next power cycle. Your music stays where it is. Press MENU Tap CONNECT Tap UPDATES Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise UPDATES before the update server has been found. What it does Downloads a signed XZ Mods version to the USB. Power cycle to activate. Recovery Updates change XZ Mods only. The original USB loader is the way back. SET UP NETWORK UPDATES Opens UPDATE SETUP, which finds the update server. DOWNLOAD UPDATE Downloads the update to the USB. It activates after a power cycle. PREVIOUS VERSION Goes back to the previous XZ Mods version at the next power cycle. REPORT AN ISSUE Opens REPORT AN ISSUE in EXTRAS. NETWORK SETUP Opens NETWORK. The three things the player needs before it can update over the network. Steps Use the updated USB loader, start network updates in the desktop app, connect the XZ to that network. DETECT UPDATE SERVER Asks the update server for a newer signed XZ Mods version. BACK TO UPDATES Returns to UPDATES. Prepare the USB with a current XZ Mods app, so the loader supports network updates. In the XZ Mods app, start network updates. See The XZ Mods app . Connect the XZ to the same network as the computer. Use NETWORK if it needs an address. Open CONNECT › UPDATES › SET UP NETWORK UPDATES and push DETECT UPDATE SERVER . Back on UPDATES, push DOWNLOAD UPDATE . Switch the player off and on to start the new version. Caution Never switch the player off while the update is being written to the USB, and never update during a set. To undo an update, push PREVIOUS VERSION and switch the player off and on. Network updates change XZ Mods only. If the player will not start XZ Mods at all, restore or update the USB loader with the XZ Mods app.","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"","t":"Extras","x":"EXTRAS holds what is not about playing a set: games, apps from a USB, reporting a problem and the About page. Nothing here starts on its own. The XZ always starts in its normal DJ view, and a game or app opens only when you choose it. Open MODS with MENU , then choose EXTRAS in the section rail.","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"the-extras-page","t":"The EXTRAS page","x":"Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 3 clicks clockwise Press BACK The four parts of EXTRAS. GAMES Doom and Chex Quest, Beat Arcade, Wave Rider, Rhythm Lab and Static Surfer. USB APPS XZ SDK apps from a USB. REPORT AN ISSUE Send a problem, a question or an idea from the player. ABOUT XZ MODS Credits, links and support. Dock Explains the highlighted card. For GAMES it reminds you that audio keeps playing. The HOME card for EXTRAS counts the games and the apps found on your USBs, for example 6 games | no USB apps .","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"games","t":"Games","x":"Every game runs on the XZ itself. The music keeps playing while you play, and PLAY and track search keep their normal jobs in Beat Arcade. Doom and Beat Arcade make no sound of their own. Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Tap GAMES Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise Every game, plus USB WAD LOADER and MY HOUSE / SETUP. DOOM / CHOOSE WAD Classic Doom or Doom II. Choose the game files next. CHEX QUEST The original Chex Quest. BEAT ARCADE Pong and Breakout scored on the beat, played with the jog. WAVE RIDER Surf the playing track's waveform with the jog. USB WAD LOADER Choose a Doom base game and an optional add-on from the USB. MY HOUSE / SETUP Checks for the engine the My House mod needs. RHYTHM LAB / 10 STUDIES Ten short rhythm studies played on the pads. STATIC SURFER A runner game set to the playing track. Game What it is Needs Beat Arcade experimental Solo Pong, Pong Duel on both jogs, Solo Breaks and a two-player Breakout. Tap CUE on the beat to build charge Nothing. Built in Wave Rider experimental The loaded track's waveform becomes hills. Steer with the jog, hold CUE to add weight. Solo, Co-op or Versus Nothing. Built in Rhythm Lab Ten short rhythm studies for the jogs and pads. They are prototypes, and you can rate each one Nothing. Built in Static Surfer A rhythm platformer. Tap to jump and tilt the jog to pass through the glyphs Nothing. Built in Doom Classic Doom or Doom II Game files on the USB Chex Quest The original Chex Quest Game files on the USB","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"moving-around-a-game","t":"Moving around a game","x":"You do not need the touchscreen in any game. Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Tap GAMES Tap WAVE RIDER Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Push ROTARY SELECTOR Push ROTARY SELECTOR Turn the left jog wheel Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Press CUE on the left deck Turn the left jog wheel Tap the screen Control In a game Turn the encoder Moves a ring over the controls on the screen Push the encoder Presses the control under the ring BACK Steps back Touch Presses what you touch. The ring hides until you turn the encoder again","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"beat-arcade","t":"Beat Arcade","x":"Turn the jog to move your paddle and tap CUE on each beat as the moving light meets the target. Good notes build charge. Eight good notes in a row earn a shield, and sixteen build a Drop that fires on the next downbeat. Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Tap GAMES Tap BEAT ARCADE Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise, then push it Turn the left jog wheel Press CUE on the left deck Press pad G on the left deck Tap the screen Tap the screen Control Action Jog Moves the paddle. In the menu, chooses a game CUE or pad A Strikes on the beat. Starts, resumes and rematches Pad B Wide paddle for 16 beats Pad C Saves one miss with a shield Pad D Queues a Drop on the next downbeat Pads E and F Aim the next return Pad G Changes the scene between Tunnel, Grid and Orbit Pad H Lines up with the mixer tempo, or taps a tempo PLAY, track search Work as usual on the music DJ VIEW on screen Saves the round and gives every control back to the deck Tap the source display at the top of the game to choose where the beat comes from: an analysed USB track, Pro DJ Link, the mixer tempo or four taps on pad H. For mixer tempo, set Beat FX to the channel you play, usually MASTER, and use AUTO BPM. While Beat Arcade runs, touching the platter does not pause or scratch the music. Choose DJ VIEW before you go back to mixing.","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"wave-rider","t":"Wave Rider","x":"Choose Solo , Co-op or Versus , then the deck whose track you ride. In Solo that deck's jog steers. With two players, the left jog is player 1 and the right jog is player 2. Hold CUE or a top-row pad to add weight and gain speed downhill. Let go as the ground rises, and the crest throws you into the air. Turn the jog to tilt the board. Clockwise points the nose down. Land with the slope to keep your speed. Clean landings in a row score more. EASY is the default and keeps the angle you set in the air. NORMAL and HARD are stricter. A missed landing never stops the music.","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"doom-and-chex-quest","t":"Doom and Chex Quest","x":"Doom and Chex Quest need game files on the USB. The XZ Mods app can download and check free Doom shareware, Chex Quest and Freedoom data when you prepare the USB. For the full Doom or Doom II you supply your own files. See The XZ Mods app . Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Tap GAMES Tap USB WAD LOADER Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise The Doom page before its game files have been checked. Status USB GAME SETUP NEEDED until the files and engine have been checked. Controls What each control does while the game is open. Notes The buttons belong to the game while it is open. Exit gives back the DJ screen. Game sound is off. SET UP DOOM Reads START DOOM once setup is done. Starts the game full screen. DJ audio keeps playing. USB WADS Opens USB WAD LOADER to choose the game files. Player control In Doom Jog Turn left or right PLAY, or pad A Walk forward Pad B Walk back CUE, or pad C Shoot Pad D Use, for example open a door Pads E and F Strafe Pad G Enter Pad H, or BACK Game menu Turn and push the encoder Moves through the game menu and enters To end the game, touch EXIT . The player goes back to the screen you had before. The three setup steps for Doom. Steps Find the Doom engine on the USB loader, choose a base game and optional map, then start Doom to check. Where the files go A WADS or VJTOOLS/DOOM folder on the USB. The XZ Mods app Prepares a Doom USB for you. CHOOSE USB GAME FILES Opens USB WAD LOADER. BACK TO DOOM Returns to the Doom page. The loader with no game files found yet. File list One row per game file on the USB. Choose the base game, then an add-on if you want one. PREV and NEXT Pages through a long list. RESCAN USB Searches both USB ports again. NO ADD-ON Plays the base game with no add-on. SETUP Opens GAME SETUP. If the list says PUT .WAD FILES ON USB, THEN RESCAN , copy the files to the USB on a computer, put it back and push RESCAN USB .","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"my-house","t":"My House","x":"My House is a Doom mod that needs the GZDoom engine. The MY HOUSE page checks for that engine and the files, but the classic Doom engine cannot load this mod, and the XZ Mods app no longer copies it to the USB. Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Tap GAMES Tap MY HOUSE / SETUP Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise The My House check. Steps Find the GZDoom engine, choose the Doom II data and MYHOUSE.PK3, check and start. Limit The classic Doom engine cannot load this mod. CHECK ENGINE Checks the engine and My House files on the USB. BACK TO GAMES Returns to GAMES.","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"usb-apps","t":"USB apps","x":"USB APPS runs apps built with the XZ SDK from a USB. DJ controls keep working while an app runs. Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Tap USB APPS Tap SET UP APPS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise USB APPS while the app manager is not running. AUTOLOAD ON starts apps in the autoload folder when their USB goes in. OFF starts apps only when you run them. Status How many packages were found, or why there are none. Message The one thing to do next. PREV and NEXT Pages through the apps. RESCAN USB Searches the USB again for apps. SET UP APPS A four-step guide from finding apps to a live test. Put apps on a USB in VJ.Tools/XZ-SDK/Applications . Apps in VJ.Tools/XZ-SDK/Autoload start on their own when AUTOLOAD is on. Each app row shows what kind of package it is and its state. State Meaning RUNNING ON SCREEN An app is showing on the player RUNNING IN BACKGROUND A service is running APPLIED A profile package is in use FAILED The app stopped. Push RUN AGAIN BLOCKED The package cannot run. Push SET UP to see how to fix it CHECKING The app manager is still reading the package Step 1 of SET UP APPS, with the app manager not running. Step Which of the four steps you are on. Step tabs DETECT, FOLDERS, INSTALL, LIVE TEST. Tap one to jump to it. Result What this step found. What to do The one action that fixes it. CHECK AGAIN Runs this step again. BACK TO APPS Returns to USB APPS. Detect. Finds the app manager and any apps on the USB. Folders. Choose START WHEN I TAP RUN or START ON USB INSERT . Install. Copy apps to the USB. The page shows the packer command for the desktop. Live test. Push RUN TEST APP . When it shows, push IT WORKS . Note APP MANAGER NOT RUNNING means XZ Mods did not start it. Switch the XZ off, start it again with its XZ Mods USB in, then push CHECK AGAIN .","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"report-an-issue","t":"Report an issue","x":"REPORT AN ISSUE sends the maintainer a problem, a question or an idea from the player. You say what it is about and, if you like, what happened. The player adds its own details. A topic and SEND take three presses. Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Tap REPORT AN ISSUE Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to SOMETHING ISN'T WORKING and push it Push ROTARY SELECTOR to choose SKIP, I'LL ADD IT ON MY COMPUTER What's this about? Push one of the five topics, or NOT SURE . What happened? Type a few words, or push SKIP, I'LL ADD IT ON MY COMPUTER . Ready to send. Check the summary, then push SEND REPORT . With the encoder, push three times: the first topic, SKIP, then SEND. Step 1: what the report is about. WHAT'S THIS ABOUT? One question. Each topic goes straight to the next step. Topics SOMETHING GOT WORSE, SOMETHING ISN'T WORKING, IT SHOULD WORK DIFFERENTLY, I HAVE A NEW IDEA and HOW DO I...? NOT SURE Skips the question. The report still goes. Steps Where you are: step 1 of 3. Step 2, before you type. SKIP is lit: one push goes on without words. OPTIONAL You can send a report without typing anything. Your words Up to 280 characters. The count is on the right. Keyboard Turn and push the encoder, or tap the keys. The first letter is a capital. SKIP, I'LL ADD IT ON MY COMPUTER Goes on without words. Your computer asks what happened later. NEXT Goes on with what you typed. Once you type, NEXT is lit instead. WHAT HAPPENED? with words typed: NEXT is lit WHAT HAPPENED? with words typed: NEXT is lit Step 3: what will be sent. ABOUT The topic you chose. WHAT HAPPENED Your words, or a note that you add them on your computer. ALSO INCLUDED Added by the player: the XZ Mods version, your settings, this stick's loader ID, the recent USB diary and the screen you were on. No music, track names or file names. IT GOES TO The XZ Mods inbox when the player is online, otherwise this stick. CHANGE Goes back to that step. Your words are kept. SEND REPORT Sends it. BACK goes back a step. If you leave the page before sending, your words wait for you there.","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"after-you-send","t":"After you send","x":"The report goes one of three ways. Whichever it is, nothing is lost and you never type it again. Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Tap REPORT AN ISSUE Turn ROTARY SELECTOR to SOMETHING ISN'T WORKING and push it Type test report on the screen keyboard Tap NEXT Tap SEND REPORT Tap EDIT REPORT Tap CHANGE Tap HOW DO I...? Tap NEXT Tap SEND REPORT Tap DONE The screen says What happened What to do SENT and a reference like R-4F7K-2M9Q It reached the XZ Mods inbox Finish it on your computer: the XZ Mods app reminds you and shows the same reference SAVED ON THIS STICK The player is offline, its clock is not set, the loader is from an older XZ Mods app, or the inbox did not take it Plug the stick into your computer. The XZ Mods app opens the report NOT SENT YET It could not be sent, and the stick could not take it Do what the line says (put the stick back, use a writable stick, make room on it), then push TRY AGAIN SENT: the reference to look for in the XZ Mods app SAVED ON THIS STICK NOT SENT YET: the reason, TRY AGAIN and EDIT REPORT While it sends. You can keep playing and close MODS SENT: the reference to look for in the XZ Mods app SAVED ON THIS STICK NOT SENT YET: the reason, TRY AGAIN and EDIT REPORT While it sends. You can keep playing and close MODS A saved report waits in VJ.Tools/XZ-Mods-reports/pending/ on the stick, up to 32 of them. The XZ Mods app sends it from there and moves it to sent/ . TRY AGAIN sends the same report, so the maintainer gets it once.","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"report-an-error-from-the-dock","t":"Report an error from the dock","x":"When an error shows in the dock's top row, REPORT THIS beside it opens REPORT AN ISSUE at WHAT HAPPENED? with SOMETHING ISN'T WORKING chosen. Push SKIP and SEND REPORT , and the error goes with it. Every report includes an error on screen, however you open it. Press MENU Tap REPORT THIS Tap SKIP, I'LL ADD IT ON MY COMPUTER Tap SEND REPORT A player warning in the dock, here E-8307: USB ACCESS ERROR, with REPORT THIS. REPORT THIS Opens REPORT AN ISSUE about this error. Touch only: with the encoder, open EXTRAS › REPORT AN ISSUE. In MODERN a deck's counter error keeps the dock's top row, with REPORT THIS beside SHOW DECK. REPORT THIS Reports this error. SHOW DECK closes MODS onto the deck.","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"what-the-player-sends","t":"What the player sends","x":"The report holds facts the player can check, never text read from its screens: the topic and your words, if any; the XZ Mods version and a fingerprint of your settings, with a few of them (stems, gate cue, interface, theme, deck view, browse preview); the loader ID from ABOUT and the ID of the computer that made the loader, so the report reaches your own XZ Mods app; the screen MODS was opened from (PLAY, BROWSE and so on), the interface, the deck view and the code of any error on screen; known status codes from decks 3 and 4 and the player, and the recent entries of the USB diary on this stick. It never holds music, track or playlist names, file names or network addresses. Only the maintainer reads it. You can also report from the XZ Mods app. See Messages and troubleshooting .","i":""},{"c":"extras","a":"about-xz-mods","t":"About XZ Mods","x":"Press MENU Tap EXTRAS Tap ABOUT XZ MODS Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise The About page with XZMODS.COM highlighted and its QR code shown. Credits Who made XZ Mods. Links XZMODS.COM, INSTAGRAM, BOOK OPTICMYSTIC, VJ.TOOLS, GITHUB / SOURCE, CREDITS / NOTICES and SUPPORT / CASH APP. QR code The highlighted link as a QR code. Scan it with your phone. Address The link the QR code opens. Thanks Thanks, and a reminder that XZ Mods is an independent project. Loader The ID of this stick's loader, written by the XZ Mods app. Reports from this stick carry it. An older loader shows Loader: not identified and can still report. Turn the encoder to a link, then push or tap it to show it as a QR code. Scan the code for CREDITS / NOTICES to read the full credits, licences and matching source. Support is voluntary. Every feature stays available without it.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"","t":"The XZ Mods app","x":"The XZ Mods app runs on your computer. It puts XZ Mods on a USB, makes stems for your tracks, makes your DJ profile, keeps the app and your USB up to date, holds tools for your library, games and the XZ screen, and sends your reports and ideas to the maintainer. It never formats a drive and never changes your music or the library your DJ software exported. You need 64-bit Windows with WebView2, or a Mac with macOS 14 or later. Making stems needs a Windows computer or an Apple silicon Mac. On an Intel Mac you can still import stems you made elsewhere.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"around-the-app","t":"Around the app","x":"The bar along the top has five sections for your work, then the Manual and About and, on the right, Feedback. The section you are in is filled yellow. The page sits on the raised panel below it. Section What it is for USB Install or update XZ Mods on a USB, add your DJ profile and games Stems Make stems for the tracks on your music USB, or import stems you already have DJ Profile Your name and logo on the XZ, and the profile track Updates App updates, the XZ Mods version for your USB, and network updates for your XZ Tools Repair library, Game downloads and XZ Screen Manual This manual, with search, animations and your place in it About The app, its maker, links, disclaimers and open-source licenses Feedback Report a problem, request a feature or ask a question, and follow what you sent Tools, Updates and the Manual list what they hold down the left, beside the page: the tools, the three Updates pages, or the manual's chapters. The button at the far left of the top bar hides that list and shows it again, and the app remembers your choice. The top left names the player firmware the app prepares USBs for, XDJ-XZ 1.26. The app version is at the top right. In a narrower window point at Preview to see it. The app opens as large as its pages need, but never larger than your screen. In a narrow window the sections show only their icons. Point at one to see its name. The list on the left then opens over the page from the button at the top left, and closes when you pick something.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"usb","t":"USB","x":"USB is the first page. Plug in your XZ USB, or any USB stick, and the app finds it. When only one USB is connected, it opens by itself. No USB yet. The app keeps looking, so plug one in. Write to a folder instead… prepares a folder on this computer Several USBs. Each card says whether XZ Mods is on it yet and whether it holds music exported from your DJ software","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"choose-a-usb-or-a-folder","t":"Choose a USB or a folder","x":"The USB list shows every connected USB the app can write XZ Mods to. Any file system works, FAT32 or exFAT, and each card shows it beside the drive letter. Choose a card to open that USB. Two USBs and a folder to choose from. One line names the drives the app leaves out. USB A USB the app can write to, with its drive and file system. Write to a folder instead… Prepares a folder on this computer instead of a USB. Drives not shown A read-only USB, or a disk of this computer, with the reason. Look again Searches for USBs at once. Write to a folder instead… puts the loader and its settings in a folder on this computer. Copy everything in it to the top of a USB stick afterward. Games are added only when you write to a USB itself. The list comes back whenever you step back from a USB: Change USB on the dashboard, Cancel in a guide, or Esc on the dashboard. The USB you left does not open by itself again until you plug in or remove a drive, so you can pick another one. Its card is still selected, and Enter opens it again.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"the-usb-dashboard","t":"The USB dashboard","x":"Once a USB is open, the page shows one status and one action for it. A fresh USB. XZ Mods is not on it yet, so the one action is Install XZ Mods. Sections USB, Stems, DJ Profile, Updates and Tools. USB The USB's name and drive. Free space The file system, the free space and a bar of how full the USB is. Change USB Goes back to the USB list, to choose another USB or a folder. Status What XZ Mods found on this USB. Action The one thing to do next. Here it installs XZ Mods. DJ profile The active profile on the USB. Add or Edit opens the profile step. Games How many games are on the USB. Choose opens the games list. Stems How many tracks have stems. Prepare opens the Stems section. Build The XZ Mods build that goes on the USB. Change opens XZ Mods version in Updates. Four decks How four decks work. It sets nothing up. See Four decks in the app . Show every file A read-only list of what XZ Mods keeps on this USB. Feedback Reports and ideas for the maintainer. See Feedback . The status changes with what the app finds: Status Action What it means XZ Mods is not on this USB yet Install XZ Mods Adds the loader, free games and your DJ profile. Music and playlists stay as they are. Update available Update USB The USB has an older build. Updating backs up its loader first. See what changes lists what is new. Up to date none The chosen build is already on this USB. Choose which XZ Mods build goes on this USB Use the newest build No build is chosen on this computer yet. The button picks the one that came with the app. No XZ Mods build is on this computer yet Set up mod versions Opens a short guide that finds or imports a build. Update available, with the number of changes Up to date No build chosen yet. Use the newest build picks the one that came with the app","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"install-or-update-xz-mods","t":"Install or update XZ Mods","x":"Install XZ Mods and Update USB open a short guide. The steps that do not apply are left out, so the count at the top changes. Every step ends in the same bar. Back on the left returns to the step before; from the first step it returns to the dashboard. The way forward is on the right. Esc does the same as Back. Cancel at the top leaves the guide without writing anything and shows the USB list, so you can choose another USB or a folder. While the USB is written there is no Back, and the done screen has Done instead, because a write cannot be undone. Your DJ profile. Appears when the USB has no profile yet. Type your name and add a logo, or choose Skip for now and add it later. Choose the screen the XZ shows. New interface (MODERN) or Standard XDJ-XZ interface (CLASSIC). See Getting started . Ready to write. A checklist of everything the write will do. Writing. The progress of each part. Underneath, the app explains four decks while you wait. Done. What was written, what to do on the XZ, and how four decks work. Optional support. A thank-you page with a voluntary support link. Every feature works whether you contribute or not. Four decks is not a step of the guide. Nothing about it happens while the USB is written: you set it up at the player, whenever you want. See Four decks in the app . Your DJ profile. Skip for now leaves it for later Choose the screen the XZ shows. The selected card plays a short clip of it. Progress Which step you are on. Cancel Leaves the guide. Nothing is written. New interface MODERN. XZ Mods draws the whole player screen. Standard XDJ-XZ interface CLASSIC. The player's own screen with MODS added. Classic themes can restyle it. Switch later How to change your mind on the player: the button above LINK first, then the menu, each with a video of the player. Back The step before. From the first step, the dashboard. Next The next step. Note The two small pictures under the cards show an older version of the MODS menu. On the player, INTERFACE is on the SCREEN page. Ready to write, with Change games open. Under the list, a line says music, playlists and prepared stems are never touched. Loader Adds the XZ Mods loader, or backs up and updates it. Games The free games that will be copied. Interface The screen the XZ starts with. Settings file A USB without settings gets a new settings file. Change games Opens or hides the games list. Add all free games Ticks every download. None unticks the ones not on the USB yet. Game state WILL ADD, NOT ON USB, or already on the USB. Add Ticks one game. The size is what it adds to the USB. Back The step before. Write to USB Writes everything in the checklist. Beat Arcade, Wave Rider, Rhythm Lab and Static Surfer are built into the loader and always come with it. Doom shareware, Chex Quest and Freedoom Phase 2 are free downloads that the app checks and copies to VJTOOLS\\Games on the USB. A fresh USB gets every free game unless you untick it. An update keeps the games the USB already has and adds none on its own. Under the checklist, Eject the USB when writing finishes ejects it for you so you can take it straight to the XZ. Press Write to USB in the bar under the checklist. If a newer build needs a setting changed on the USB, the app first asks in Adjust USB settings for this version . It saves a copy of the settings file first and puts it back if the loader write fails. Your USB is ready. Four decks and the optional support link follow further down. Result Your USB is ready, or Finished, with something to check. What was written One line per part. A game that did not download says why. On the XZ What to do with the USB next, and how to switch between CLASSIC and MODERN with the button above LINK . Four decks How four decks work. See Four decks in the app . Done Back to the dashboard. Eject USB Ejects the USB so you can unplug it. Under Four decks, Support XZ Mods (optional) opens the optional support page, and Eject the USB by itself next time ejects the USB on its own after the next write. If a game download failed, Retry the failed games tries only those, and the USB is not ejected until you have. When the write also saved a DJ profile, Make the profile track opens the profile track steps. Writing. The progress of each part shows inside the guide The USB is ejected and can be unplugged","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"four-decks-in-the-app","t":"Four decks in the app","x":"Four decks is set up at the player, so the app explains it rather than asking you to do anything. The USB list and the dashboard show a Four decks row. While a USB is written, and again on the done screen, a Four decks section shows the cable animation and the three things to do at the player. The Four decks section on the done screen. Four decks Experimental. Nothing to do now. You set it up at the player when you want it. Cable animation The loopback cable from the rear USB-B socket to a top port. The animation shows USB 1; USB 2 works too. Pause cable animation Stops and starts the animation. With reduced motion turned on, the app shows a still picture. At the player Cable from the rear USB-B socket to top USB 1 or 2, music in the other top port (a stick, or one USB 2.0 hub), and CH 3 INPUT and CH 4 INPUT set to USB. How four decks work Opens the Four decks chapter of this manual. How four decks work and the Four decks row both open the Four decks chapter of this manual. If the build just written has no four-deck engine, the section says so and offers Choose the four-deck build , which opens the four-deck build choice in XZ Mods version . Save it, then update the USB.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"stems","t":"Stems","x":"Stems makes vocal, harmonic and drum stems for the tracks on your music USB and writes them beside each track. Plug in the USB your DJ software exports your music to. The app lists every track on it. Your tracks and the library your DJ software exported stay as they are. Twelve tracks selected and the stem engine set up. USB Your music USB. Its menu also offers Choose a folder and Look for USBs again. Tracks How many tracks the USB holds and how many have stems. Estimate How many tracks you selected, about how much space their stems take and what is left after. Prepare Makes stems for the selected tracks. The label counts them. Engine The stem engine and the quality in use. Change sets another quality. Tabs Show All, Missing, Ready, Can't prepare, or only the Selected tracks. Search Finds a title or artist. Import stems Brings in stems you made elsewhere. Select Ticks a track. The box in the header ticks every Missing track in view. Status Ready, Missing, Not yet, No audio file, Preparing, Queued, Failed or Damaged. Details Opens the track's details. Status What it means What to do Ready Stems are on the USB Nothing. Open the details to Verify them Missing No stems yet Select it and prepare Not yet XZ Mods cannot prepare this format yet, such as AIFF Export the track as WAV, FLAC or MP3 No audio file The track's file is not on the USB Export the track to the USB again from your DJ software Failed Preparing stopped, with the reason under it Fix the reason, then Retry Damaged Verify found a broken stem page Select it and prepare it again Prepare again Made by an older version Open the details and choose Prepare again A batch holds up to 100 tracks. The estimate turns amber when space gets tight and red when the selection does not fit. The button then reads Prepare N that fit and prepares the tracks in order until the next one would not fit. While a batch runs, each row moves from Queued to Preparing to Ready, and the bar shows the track, the step and about how long is left. The first time on a new computer it says Timing this computer until it has measured. Cancel stops within a second. Finished tracks are kept. When the batch ends, the bar offers the next step. No music USB found. Connect a USB opens a short guide to find or choose one The selection does not fit. Prepare 7 that fit A batch running, with the step and the time left Finished with one failure. Retry 1 failed After a batch What it offers A track failed Retry N failed You pressed Cancel Prepare N remaining The USB was unplugged Continue . Nothing is left half-written The USB filled up Choose fewer tracks Open a row for its details. A Ready track shows who prepared it and offers Verify , which reads every stem page without changing the USB, Import stems to replace them, and Prepare again . Prepare again keeps the current stems until the new ones pass their check.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"set-up-the-stem-engine","t":"Set up the stem engine","x":"The first time, the button reads Set up stem engine . It opens a short guide that ends on a working engine. Check. The app looks at this computer's graphics card or processor. Choose. Pick a quality. The recommended one is marked for this computer. Install. The app downloads what the engine needs once and checks every file. Test. It separates 30 seconds of your first selected track and tells you how long a whole track will take. Nothing is written to the USB. Quality Use it for Balanced The best quality. Recommended with a graphics card or Apple silicon Fast Good separation in about half the time. Recommended without a graphics card Light Computers without a graphics card and with little memory. Vocals bleed more If setup cannot finish, it names the one reason and offers the fix. For example, when the graphics driver is too old, Use the processor sets up the engine on the processor instead. Set up stem engine replaces Prepare until the engine is set up Step 1. The graphics card the engine will use Step 2. Choose quality Step 3. What it downloads, and the free space on this computer Step 4. The test result, then Prepare 12 tracks The driver is too old. Use the processor, or update the driver and check again","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"import-stems-you-already-have","t":"Import stems you already have","x":"Choose Import stems in the toolbar, or Import stems made elsewhere in a track's details. Drop stem files or a ZIP into the window, or choose files. WAV, FLAC, MP3 and AIFF sets work. Add files. From the toolbar, also pick which track the stems are for. Check. The app places each file on VOCALS, DRUMS or HARMONICS by its name and lines the stems up with the track on your USB. Change any Goes to choice you disagree with. Leave out skips a file. Write. Write stems to USB writes the stems and checks them. Two files need a place. Play a file to hear what it is Stems written and checked A vocals and instrumental pair needs the stem engine to pull the drums out of the instrumental. If the engine is not set up yet, the import offers Set up stem engine and carries on afterward. To use stems on the player, see Stems .","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"dj-profile","t":"DJ Profile","x":"DJ Profile makes and edits the profiles on a USB. A profile is your name, logo and colour. The XZ shows each profile as a logo tile, and the active one is the DJ the XZ and VJ software on the same network see. Profiles are saved on the USB only. Nothing is uploaded. To use them on the player, see Connect and DJ profiles . A new profile. DJ name Your name as it should read on the XZ. Logo A PNG or JPEG up to 8 MB. A transparent PNG looks best. You can add alternate logos. Colour The profile colour. The first swatch matches the USB's colour in your DJ software. On the XZ The header and the logo tile as the XZ draws them. What VJ software sees Your name and links as VJ software reads them. More An optional tagline, links and more. The profiles on a USB after a save. Create profile track The next step after a save. Profile tile One tile per profile. Active The profile the XZ uses. Edit Changes this profile. New DJ profile Adds another profile to the USB. Profile track A track that carries your profile to players that cannot read extra files. For players that only read tracks, a profile track carries your name, logos and links. It is a silent song, so it goes through your DJ software like any other track. Making a profile track. Steps Where, Create, then Add it to your library. This computer Saves the track in your Music folder, ready for your DJ software. Choose folder Saves the track somewhere else. Copy on the USB Also puts a copy in your profile folder on the USB. Create or Cancel Makes the track, or leaves without one.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"updates","t":"Updates","x":"Updates keeps every version in one place, on three pages listed on the left: App updates for this app, XZ Mods version for the build that goes on your USB, and Network updates to send that build to XZs on your network. Updates opens on App updates. A yellow dot on Updates and on App updates in its list means a newer app is ready.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"app-updates","t":"App updates","x":"The app is up to date. Updates pages App updates, XZ Mods version and Network updates. Updates opens on App updates. Version The app version on this computer. Status Up to date, or the newer version on offer. Check for updates Checks now. Download and install update appears when there is one. What's new The release notes. Other downloads The installer and the portable ZIP. On Windows the app checks for updates by itself at launch and shows Review update at the top of the page when one is ready. The installer updates the app and opens it again. Mac versions download from the release page. Caution Updating the app does not change the loader on your USB. Open the USB page afterward and choose Update USB .","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"xz-mods-version","t":"XZ Mods version","x":"XZ Mods version chooses which build goes on your USB the next time you install or update it. Saving your choice does not write to any USB. The saved build choice. Verified Says whether the build was checked on a real XDJ-XZ. Saved choice The build your next install or update uses. Details Its channel, whether it stays on the USB and where it came from. Change mod version Every build on this computer. Keep this version on the USB A loader built with this on skips network updates, so the USB stays on this build. Save choice and Import a build Saves the choice, or adds a build from a folder. Set up four decks Chooses the included four-deck build. Restore or update a loader by hand Updates the loader on a USB you choose and keeps a backup of the old one. Lower on the page: Restore or update a loader by hand updates the loader on a USB you choose and keeps a backup of the old one. Music and saved settings stay in place. Prepare from a downloaded firmware file builds the loader from a firmware 1.26 file you choose, into a folder you choose. Import a build takes a prepared XZ Mods resources folder, or a whole XZ Mods app folder that holds one. The app checks every file before it adds the build. Imported builds are not checked on a real XDJ-XZ.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"network-updates","t":"Network updates","x":"Network updates sends the build installed on this computer to XZs on your local network. Each XZ checks the signed update, saves it on its USB and starts it at the next boot. The update server, before it starts. Choose mod version A USB built with Keep this version on the USB ignores network updates. Change that here. Detect adapters Lists this computer's network connections. XZ network adapter The connection that reaches the XZ. Start update server Offers the update on that network until you cancel. On the XZ What to do on the player. Prepare or update the USB loader once, so it supports network updates. Choose Detect adapters , then the adapter connected to the XZ network. Choose Start update server . On the XZ, open CONNECT › UPDATES , then download the update. See Updates over the network . Switch the XZ off and on when you are ready to start the new version. Network updates change XZ Mods and the game engine. They keep your music and the original USB loader, so you can always go back. Cancel stops the server. Note The app's step 3 still says MODS › Extras › Network updates. On the player the page is CONNECT › UPDATES.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"tools","t":"Tools","x":"Tools holds what you need now and then, grouped by what it works on: your USB and your XZ. The list on the left holds the same tools, so you can go straight from one to another. Tools in the top left of each tool goes back to this page. Every tool, in two groups. Repair library Fixes a music USB the XZ cannot read. Game downloads Gets the free games again and copies them to a USB. XZ Screen Shows the XZ screen on this computer, ready for OBS. Updates App updates, XZ Mods version and Network updates have their own section in the top bar. Feedback Reports and ideas have their own section at the right of the top bar.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"repair-library","t":"Repair library","x":"Repair library checks the music library your DJ software exported to a USB the XZ cannot read. It can clear invalid unused pages and reconnect playback history pages that survived. It keeps track records, playlists, music and prepared stems. Step 1, choose the USB. USB Your music USB or a folder holding a copy of it. Choose folder and Find USBs Picks a folder, or looks for USBs again. Connect a USB Appears when no USB is found. Opens a short guide to connect one. Read only Checking only reads the library. Choose the USB. Then choose Check library . Library check. The verdict, what the library holds and what is wrong. Save report keeps the result on this computer. Repair plan. What changes and what stays the same. Back up and repair backs up the library files first. If the DJ software that writes the USB is open on this computer, the check says so and offers Prepare for repair . Close it so both apps do not write at the same time, then check again. After a repair, Undo this repair puts the library files back exactly as they were before it.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"game-downloads","t":"Game downloads","x":"Game downloads gets the free games again and copies them to a USB. Use it to retry a download that failed while the app wrote your USB, or to add the games to a USB that already has XZ Mods. Games already on the USB stay in place. The free games. Choose USB and set up games Downloads and checks every free game, keeps its license notice and copies it to the USB you choose. One game Download keeps the game on this computer. Download and copy to USB also puts it on a USB. Doom shareware , Chex Quest and Freedoom Phase 2 each have their own download. Put your own compatible WADs in a WADS folder on either USB, then choose a base game and an optional add-on in the XZ's USB WAD loader. Downloading games does not change the XZ loader.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"xz-screen","t":"XZ Screen","x":"XZ Screen shows the XDJ-XZ screen on this computer over the network, so you can add it to an OBS scene. It sends the picture only, no audio, and the XZ keeps all its controls. Before the first connection. Set up Live Streamer Opens the three-step connection guide. Stop stream and Fullscreen Work once the XZ is connected. Stream color 8-bit with 256 colors, or 16-bit with the original colors. A change applies when you reconnect. Status What the connection is doing, and the frame rate it measures. Screen The XZ screen at 800 × 480 once it is connected. The connection guide. Look again Searches the network for the XZ again. XZ address Found by itself, or type the address the XZ shows. Network details The ports a firewall must allow, UDP 50006 and TCP 50010. Open USB setup Older USB loaders have no screen service. Update the loader on the USB page. Status Found your XZ, still looking, or what stopped it. Connect and Close The first picture from the XZ confirms the connection. Connect this computer and the XZ to the same network, for example the same router or a network cable between them. Choose Set up Live Streamer . The app looks for the XZ at once. If the guide asks, update the USB loader on the USB page, then switch the XZ off and on with both decks stopped. The guide never restarts the XZ. Choose Connect . To use the picture in OBS, add a Browser source, paste the OBS Browser Source URL , and set its width to 800 and height to 480 . Copy OBS URL copies it. Keep the app running. The URL works on this computer only and changes when you reconnect. Tick Show a logo while browsing USB to cover the stream with the XZ Mods logo while you browse your USB. The play screen comes back on its own. Menus, custom themes and screens the app does not recognise stay covered. With an older USB loader the picture updates about once a second and the status says it is not performance video. Update the USB loader appears beside it.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"manual","t":"Manual","x":"Manual is this manual, inside the app. It comes with the app, so it needs no internet connection. Where the app explains a feature, Read in the manual opens the chapter about it. Four decks open in the Manual, at the video of how the sound of decks 3 and 4 reaches the mixer. Manual Opens the manual. It sits between Tools and About in the top bar. Search Searches every chapter as you type. Press / to get here from anywhere on the page, and Enter to open the first result. Progress How much of the manual you have read. A chapter's circle fills as you read and turns into a tick at its end. Start page What XZ Mods adds, the interface you play on, and every chapter in order. Menu map Every screen of the player as a flow chart. See The menu map . Chapter list Every chapter, on the left beside the page. The one you are reading is outlined and lists its sections. Chapter The chapter you are reading. Previous and Next at its end move through the manual in order. Video An illustration of the XDJ-XZ shows how a feature works. It plays when it comes into view, and Play pauses it. A video in several steps also has arrows and numbered steps, and its caption follows the step. How-to videos. Many sections show how to get there on the player: the player's screen, beside a picture of the key, rotary selector or pad you use, pressed in time with the screen. The steps under the video light up as it reaches them. Click a step to play from there. Where a section shows more than one way, the tabs above the steps switch between them. Numbers on pictures. Point at a number, or tab to it and use the arrow keys, to light up that part of the picture and read what it is. Play steps through every number. The list under the picture says the same. Your interface. Choose MODERN, CLASSIC or Both on the start page or at the foot of the chapter list. The manual then hides what does not apply to you. A MODS page drawn in both interfaces has a MODERN and CLASSIC switch on its picture. Where you stopped. The manual remembers the chapter and section you read last. The start page offers Continue where you left off . Less motion. When your computer is set to reduce motion, nothing in the manual moves by itself. A video shows a still picture of each step and plays only when you press Play.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"the-menu-map","t":"The menu map","x":"Menu map , under the start page in the chapter list, shows every screen on the player and how to get to it, as a flow chart. The play screen is on the left, and what each key opens fans out to its right. Every branch is labelled with the control that opens it: a key such as MENU , the rotary selector, or a tap on a word on the screen. The menu map at BEAT JUMP PADS, opened with MENU, then PLAY, then BEAT JUMP PADS. Interface MODERN or CLASSIC. The map starts on the interface you chose for the manual. Find a screen Type the name of a screen and press Enter to go to it. View Zoom out and in, fit the whole map, open every branch, or close them back to the MODS sections. Show every state lays out every state of every screen. Path How you got here from the play screen, one control at a time. Click a step to go back to it. Jump to The play screen and what each of its keys opens. Screen The screen you picked, outlined in yellow, as are the branches that lead to it. The number on its picture counts its states. Control The control that opens the screen. A keycap is a key on the player; a tap names the words on the screen. The screen The screen at full size. Its states follow below it, then the parts you can pick, how you get here and where it leads. States Each state of the screen as you turn the rotary selector or change a value, and the control between them. Read in the manual Opens the part of this manual that explains the screen. Room to work. The chapter list folds away while the map is open, so the map has the width. The button at the far left of the top bar brings the list back. Move around. Drag the map to move it. The mouse wheel, or the + and − keys on your computer, zoom in and out, and 0 fits the whole map. In a wide window the small map in the corner shows where you are; click it to go there. Branches. The number beside a screen opens the screens after it, and − closes them again. The map opens with the MODS sections closed, so the first view stays readable. Keys. The arrow keys walk the map: right into a branch, left back out, up and down to the screens beside it. Enter opens a screen and Esc closes it. Previous screen and Next screen at the foot of a screen walk the whole map in order. From a chapter. A section of the manual about a screen has On the menu map beside its heading. It opens the map at that screen.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"about","t":"About","x":"About says what XZ Mods is and who makes it, and gathers the links, the disclaimers and the open-source licenses in one place. About. Version The app version on this computer. Maker XZ Mods is made by OpticMystic. App updates and release notes Opens App updates in Updates. The maker OpticMystic's projects: XZ Mods, VJ.Tools and DJ Profile. Make yours opens DJ Profile. Links The source code, issues and releases on GitHub, xzmods.com and vj.tools. Each opens in your browser. Feedback Opens Feedback in the app. Support XZ Mods (optional) Voluntary support on Cash App. Every feature stays available. Disclaimers XZ Mods is independent of the maker of the XDJ-XZ, is experimental and runs from the USB. Open license notices Every open-source project XZ Mods uses and its license.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"feedback","t":"Feedback","x":"Feedback is where you tell the maintainer about a problem, ask for a feature or ask a question, and follow what you sent. It sits at the right of the top bar on every page. The Feedback section. Feedback Opens this section from any page. A count on it shows reports from your XZ that wait for your words. Report a problem Opens the report window at its first question. Request a feature Opens the report window at the kind of idea. Ask a question Goes straight to the box. Answers from this manual appear as you type. My reports What you sent from this computer and where each report is now. Maintainer inbox For the maintainer only. Reports from your XZ that wait for your words appear above My reports, under From your XZ . The sticks that may send them are listed under Your XZ sticks .","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"report-a-problem-or-share-an-idea","t":"Report a problem or share an idea","x":"The report window sends a private report to the maintainer: a problem, something that got worse, an idea or a question. Report a problem in Feedback opens it at the first question. Request a feature and Ask a question answer that question for you. The only thing you have to fill in is one box. Nothing is posted publicly. The first question. Steps Where you are. The box with Send is always the last step. Topic Pick the closest one. The next question depends on it. How do I...? For a question. Answers from this manual appear as you type. Not sure Skips the question. Every question has it. Cancel Closes the window. What you typed comes back when you open it again. Pick what it is about, or Not sure . Answer at most two more short questions, or press Not sure . Write what happened in your own words. One sentence is enough. Press Send privately . You pick It then asks Something got worse When it got worse, then for the USB sticks that were in the XZ Something isn't working What kind of problem: sound, SYNC or tempo, the screen, buttons and pads, loading and USB, four decks, a crash, or something else It should work differently Compared with what: the XZ before XZ Mods, another XZ feature, other DJ gear or software, an earlier XZ Mods version, or just your preference. For gear or another feature, which one I have a new idea What kind of idea How do I...? Nothing more. Go straight to your question The box, with an answer from this manual. Your answers What you picked. Change goes back to the first question. The box The only thing you have to fill in. Up to 4,096 bytes; a counter appears near the limit. Is this it? Up to three answers from this manual that match what you typed. Answer buttons Set up four decks opens that setup. That answers it closes without sending anything. Included details What the app collected to send with your words. Closed until you open it. Send privately Sends your words and the details shown, to the maintainer only. As you type, Is this it? shows answers from this manual. The matching runs on your computer; your words are not sent anywhere for it. If an answer solves it, its button opens the right setup, such as Set up four decks , or That answers it closes the window. Nothing is sent.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"included-details","t":"Included details","x":"While you answer and type, the app reads the details that help the maintainer, for at most 10 seconds: the session log and settings on your XZ Mods USB, the diary on each stick, the app's events and the build. Everything is cleaned first. No track names, file paths, serial numbers or network addresses are kept. Included details, opened, with one source shown and one left out. Included details How many sources are included, their size and the time around the problem they cover. A source What it is and where it comes from. Untick it to leave it out. Show The exact content that would be sent for this source. Left out An unticked source is not sent. Exact content What is sent for this source, after cleaning. Send privately sends exactly your words and the ticked details shown at that moment. If you send before the app has finished reading, it sends what it has read and notes what is missing. Collect again reads everything again. Ideas include no details at all, only your words. Details are deleted after 14 days.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"when-something-got-worse","t":"When something got worse","x":"For something that got worse, the app asks you to plug in every USB stick that was in the XZ when it happened. XZ Mods versions that keep a diary write it to each stick while the XZ plays. The app reads only that diary, never your music. Two sticks plugged in: an XZ Mods USB with a diary and a music stick without one. XZ Mods USB A stick with the XZ Mods loader on it. Diary The time range the diary on this stick covers. Music stick A stick with music only. No diary on this stick This stick has no diary, for example from a version that does not keep one. That's all of them Goes on to the box. Each stick appears by itself as you plug it in. Press That's all of them when every stick is in. A missing stick or a missing diary never stops you sending.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"after-you-send","t":"After you send","x":"The receipt after sending. Your reference The permanent reference for this report, also shown in My reports. Status Where the report is now. Copy Copies the reference so you can quote it to the maintainer. Track my report Opens it in My reports. Every accepted report or idea gets its own reference, such as R-4F7K-2M9Q . Quote it when asking about that report. Copy copies the reference. The reference stays the same if you send again after a connection failure. It does not let anyone read your report or its status. If the app cannot confirm that a report arrived, it says Not confirmed yet . Nothing is lost. Set up reporting connection checks the internet connection and the computer's clock, then Send again sends the same report. If the first attempt did arrive, you get its receipt and nothing arrives twice. Save to a file keeps a copy without sending. The setup after a send that was not confirmed. Connection Whether this computer is online. Clock Secure connections fail when the date is wrong. Send again Sends the same report again.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"my-reports","t":"My reports","x":"My reports lists every report and idea sent from this computer, with its kind and where it is now, in plain words. It is the list under the buttons in Feedback. Four reports, one with news. Kind Such as Problem, Got worse, Works differently, Idea or Question. Your words The start of what you wrote. It stays on this computer. Status Where the report is now. New marks a change you have not opened yet. Reference and date Your report reference and the day you sent it. Part of XZ-1042 appears when the maintainer assigns an item. Check now Checks every report at once, and asks for new reports from your XZ. When a report's status changes, a notice appears at the top of whichever page is open. A status change, shown while App updates is open. Notice Appears when the status of one of your reports changes. View Opens that report. The app checks for news when it starts, after it checks for app updates, and when you open My reports, at most every 15 minutes for each report. Check now checks at once. If you are offline, the last known status stays. Open a report to see where it is. The view is read-only. Once the maintainer assigns it, Part of XZ-1042 names the bug, feature or question it belongs to. Reports about the same item share that item number. If the maintainer moves your report to another item, this number changes; your R reference stays the same. Item numbers remain after the report's details are deleted. A problem the maintainer confirmed, with a fix in progress. Progress Received, Confirmed, Fix in progress, Ready to test, In an update. Ideas and questions show Received, Looked at, Decided. Reference This report's permanent reference and kind. Your words The start of what you wrote. Status Where it is now, in plain words. Dates When you sent it, the last change, when its details are deleted and how long tracking lasts. Status link and forgetting The status link, and Forget this report. Check now Checks this report at once. Part of The item this report belongs to, such as XZ-1042. If the maintainer needs one more detail, the question appears in the report. Answer in a new report starts a report that names this one. Open status page and Copy status link give a read-only web page with the same status, report reference and item number. It shows none of your words or details. Anyone with the link can read the status. Turn off status links stops every link for this report; the app still checks it. Forget this report removes its receipt from this computer. The maintainer keeps the report. A report saved, but not sent, by an older version of the app appears under Saved, not sent . Use this text starts a new report with its words. Details are deleted 14 days after you send them. Tracking lasts while a report is open, up to one year without news, then 180 days after it closes. A fix in a local test build is not a published update.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"from-your-xz","t":"From your XZ","x":"A report sent from the XZ waits in Feedback for your words. From your XZ appears above My reports while one waits. The XZ notes the screen you were on as names only. It keeps no picture and no text from the screen. A report from the XZ, waiting for your words. From your XZ Reports from your XZ that wait for your words. Reference and time The report's reference and when the XZ sent it. It stays the same when you add your words. Screen The screen the XZ showed just before you reported, with any error code on it. Stick The stick the report came from, and when XZ Mods wrote it. Typed on the XZ What you typed on the XZ, if anything. What happened? Starts with what you typed on the XZ. Change it or add to it. Collected details What the XZ collected and sent with the report. Show displays each part exactly. Stop reminding Ends the reminders for this report. It stays in the list. Send without comments Finishes the report without words from you. Send Adds your words to the same report. Send adds your words to the same report, under the same reference. The report then moves to your sent reports, where you follow it like any other. Send without comments finishes the report as it is. If the app can't reach the report service, it keeps your words and sends them by itself later. You can close the app. The XZ already sent the collected details. They are deleted 14 days after it sent them. After that the report says so, and your words still reach the maintainer. The maintainer sees the report as soon as the XZ sends it, marked as waiting for your comments, and can start from the logs. The app tells you when a report from the XZ waits: While the app is open, a new report brings a Windows notification, such as \"Your XZ sent a report, R-4F7K-2M9Q. Add what happened?\" Click it to open that report. Feedback in the top bar shows how many reports wait. When the app starts with reports waiting, a callout under the page title names them. The callout when the app starts with a report waiting. Callout Names the report your XZ sent. It never covers the window or takes the keyboard. Add what happened Opens the report in Feedback with its box ready. Remind me later Hides the callout until the app starts again. Stop reminding Ends the reminders for these reports. They stay in Feedback. Badge How many reports from your XZ wait for your words. Reminders end when you choose Stop reminding , or 7 days after a report arrives. Each report brings one notification at most. If Windows notifications are off for XZ Mods, or your copy of the app is not installed, the badge and the callout tell you instead.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"your-xz-sticks","t":"Your XZ sticks","x":"Every stick XZ Mods writes gets a loader ID, such as L-7K2M-9Q4F . It lets the XZ send reports from that stick to this computer, and to nothing else. Your XZ sticks , near the bottom of Feedback, lists them. Three sticks: one waiting to register, one ready and one revoked. Your XZ sticks The sticks XZ Mods wrote on this computer. Loader ID Reports from this stick carry it. Written When XZ Mods last wrote the stick. State Can send reports, Registers when online, Plug it in to finish, Revokes when online or Revoked. Revoke Stops this stick sending reports. The app asks first. Revoke a stick you lost or gave away. The XZ can no longer send reports from it. If you are offline, the stick is revoked on this computer at once and the report service hears of it later. Writing XZ Mods to that stick again gives it a new key, and it can send reports again. Plug it in to finish means a write to that stick was not confirmed. Plug the stick in with the app open. If the state stays, write XZ Mods to the stick again. With no sticks yet, Set up a USB opens the USB setup.","i":""},{"c":"desktop-app","a":"maintainer-inbox","t":"Maintainer inbox","x":"Maintainer inbox , at the bottom of Feedback, is for the maintainer. Connect it with the report-only owner key. The short setup checks that key by reading the inbox. Enter a report reference or item number in the search box and choose Find . You can type either case, with or without spaces and dashes. For a report reference, I or L also means 1, and O means 0. A report reference finds one report; an item number finds the reports assigned to that item. Clear returns to the inbox. The inbox, scrolled right to show Reference and Item. Find Searches the whole inbox by report reference or item number. Reference The permanent reference for each report. Item The bug, feature or question the report belongs to. A dash means it has not been assigned yet. Scroll Scroll right or left to see every column. The reference and item number identify a report; the owner key is still required to read the inbox.","i":""},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"","t":"Messages and troubleshooting","x":"This chapter lists every message XZ Mods can show you, what it means and the one thing to do about it. Find the words you see on the screen in the tables below. Messages in capitals come from the player. Messages in normal case come from the XZ Mods app on your computer.","i":""},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"if-the-player-will-not-start-with-the-usb","t":"If the player will not start with the USB","x":"XZ Mods runs from the USB. Without the USB the player starts as it was. Press MENU Tap CONNECT Tap UPDATES Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 2 clicks clockwise Switch the player off. Remove the XZ Mods USB and switch the player on. It starts without XZ Mods. Play from a stick without XZ Mods if you are in a set. On your computer, open the USB in the XZ Mods app. If it says Update available , choose Update USB . If it says Up to date , open Updates › XZ Mods version › Restore or update a loader by hand and update the loader again. The app keeps a backup of the old loader each time. Try the USB again. If it still does not start, report the problem . Check these first: Check Why The player runs firmware 1.26 XZ Mods supports no other firmware version autoexec.bin is at the top of the USB A loader prepared into a folder has to be copied to the USB yourself You updated the USB after updating the app An app update does not change the USB If XZ Mods started after a network update and stopped working, open CONNECT › UPDATES and push PREVIOUS VERSION , then switch the player off and on. See Updates over the network . If the sound goes wrong while you test, stop playback and switch the player off and on. Load the same track again and check the original mix before you go on. Tip MODS is always reachable with the hardware alone. In CLASSIC, the button above LINK switches to MODERN, where MENU opens MODS. Turn the encoder to move, push it to choose and press BACK to go back.","i":""},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"stems-on-the-usb","t":"Stems on the USB","x":"When a deck cannot play stems, its stem row says why and its last button offers the next step. In CLASSIC the row sits under the deck's waveform. Open the button to see the deck's setup page in MODS. Press MENU Tap STEMS Tap SET UP USB STEMS Tap CHECK STEM ENGINE Tap CHECK THIS DECK AGAIN Tap CHECK THIS DECK AGAIN Tap STEMS READY / BACK TO PLAY Press MENU Deck 1 has a track loaded that has no stems yet. STANDALONE STEMS SETUP The three things stems need, in order. Steps 1 CHECK ENGINE, 2 TURN ON (ALL DECKS), 3 LOAD A PREPARED TRACK. Deck state The deck and why it has no stems. Next step The one thing to do. Deck Choose DECK 1 or DECK 2 to check the other deck. CHECK THIS DECK AGAIN Reads the deck again after you fixed it. State The deck's stem state in a word or two. Stem row says What it means What to do STEMS READY Stems are ready on this deck Nothing NO STEM ENGINE, with SET UP The loader on the USB has no stem engine Update the USB loader with the XZ Mods app, then restart the player STEMS OFF, with TURN ON USB stems are switched off Push TURN ON . It turns USB stems on for decks 1 and 2 NO TRACK LOADED The deck has no track Load a track from the USB NOT PREPARED, with HOW TO FIX The track has no stems on this USB Prepare it in the XZ Mods app, then load it again LOADING STEMS Stems are loading from the USB Wait a moment PLAY TO ALIGN Stems are loaded but not locked to the track yet Press play. Stems lock to the track a few seconds in STEM SET ERROR, with HOW TO FIX The stems on the USB are incomplete or damaged. The page names the problem Verify the track in the XZ Mods app and prepare it again Every state on both interfaces, with pictures, is in Stems .","i":""},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"notices-on-the-play-screen","t":"Notices on the play screen","x":"A notice is a short message in the middle of the lanes. It clears on its own after a few seconds, and the deck keeps playing. Press BROWSE Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise Press LOAD 1 Press BACK A notice over the lanes. Notice What happened. Nothing else on the screen changes. A long notice wraps onto two lines Notice What to do DECK 1 DID NOT LOAD THE TRACK Load the track again. If it fails again, check the file in your DJ software THE TRACK ON USB 2 COULD NOT BE READ BECAUSE THE DEVICE WAS REMOVED WHILE IT WAS LOADING Plug the USB back in and load the track again USB1 IS NOT CONNECTED, USB2 IS NOT CONNECTED Plug in the USB, or choose the other source USB SOURCE CHANGED: SELECT TRACK AGAIN The USB changed under the list. Choose the track again SELECT A TRACK, THEN PRESS LOAD Highlight a track first OPEN A TRACK LIST TO LOAD, NO USB TRACK LIST TO LOAD FROM Open a track list on a USB, then load LOAD FROM THIS LIST IS OFF Loading from this list is switched off. See Browsing and loading THIS ROW CANNOT BE LOADED, THAT DECK CANNOT LOAD THIS TRACK Choose another track or another deck TAG LIST IS FULL: 100 TRACKS Remove a track from the tag list first MATCHING NEEDS A MASTER DECK Set a master deck, then use MATCHING NO MASTER DECK: BPM FILTER OFF, NO MASTER KEY: KEY FILTER OFF The filter has nothing to compare with. Set a master deck COMPUTER BROWSING IS NOT AVAILABLE YET, LINK BROWSING IS NOT AVAILABLE YET Browse a USB instead. These sources come in a later version LINK DID NOT OPEN, EXPORT MODE DID NOT OPEN Try again. The player's own screen did not open MODS DID NOT OPEN: PUSH AGAIN Push again TOUCH CANNOT OPEN THIS YET: PUSH THE ENCODER Use the encoder for this item THAT SETTING CANNOT CHANGE HERE Change it in the player's own UTILITY. Hold MENU DECK 3 AND 4 ARE NOT RUNNING Set up four decks first. See Four decks KEY SHIFT REFUSED: AUDIO LOAD TOO HIGH The measured audio workload leaves too little headroom for a new shift. Current shifts keep running. Check SYSTEM READOUT and retry when the load falls. See Keys and KEY SYNC THIS DECK IS MASTER KEY SYNC matches a deck to the master. Make another deck the master first A player warning such as E-8307: USB ACCESS ERROR The player raised its own warning window. MODERN says it once in the player's words and keeps working. See The player's own warnings THIS DJ PROFILE CANNOT BE READ Make the profile again in the XZ Mods app. See Connect and DJ profiles","i":"modern"},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"errors-on-a-deck","t":"Errors on a deck","x":"When the player cannot play a track, XZ Mods shows the player's own error code and text on that deck. XZ Mods never hides these errors. Tap CHOOSE TRACK Turn ROTARY SELECTOR 1 click clockwise Press LOAD 1 Press BACK A read error on deck 2. Error The player's own code and text. CHOOSE TRACK Opens browse so you can load another track. EMERGENCY LOOP. The deck loops until you load a track The same error on deck 3, with four decks MODERN. The error covers the deck's lane, with CHOOSE TRACK . While MODS is open, the strip at the top of the dock turns red with each deck's badge, the code, the player's text and SHOW DECK . Tap the strip to close MODS and see the deck. CLASSIC. The player's own error stays visible in the deck's lower area, also while MODS is open. Touches there go to the player. Code Player's text What to do E-8302 CANNOT PLAY TRACK Load another track. Check the USB and the file on a computer E-8304, E-8305 UNSUPPORTED The player cannot play this file. Export it in another format E-8306 NO FILE The file is missing from the USB. Export the track to the USB again from your DJ software E-7206 AUTH CHIP ERROR Switch the player off and on. If it also happens without the XZ Mods USB, the player needs service","i":""},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"the-player-s-own-warnings","t":"The player's own warnings","x":"The player sometimes raises its own warning window, for example about a USB or a device. XZ Mods shows it and keeps working. MODERN. The play screen says the warning once, in the player's own words, for example E-8307: USB ACCESS ERROR . Browse, the decks and every control keep working. MODS, in either interface. MODS stays open on the same page. The strip at the top of the dock turns red with the warning's code and text, and REPORT THIS . The strip goes when the warning does. CLASSIC with MODS closed. CLASSIC shows the player's window. Touches, keys and the encoder go to the player until it closes the window. A player warning in the dock while MODS is open. Warning The player's code and text.","i":""},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"loopback-cable-connected","t":"LOOPBACK CABLE CONNECTED","x":"With the loopback cable in, CLASSIC shows a LOOPBACK CABLE CONNECTED card, and decks 3 and 4 work as described in Four decks .","i":""},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"when-settings-cannot-be-saved","t":"When settings cannot be saved","x":"Every change in MODS saves on its own to the USB. The save state at the right of the MODS dock says what happened. Lines that say NOT SAVED or NO SETTINGS USB show in amber. The full list is in Saving to the USB . Press MENU Tap SCREEN Tap CLASSIC Tap MODERN Press MENU Message What it means What to do NO SETTINGS USB: CHANGES LAST UNTIL POWER OFF. No USB to save on Insert the XZ Mods USB, or your settings USB NOT SAVED TO USB 1: CHECK USB Writing failed Check the stick is in and not write-protected, then change the setting again USB 1 IS LOCKED: NOT SAVED The stick is write-protected Unlock it, or check it on a computer THE STICK IS FULL: NOT SAVED No space left on the stick Free some space on a computer THIS STICK IS READ-ONLY: NOTHING CHANGES The player opened the stick read-only Check the stick on a computer INVALID USB SETTINGS: KEPT CURRENT, USB 1 SETTINGS INVALID: KEPT CURRENT The settings file on the stick is damaged. The player keeps the settings it has Change any setting to write a new file, or update the USB in the app USB 1 HAS NO SETTINGS: KEPT CURRENT The stick has no settings yet Nothing. Your next change creates them PROFILE APPLIED / NOT SAVED A DJ profile was applied but could not be saved Check the stick is in and not locked SETTINGS SAVE UNAVAILABLE Saving stopped in this session Switch the player off and on NOT SAVED: CHANGES LAST UNTIL POWER OFF., TRIAL RUN: NOTHING SAVED This build runs as a trial that saves nothing Start from a USB prepared in the XZ Mods app to save TRIAL RUN: SETTINGS NOT LOADED A trial build ignores the settings on the stick Start from a prepared USB A padlock beside a setting means XZ Mods shows it but cannot change it there. The help under it says why. See UTILITY, the player's own settings .","i":""},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"messages-in-the-xz-mods-app","t":"Messages in the XZ Mods app","x":"Every \"needs setup\" state in the app comes with one button that starts a short guide. Press it. Message Button What it does No XZ Mods build is on this computer yet, so there is nothing to write Set up mod versions Finds or imports a build Choose which XZ Mods build goes on this USB Use the newest build Picks the build that came with the app Stem engine not set up yet Set up stem engine Checks the computer, downloads the engine and tests it Connect your music USB Connect a USB Finds a USB or a folder and checks its library Set up Live Streamer to connect to your XZ Set up Live Streamer Finds the XZ on the network and connects Older USB loaders have no screen service Update the USB loader Opens the USB page to update the loader The DJ software that writes this USB is open on this computer Prepare for repair Waits for you to close it, then checks again Not confirmed yet, after sending a report Set up reporting connection Checks the internet connection and the clock, then sends the same report again. It never arrives twice Maintainer inbox, not connected (maintainer only) Connect and check Keeps the owner key under Windows protection and reads the inbox to check it Message What to do USB drives could not be listed Choose Choose a folder instead , or plug the USB in again and choose Look again The USB could not be read Reconnect it and choose it again This is a folder, not a USB Copy the finished autoexec.bin to the top of the USB afterward Nothing to write yet Add a game or a DJ profile, or cancel XZ Mods is updating itself Write to the USB once the app update has finished Finished, with something to check Read the lines under it. Retry the failed games tries only the games that failed Settings were not written Open the USB again and write again Your DJ profile was not saved Read the reason under it, fix it and save the profile again The USB was not ejected Choose Try ejecting again , or eject it from your computer Making stems needs a Windows computer or an Apple silicon Mac Import stems made elsewhere, or make them on another computer The graphics engine needs a newer NVIDIA driver Choose Use the processor , or update the driver and check again The USB is full Choose Choose fewer tracks The USB was disconnected Plug it back in and choose Continue . Nothing was left half-written Every page of the app is in The XZ Mods app .","i":""},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"the-diary-on-your-usb-sticks","t":"The diary on your USB sticks","x":"XZ Mods keeps a short diagnostic diary in VJ.Tools/XZ-Mods-diary/ on each mounted USB stick, including music sticks. If a problem happens during a set, keep those sticks so you can include their diaries in a later report. The diary records the XZ Mods version, settings fingerprint, USB slots, interface, deck view, state changes and fixed notice codes. It also records available CPU, memory, audio, SYNC, key-processing and USB-read measurements. It never records track titles, music paths, serial numbers or network identities. A missing measurement stays unknown. Each stick holds at most 4 MiB of diary files. Older segments are replaced first, and the previous session's latest segment is kept when a new session starts. Writing pauses during track loads, RAM copies and heavy USB reads. No diary is created on a read-only stick or when less than 64 MiB of free space plus a small write reserve remains. Read-only test sessions save nothing. Normal USB-loader sessions write diary entries when these conditions allow it. Long busy periods and removal can leave gaps. The diary stays on the sticks. Nothing is sent until you choose to include it in a report.","i":""},{"c":"troubleshooting","a":"report-a-problem","t":"Report a problem","x":"When something goes wrong, send a report. It helps fix the problem for everyone. Press MENU Tap REPORT THIS Tap SKIP, I'LL ADD IT ON MY COMPUTER Tap SEND REPORT On the player. Open MODS › EXTRAS › REPORT AN ISSUE , or push REPORT THIS beside an error in the dock. Choose a topic, add words if you like, and send. Offline, the report waits on the stick for your computer. See Report an issue . On your computer. In the XZ Mods app, open Feedback at the top right and choose Report a problem . Only one box is required, and My reports in Feedback shows where your report is afterwards. See Report a problem or share an idea . On GitHub. Open an issue at https://github.com/OpticMystic/XZ-Mods/issues. Say what you did, what you expected and what happened. The app adds the cleaned-up details itself, and you can see and untick each one. Nothing is sent until you press Send privately , and the app posts nothing publicly. From the player, the public GitHub issue is a separate step you submit yourself.","i":""},{"c":"settings","a":"","t":"Settings reference","x":"XZ Mods keeps its settings on your USB, so they travel with you from player to player. This page explains where they are kept and what happens when the USB changes, then lists every setting with its values, its default and the chapter that explains it.","i":""},{"c":"settings","a":"where-settings-are-kept","t":"Where settings are kept","x":"Your settings live in one file on the USB: VJ.Tools/XZ-Mods.cfg . You change them in MODS, or on your computer with the XZ Mods app . There is no save button. Every change saves on its own to the USB you are browsing, and the bottom of the MODS page says what happened for a few seconds. Message Meaning SAVED TO USB 1 (or USB 2) The change is on that USB. NOT SAVED TO USB 1: CHECK USB The USB could not be written. Check that it is not full or locked, then change the setting again. SAVED ON THIS XZ / NO USB No USB is in. The change is kept on this player only. USB REMOVED: SETTINGS KEPT You pulled the USB. The player keeps your settings for the rest of the set. USB 1 HAS NO SETTINGS: KEPT CURRENT The USB you browsed has no settings file. The player keeps the settings it has. USB 1 SETTINGS INVALID: KEPT CURRENT The settings file on that USB could not be read. The player keeps the settings it has. NOT SAVED: CHANGES LAST UNTIL POWER OFF. This start of XZ Mods cannot save. Your changes work until you switch the player off.","i":""},{"c":"settings","a":"when-the-usb-changes","t":"When the USB changes","x":"The player follows the same rules as its own MY SETTINGS: Browsing a USB in USB 1 or USB 2 loads that USB's settings. Browsing a computer or a LINK source never changes them. A USB without settings, or with settings the player cannot read, leaves your current settings as they are. Nothing resets to defaults in the middle of a set. The player remembers the last settings it used. Started without a USB, it uses those. A USB with its own settings takes over again once you browse it. The player's own MY SETTINGS, which your DJ software writes to the USB, are a separate set. XZ Mods settings never change them, and loading MY SETTINGS does not change XZ Mods settings. MODERN's own display choices are settings too: its waveform colour, waveform position and zoom, how it writes keys, the TRACK COLOURS choice, the LAMPS AND TITLES and BYPASS BUTTON switches, and the columns of its track list. So are the 3-band colours. They are saved to the USB with everything else and come back after the player restarts. Things you do during a set, such as muting a stem, BYPASS, a key shift, KEY SYNC or a RAM copy, are not settings. They start fresh every time the player starts.","i":""},{"c":"settings","a":"going-back-to-the-defaults","t":"Going back to the defaults","x":"There is no single button that resets every setting. Set each one back in MODS, using the Default column below. Some pages have their own way back: PAGE 1: STOCK for beat jump page 1, RESET STEM COLORS for the stem colours, and RESET 3-BAND COLOURS for the 3-band colours. Note Deleting the settings file from the USB does not reset anything. The player keeps the settings it has, and saves them to the USB again with your next change.","i":""},{"c":"settings","a":"every-setting","t":"Every setting","x":"Each row names the chapter that explains the setting. Setting Values Default Explained in Stem audio Off / On On Stems Gate cue Off / On Off Beat jump and performance features Smart cue Off / On Off Beat jump and performance features Interface 0 to 1 1 Getting started Classic theme 0 to 23 0 Screen, interfaces and themes Modern theme 0 to 0 0 Screen, interfaces and themes Deck view 0 to 2 0 Four decks Preview waveform in MODERN browse 0 to 1 0 Browsing and loading Stem shortcut pad mode 0 to 3 0 Controls on the player Stem pad lights Off / On On Controls on the player VJ.Tools screen view Off / On Off Connect and DJ profiles Screen switch button 0 to 2 0 Controls on the player Stem shortcut bank 0 to 1 0 Controls on the player Page 1 custom Beat Jump Off / On On Beat jump and performance features Page 1: A/B 0 to 9 0 Beat jump and performance features Page 1: C/D 0 to 9 1 Beat jump and performance features Page 1: E/F 0 to 9 2 Beat jump and performance features Page 1: G/H 0 to 9 3 Beat jump and performance features Page 2: A/B 0 to 9 4 Beat jump and performance features Page 2: C/D 0 to 9 5 Beat jump and performance features Page 2: E/F 0 to 9 6 Beat jump and performance features Page 2: G/H 0 to 9 8 Beat jump and performance features Stem row layout 0 to 4 1 Stems Stem buttons (modern interface) 0 to 5 5 Stems Scrolling waveform 0 to 2 1 The play screen Browse column 1 0 to 3 0 Browsing and loading Browse column 2 0 to 3 2 Browsing and loading Browse column 3 0 to 3 3 Browsing and loading Show key before track title Off / On On Browsing and loading Color compatible keys Off / On On Browsing and loading Key notation 0 to 2 0 Screen, interfaces and themes Drums color 0 to 8 0 Stems Harmonics color 0 to 8 0 Stems Vocals color 0 to 8 0 Stems Effective key and Key Sync display Off / On On Beat jump and performance features Button above LINK 0 to 6 2 Controls on the player SHIFT + button above LINK 0 to 6 1 Controls on the player Stem order 0 to 5 0 Stems 3-BAND LOW COLOUR 0 to 8 0 Screen, interfaces and themes 3-BAND MID COLOUR 0 to 8 0 Screen, interfaces and themes 3-BAND HIGH COLOUR 0 to 8 0 Screen, interfaces and themes MODERN WAVEFORM COLOUR 0 to 3 2 Screen, interfaces and themes WAVEFORM POSITION 0 to 1 0 The play screen KEY DISPLAY 0 to 2 0 Screen, interfaces and themes WAVEFORM ZOOM 0 to 6 3 The play screen USB COLOURS 0 to 2 0 Screen, interfaces and themes Hidden MODERN parts (bitmask) 0 to 31 0 Screen, interfaces and themes MODERN browse columns (bitmask, 0 automatic) 0 to 2047 0 Browsing and loading","i":""}];
